[84162]="Hail, $c! I can tell by your demeanor that you've seen and done much in this world. Yet I'm willing to wager you haven't seen a piece of armor like this.$B$BPerform a small favor for me and I'll be willing to trade it to you for an ordinary set of bracers.$B$BI'm in need of a sizeable sample of venom drawn from the spiders and scorpions that inhabit Silithus. Bring this to me along with a few gold coins and I'll perform the exchange.",
[84163]="You kept your word and brought the device built by Mux. I believe a reward is in order if I'm to keep you interested in saving my skin. Bring me the belt and set of gloves that you wish to upgrade. I promise the ones I give you in return will be far superior.",
[84164]="You kept your word and brought the device built by Mux. I believe a reward is in order if I'm to keep you interested in saving my skin. Bring me an ordinary belt and a set of gloves that you wish to upgrade.",
[84165]="You kept your word and brought the device built by Mux. I believe a reward is in order if I'm to keep you interested in saving my skin. Bring me an ordinary belt and a set of gloves that you wish to upgrade.",
[84166]="You kept your word and brought the device built by Mux. I believe a reward is in order if I'm to keep you interested in saving my skin. Bring me the belt and set of gauntlets that you wish to upgrade. I promise the ones I give you in return will be far superior.",
[84168]="You kept your word and brought the device built by Mux. I believe a reward is in order if I'm to keep you interested in saving my skin. Bring me the belt and set of gloves that you wish to upgrade. I promise the ones I give you in return will be far superior.",
[84170]="You kept your word and brought the device built by Mux. I believe a reward is in order if I'm to keep you interested in saving my skin. Bring me the belt and set of gauntlets that you wish to upgrade. I promise the ones I give you in return will be far superior.",
[84171]="You've proven to be a very reliable individual, $n. As much as I trust that you'll help me through this predicament, it would be wise of me to reward you according to your performance.$B$BFor now I will exchange your belt and gloves. If we both see this through I shall make the rest of the pieces available to you.",
[84172]="You've proven to be a very reliable individual, $n. As much as I trust that you'll help me through this predicament, it would be wise of me to reward you according to your performance.$B$BFor now I will exchange your belt and gloves. If we both see this through I shall make the rest of the pieces available to you.",
[84173]="You've proven to be a very reliable individual, $n. As much as I trust that you'll help me through this predicament, it would be wise of me to reward you according to your performance.$B$BFor now I will exchange your belt and gloves. If we both see this through I shall make the rest of the pieces available to you.",
[84174]="You've proven to be a very reliable individual, $n. As much as I trust that you'll help me through this predicament, it would be wise of me to reward you according to your performance.$B$BFor now I will exchange your belt and gloves. If we both see this through I shall make the rest of the pieces available to you.",
[84176]="You've proven to be a very reliable individual, $n. As much as I trust that you'll help me through this predicament, it would be wise of me to reward you according to your performance.$B$BFor now I will exchange your belt and gauntlets. If we both see this through I shall make the rest of the pieces available to you.",
[84177]="You've proven to be a very reliable individual, $n. As much as I trust that you'll help me through this predicament, it would be wise of me to reward you according to your performance.$B$BFor now I will exchange your belt and gloves. If we both see this through I shall make the rest of the pieces available to you.",
[84178]="You've proven to be a very reliable individual, $n. As much as I trust that you'll help me through this predicament, it would be wise of me to reward you according to your performance.$B$BFor now I will exchange your belt and gauntlets. If we both see this through I shall make the rest of the pieces available to you.",
[84179]="Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet. In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.$B$BThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the medallion back together. Return to Deliana and tell her that Bodley is her only hope for finding the remaining pieces. Speak to her about any rewards you've arranged for.$B$BI, for once, shall rest in peace. I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!",
[84194]="Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet. In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.$B$BThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together. Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces. Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.$B$BI, for once, shall rest in peace. I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!",
[84211]="Picking up the bag, you immediately notice it's nearly empty. Somehow you get the impression Nami wont trade the book for the bag by itself. But what's not empty, is the camp. You'd better defend yourself and keep your eyes peeled for more of this stuff.",
[84212]="Nami hands over Jurgens' book. With it safely stowed, you begin the long journey back to the other side of the world.",
[84213]="Join me in this historic experiment and witness the wonders of my invention! I've calculated two locations with suitable geothermic bioflux energy. With manual-auto-locking phasers, I'm ready to send us to the coordinates within compatible regions.$B$BOnce you're at compatible coordinates, use this remote transponder to send the signal to me. I'll configure the warp transmitter to fold the space between here, and there.$B$BWhat I'm saying is, I'll meet you there when you say you're ready!",
[84318]="Oi! $c! Yes, ye! Ye did me a solid by smashing up that depressin' mess of a meatsuit I've been riding in all these years, but I dinnae feel much of a pull to move on. I'm expectin' it's because I got some \"Unfinished Business\" to get up to 'afore I can be on me way. Well dull-wit, ye just been conscripted to help!$B$BI need ye to fetch me hammer. Should be somewhere in Corrin's Crossing and it'll be hard to miss.$B$BOi, take this too. It's me favorite gold tooth. Give it a rub when you've found me weapon.",
[84319]="Great job with the hammer, $c. Next up is me armor. Definitely need that back to move on to the great beyond.$B$BOnly problem is it's in the eh... innards o' one of them abominations. I know, I know, it's askin' a lot, but ye gotta understand I was once a mighty thane under the mountain! I simply can't move on knowin' that the ancestral armor of me clan is dissolving in the gutjuice of a giant rotting mountain o' meat!",
[84330]="So ye see, we need to find a suitable Dwarf corpse and do a bit o' ritual to em' to get my spirit grounded so I can be sent on me way! All perfectly normal stuff, o' course! We'll also need a bit o' Necrotic Runestone from a necromancer type, of course. There's one in Stratholme that goes by Maleki the Pallid. Can't expect he'll be too willin' to part with it willingly but there's a solve for that!$B$BGet me that stone and then head to the undercroft. There's a corpse there that'll do!",
[84332]="<You hear a disembodied voice in your head as you touch the small chest>$B$BCan't be thankin' ye enough, $n. Not how ye'd be expecting it to turn out, no doubt! Just so you aren't too sour about it, I've got something for ye that I've no more use for that I think ye might find useful.$B$BGood luck to ye, $n. Ah, one last thing... if ye happen to see a giant floating necropolis in the distance someday soon, I'd be turnin' tail and runnin' if I were ye. Hah!",
[84377]="The deed is done. Dal'rend Blackhand, Warchief of the Dark Horde, lies dead at your feet.$B$BTake his head and present it to Master Shaw.",
[84414]="<You hear the disembodied voice of Orthas in your mind>$B$B'Ere we are then. Let's get on with it, shall we?",
[84555]="You have uncovered something of great importance. This book is unlike any that you have seen.$B$BIt would appear as if someone or something has managed to shatter the seal of Athenaeum. The text within is garbled and barely legible.",
[86574]="<The unfortunate body here bears the marks of many strikes from the Pridewing wyverns. The pack nearby is rumpled and discarded, with its contents missing, and only a small note clutched in the courier's hand to indicate what was lost: a shipment meant for Innkeeper Faralia at Stonetalon Peak.>$B$B<The wyverns have probably carried off the supply bundles to line their nests.>",
[86576]="In addition to spreading their filth across the Charred Vale, the Bloodfury harpies gather anything shiny that they can find. I'm told that they collect a variety of golden-yellow sunstones for decoration. I have no use for such trinkets, but Mor'rogal has mentioned using them before.$B$BWhile you're fighting the harpies of the Vale, keep your eye out for Glittering Sunstones. Bring any that you find to Mor'rogal, up on the hills above us.",
[86577]="The corruption that rains down from Hyjal flows through the mountain's waters and seeps into everything here in the wood. The creatures that drink the water take the corruption into themselves. It makes them ferocious, diseased, and fearless.$B$BTo counter these effects, I must understand them, and to do that I need samples from the afflicted.$B$BA few samples of putrescent organs from the wolves and bears should do. Take your time; the creatures are common here in Felwood.",
[86585]="The fallen mountaineer bears a standard of Ironforge. Perhaps she was scouting, or making a doomed charge. Either way, the standard has been cast down and trampled. The mountaineer was hit on the head so hard that her helm was knocked off and she was killed outright by a trogg, likely with a spiked club.$B$BThe trogg that killed her is probably still nearby, and likely remembers the banner. Raising the banner of Ironforge once more may call it out.",
[86611]="<The pool of fetid slime has eroded the statue of the stag. It is unclear how it arrived here at the bottom of the lake.$B$BA single crystal stone set in a medallion around its neck bears an unwholesome green gleam. It is worth taking to someone who might know the history of this monument.>",
[86612]="<The pool of fetid slime has eroded the statue of the stag. It is unclear how it arrived here at the bottom of the lake.$B$BA single crystal stone set in a medallion around its neck bears an unwholesome green gleam. It is worth taking to someone who might know the history of this monument.>",
[86613]="The excavation's tools, left behind when the dwarves fled from the troggs, seem mostly untouched. Returning them to the excavators will surely aid their work.",
[86614]="<Among the fishing knickknacks in the debris are some rusty hooks, broken spools of wire, and a slightly corroded but ornate silver hair clip with the monogram \"K.D.\">",
[86615]="Ach! Here I am serving as ambassador to the Wildhammers, and I left me satchel of the latest diplomatic missives somewhere in Wildhammer Keep. I must've left it in the tavern... or maybe I misplaced it by the steam tanks... or was it upstairs? I can never keep track!$B$BI need those papers! If you have a better eye for the keep than I do, see if you can spot my missing diplomatic satchel!",
[86616]="As a shaman, one of the challenges of communing with the elements is that there are other shaman with opposing agendas. The elements do not care why we do what we do, they just do as we ask!$B$BThe trolls at Jintha'alor also practice the shamanic arts, and their interruptions and attacks are a constant thorn to us here.$B$BFind their Vilebranch totems and bring them back to me so that I can nullify their powers. Some they carry, some they place as wards around their altar.",
[86620]="Though we have a good line of gryphons here, there are always a few egg clutches in the wild that are in danger of not making it. A gryphon parent can lose a fight against a wolf, or fall sick. Without help, the fledglings will never survive.$B$BFortunately, we have the means to raise and protect lost young ones like this. If you find lost eggs in the wild, bring them to me.",
[86667]="My old mentor, Norric, sent a minor elemental with an odd request. He needs a jar of snow for some of his shamanic workings! I don't know what he's going to do with that, but I learned a long time ago not to question his ways with respect to magic.$B$BI'm busy learning about the local elementals, so I can't leave to help him. Go to the tunnel entrance at South Gate Pass where there's snow year-round. Scoop some up in this ceramic jar and bring it to him before it melts. The jar should keep it cold.",
[86746]="My people are struggling, $n.$B$BThe Legashi satyr have invaded our den, corrupting many of the Blackmaw and separating us from our Timbermaw allies. Those of us who survive their attacks are huddled in makeshift camps. Worse still, the satyr's corruption is spreading across the land, and poses a threat to my already vulnerable tribe.$B$BThe Legashi lurk among the ruins northeast of here. I must ask you for help in defeating them.",
[86752]="There is much more to be done in our fight against the satyr, $n.$B$BIf you wish be of further help, speak with Gatekeeper Rageroar at the camps of Ursolan to the north. He will know where to use your abilities best. You should find Ursolan to the north of here.",
[86757]="Orcs have taken over the eastern forest, and their scouts and grunts now lurk throughout the woods! It's not safe for our kind to move about Ashenvale any more.$B$BWe need to push back the orcs and secure the forest. We've been able to pick off some of the grunts and scouts by carefully sneaking around the edges of their camp.$B$BFight the orcs and bring me the jagged swords and curved knives that they use. I'll make sure their weapons are salvaged and repurposed, so nothing goes to waste.",
[86758]="Did I ever tell you how I almost lost me hand to a crocolisk? Managed to jam me knife into its jaw, and scrambled out real quick. I thought I had the knife around here somewhere, but I can't seem to find it.$B$BAnyway, that croc is probably still out there hunting along the edge of the lake. That nasty brute probably needs to go, for the safety of the other hunters, if nothing else.$B$BI've taken to calling it Daggerfang. If you see it, give it a friendly hello from me! And by \"hello\" I mean \"stab.\"",
[86776]="Thelsamar's a great place to live, but we don't have all of the amenities of Ironforge. I'm always running out of bronze! I need more bronze if I'm going to keep making tools and kettles and pots!$B$BI can tell you have a little experience at the forge. Think you could smelt me some bronze bars? I can pay you well for it!",
[86777]="Many satyr corrupt Azshara, but none are as terrible as the Legashi. Led by Varrox Bleakhoof, their camps litter the northern peninsula. They have driven us from our homes, and I fear they will ransack Ursolan before long.$B$BWe must strike back if we are to have any chance of survival.$B$BMaster Feardred, a servant of Varrox, oversees a nearby camp to the south. You can see it from here. Feardred is a key target in weakening Varrox's forces. Kill him, and bring me his amulet.",
[86784]="My associate Eleanor Shackleton prides herself on traveling the wilds, surviving against weather and monsters. She is currently camped not far from here, in the hills to the west, and I remember a piece of advice that she once gave me: \"When you think you have enough firewood, gather five times more.\"$B$BIf you have some spare time, you could collect some wood in this basket and take it to her camp. I'm sure she could give you a few tips about the existence of a traveling adventurer.",
[86791]="Not long ago I sent a party of scouts to gather information on the Legashi stronghold and possibly find our chieftain. They have yet to return. I am beginning to fear the worst.$B$BThe Legashi have many camps to the east of here. If any members of the party are still alive they are likely somewhere nearby.",
[86792]="The satyr within the Legashi stronghold are even more fearsome than those of the outer camps. When our party was discovered, we found ourselves overwhelmed.$B$BOne of us was slain, and another captured. I was the only one able to successfully retreat. I cannot return to Rageroar with my head hung in shame, but I cannot fight the Legashi alone, either.$B$BI ask you, then, to assist me in weakening the satyr's forces. Go into their stronghold and slay them.",
[86796]="You there, $r!$B$BThese fiends ambushed my scouting party, and have taken me captive. I don't know what plans they have for me, but I don't intend to find out. I must escape and return to Ursolan; no doubt Korsa is worried about me.$B$BWhile I would love to break out of this cage and leave a trail of satyr corpses in my wake, I'm afraid I'm slightly outnumbered.$B$BPerhaps you share my hatred for the fiends, and would help me escape?",
[86797]="With the Legashi stronghold weakened, we can return to Ursolan in honor.$B$BGo ahead of me, and inform Gatekeeper Rageroar of the situation here.",
[86798]="With the satyr weakened, now is the time to mount a counter-offensive. Prince Halanox, commander of the Legashi Stronghold, will be our target. However, we still lack the numbers to face him head-on.$B$BSince the Legashi drove us out we have been cut off from the furbolgs of Timbermaw Hold. We could call upon them for reinforcements, but we will need an emissary. You will be that emissary, $n.$B$BGo to Timbermaw Hold and find a furbolg named Gorn One Eye. He will provide us with the soldiers we need.",
[86799]="<Furze lets loose an ugly, hacking, cough.>$B$BHear me, $r, I haven't much strength to speak. I am stricken by an illness unlike any I have ever known. It is as if my blood itself is aflame, and my very essence is coming undone. I can hardly move, much less fetch help.$B$BPlease, go find Elder Bramblesnap. Her tent is just northwest of here. She will know what to do.",
[86804]="Furze is not the first with his affliction. Since the Legashi's attacks against us began, many Blackmaw have presented with a similar illness. Each one eventually fell to corruption, becoming mindless and destructive.$B$BI have been working towards a cure. My studies indicate that one could possibly be made by transmuting the Legashi's own firewater, but I cannot acquire it myself.$B$BYou might find firewater, or a way to brew it, in the Legashi camps to the east. You would be a great help in doing so.",
[86812]="I have transmuted the firewater into a tincture which I believe will be the key to undoing the Legashi's corruption. Eager as I am to ease the suffering of the Blackmaw, it must be tested.$B$BI have seen many of the coursers and skystormers east of Ursolan suffering from the satyr's corruption. They will serve as our test subjects.$B$BGo, and test my would-be cure on the afflicted beasts. Before giving the tincture the beast must be weakened to ensure it can be administered with little resistance.",
[86813]="I must say, $c. I have not felt this optimistic in some time. This tincture could be the panacea that saves us from the satyr's ever-expanding blight. Even if we remain in these camps for the rest of our lives we will stand strong and free of corruption.$B$BGo to Furze and give him this panacea. He has suffered for long enough. Return to me to report any findings.",
[86814]="I will send the reinforcements to Ursolan at once.$B$BTake this banner. When you are ready to face Halanox, plant it in his demonic summoning circle. This will provoke him, and signal our warriors to strike.$B$BOnce Halanox is defeated, inform Gatekeeper Rageroar.",
[86925]="It appears this cauldron could be used to brew the firewater that Elder Bramblesnap is after.$B$BIf only you knew how. Surely, one of the satyr in the Legashi Encampment must carry a recipe.",
[86926]="The recipe reads:$B$BHarvest ye the sprout of hell$Bbushel o' five will serve ye well$Bmixed with mote of demon's power$Bshall usher in their final hour",
[86927]="As the satyrweed and fel mote splash into the boiling liquid, a plume of noxious gas emerges.$B$BBest to hold your nose, quickly grab a sample, and bring it back to Elder Bramblesnap.",
[87288]="Hello, traveler! I hope you are enjoying your visit to our village. I like Dolanaar because it is small and rustic and everyone is friendly.$B$BI'm a local trader, and I bring in all sorts of tools and trinkets that might be useful to you in your travels. Indeed, if you are interested in a trade, I find myself in need of some nightsaber pelts. While these majestic creatures are beautiful, the local ones are rather aggressive, so don't feel too bad about defending yourself.",
[87295]="You may have seen the Redstone basilisks wandering the wastes outside while you were on your way to Nethergarde Keep. They're tough creatures, well adapted to survival in the Blasted Lands. One of their key qualities is their sturdy scales, which reflect heat, protect against sand and wind, and even deflect weapon blows!$B$BThey're a perfect material for making shields, and if you can bring me a bundle, I'll compensate you well. Only bring ones in good condition!",
[87346]="When the Legashi overran the Blackmaw, the rest of the Timbermaw sealed their passage to the hold to keep out the satyr. We had no idea they lived on as refugees.$B$BI would gladly aid my brethren, but we are fighting our own battles. Like the Legashi threaten the Blackmaw, the Deadwood do likewise to us. We haven't many warriors to spare.$B$BThe Deadwood chieftain, Bloodmaw, is in Felpaw Village to the south. Eliminating him would greatly ease our struggle. Bring me his mace, and you will have our aid.",
[87451]="This trinket, carried by the ogre, seems to be a small stone carving depicting an orc family. It may be a memento from the orcs who lived here when this was the town of Rockard, before the ogres invaded.$B$BIt probably has sentimental or spiritual value to the survivors at Stonard.",
[87491]="Sss! The foul Dark Irons have summoned me and kept me caged next to their petty fire pit!$B$BFire must run wild, run free! Release me! Must escape! Must BURN!$B$BNo Dark Iron is safe! Burn them to the ground! Burn their black powder! Burn their fortress, their fuses, their folly!$B$BLet me out and I will BURN THEM ALL!",
[87492]="You may have seen some of the unusual crystal growths that dot this crater. I'm not a miner, but these growths don't seem to fit with the kinds of soil deposits all around here.$B$BI believe I caught sight of a damaged crystal not far from here while I was foraging. I wonder if it holds any secrets about the origins of these strange formations? If you happen to spot it, I would love to investigate a sample piece.",
[87494]="This scale is slightly more reflective and iridescent than the others, as if it's embedded with tiny particles of crystal.$B$BTorwa Pathfinder might be able to make something of this.",
[87760]="I have received word back from Darnassus, $n!$B$BFrom the animal samples, we learned that the naga dominated these sea creatures to use as unwilling mounts and beasts of burden. The ones that were too obstinate, or too old or badly injured, they drove out for sport. Monstrous!$B$BIt is our sacred duty to put a stop to this!$B$BThe naga have forces in the Ruins of Mathystra, and they must be seizing threshers from off the shore. Find their beastmistress, slay her, and bring back her tools of domination!",
[88756]="The Dark Irons have a few camps east of here on Direforge Hill, and they've stolen a bunch of explosives from our construction site and hauled 'em back to their tents.$B$BI don't need tae tell ya what kinda mischief Dark Irons can get up tae with a barrel o' powder!$B$BI know the Dark Irons are dangerous, but we need those barrels back. You can tell 'em from other barrels because of the red markings on 'em. We cannae let the Dark Irons keep 'em!",
[88807]="Azshara may appear beautiful, but it is a cursed place. There are horrors deep beneath its waters, waiting to emerge and tear the world asunder.$B$BAll we can do for now is fight the horrors that have already surfaced.$B$BThe Spitelash Naga occupy the Ruins of Eldarath to the north east. The ones within the ruins are well-fortified, so we must pick off the weaker ones along the outskirts first.$B$BAs you can see, we could always use another fighter here, if you are up to the task.",
[88809]="Millennia ago, Eldarath was a sight to behold; a living testament to the glory and might of the Kaldorei. What we call Eldarath today is hardly a pile of rubble by comparison.$B$BNonetheless, what remains is worth salvaging, if only to preserve our history. The Spitelash must be driven out before Eldarath is completely ransacked.$B$BFollowing the road north east will lead you right into the heart of the ruins. Go there, and retrieve as many of our relics as you can--and their commander's head.",
[88812]="I fear time may soon forget the Kaldorei house of Ravencrest. A lone, crumbling, monument is the only surviving proof of their presence here.$B$BThe monument can be found atop the cliffs at the very tip of the southern peninsula. Spitelash enchantresses there have a set of power stones which they use to channel their magic. Take this ward, and nullify them. This will cripple the Spitelash's magic, and give us an upper hand in driving them out.$B$BWhile you're at it, be sure to take out a few naga yourself.",
[88813]="Your final target is Warlord Krellian, the leader of the Spitelash. He cowers behind his guards in the Temple of Zin-Malor in the ruins of Eldarath.$B$BCut off Krelian's head, and his minions will be slithering back to the sea in fear. Then, finally, Azshara will belong to Kaldorei once again.",
[88821]="While scouting along the cliffs of the Shattered Strand, one of our sentinels noticed a kaldorei woman on the beach.$B$BClearly, she is not with our expedition, and she did not have the makings of a fighter. I wonder then, what she could be doing in such a hostile place as this.$B$BIf you can, try to make contact with her. I would like to know her purpose for being here, and if our interests are perhaps aligned.$B$BShe was last seen on the eastern coast, along the north side of the Bay of Storms.",
[88857]="<The sentinel speaks in a low whisper>$B$BListen, $c, before they hear us. I am a sentinel from Talrendis Point. The satyr here believe me injured, but I am only feigning; waiting for the moment they drop their guard and I can escape.$B$BYour arrival is perhaps such a moment.$B$BHelp me out of here, would you?",
[88884]="Just south of here, along the beach, there are some tablets of highborne writing. They document the highborne's investigations into the laws and powers of the arcane.$B$BThe tablets are being kept in pagoda-like structures, guarded by naga, so I wouldn't dare attempt to procure them myself.$B$BFortunately, I've found myself a new assistant!$B$BSo, what do you say? Think you could be of further use in the pursuit of knowledge?",
[88917]="I came here in search of highborne artifacts. You could call me an archaeologist of sorts.$B$BThe ruins of Eldarath to the west hold many of them, although the naga are looting the ruins as we speak.$B$BA naga called Lady Sesspira leads the pillaging; no doubt keeping the best finds for herself.$B$BIf my research is correct, I believe she may be in possession of the staff of Archmage Selwyn, a fallen highborne mage.$B$BI need your help to get that staff, $r. Scholars like me are ill-suited for combat.",
[89001]="Greetings traveller!$B$BIf yer lookin' for a place to hang yer hat, look no further than Berdun's travel lodge! The tent's in a bit o' disrepair right now, but that can be remedied.$B$BTell ye what. If ye get me what I need to fix the tent, I'll let ye stay here for free. How's that sound?$B$BI'll need some mosshoof hides. The easiest to hunt mosshooves are just north o' here, but the hide of any mooshoof will do.",
[89013]="What's a travel lodge without somethin' to drink?$B$BI can brew a fine mead, but I'm gettin' a bit on in years to gather the honey myself. There are wasp nests in the trees north of the Haldaar camp, an' west of Valormok. If ye see hippogryphs, yer in the right place.$B$BThey're nasty buggers, but the honey is like nothin' ye've ever tasted. I'll lend ye my pellet gun to knock down the hives, ye can't reach 'em otherwise.",
[89015]="If ye fancy yourself a real angler, there's bigger fish out here than ye can catch with a rod.$B$BMammoth Sharks lurk in the deepest waters of the northern an' southern coasts. They swim far out, right before the sea floor drops away into the great ocean.$B$BThey're mighty big; I'd advise ye take a group of anglers with ye.$B$BDwarf like me? I prefer dry land. Those sharks'd swallow me in one bite.$B$BIf ye do go hunting one, bring me a cut o' the meat. I'd be mighty thankful.",
[89037]="On the beaches of the northern peninsula, east of here, I came upon the Tower of Eldara. While surveying the site, I noticed a large orange murloc wielding a spiked club, and carrying a peculiar glowing crystal. Given the location, it was likely the kind that the highborne used to store their history and memories.$B$BWe must recover that crystal, $r. Who knows what secrets it could contain?$B$BThe best route to the tower is along the cliffs, with the nearest way up being just west of here.",
[89038]="It is said that Queen Azshara once bestowed a gift upon the kaldorei of House Ravencrest; an emblem of great beauty and magical power. This mark was given as recognition of the Ravencrests' unwavering loyalty to the queen.$B$BThe mark was last seen near the Ravencrest Monument, atop the cliffs of the southern peninsula. Securing such a relic would be the discovery of a lifetime.$B$BAs always, the ruins of the monument are crawling with Spitelash, but I trust you're rather adept at handling them by now.",
[89053]="I know you were initially sent here on reconnaissance, $n, but you've done a great deal for the field of archaeology.$B$BSurely, after all of your toil, you'd like to know what fruits my studies will come to bear.$B$BTo that end, before you return to your camp, I'd like to show you something. Would you oblige me?",
[89228]="Any travel lodge worth its salt's gotta have somethin' to eat.$B$BSquid are in season, and ye can fish 'em up from the coasts here in Azshara. Never was much of an angler myself, but I'm a mean cook!$B$BWhat do ye say? Feelin' some seafood?$B$BIf ye aren't much for fishin', try makin' friends with one! Or pay 'em for their goods and buy some.",
[89470]="<With Saria's true intentions revealed, and a bag of powerful artifacts in hand, perhaps now would be a good time give Commander Truesong her report.>",
[90487]="$n, I have little more to offer. If you mean to make the long trek up the mountain, you might do well to speak with some of its ancient caretakers.$B$BFollow the road to the west. Look north, toward the foot of the mountain. You will eventually see an outpost, a remnant of the guardians that once roamed the slopes. There is an ancient there named Fraxinus. He and his friends can assist you.",
[90647]="With all of the ingredients you assembled I was able infuse the staff you recovered with a new magic. You should now be able to bring this to bear to counteract the magic of the Wild Gods that Ve'han has so brazenly stolen.$B$BWe will need to test it, however. Bring this to the druid known as Tiala Whitemane at the Summit of Eternity. She may be able to help.",
[90702]="<Someone, or something, has rummaged through the dirt, leaving fragments of bone scattered about. An oddly shaped indentation leads deeper into the cold, wet dirt.$B$BSomething within the area may have caused the disruption.>",
[90750]="Battles are often long and hard fought, led by those willing to stand against an imminent threat and look death in the face.$B$BThe truth is, many sacrifices were made, not just on the battlefield. We often overlook those who do their part to contribute.$B$BJust yonder is a peasant by the name of... well come to think of it, I don't even know his name. What kind of person am I? He's kept us well-tended and nourished throughout our stay.$B$BCould you speak with him? Let him know the job's done.",
[90789]="There isn't much time, $n! My scrying spells have revealed a powerful source of magic. I cannot leave the tower, and would ask you to kill the vile creature in possession of this artifact.$B$BThe beast is known as Scalebeard, hiding in a cave among the Bay of Storms. Burn him to ashes and take the prismatic shell from his den.",
[90813]="<The large hunk of crystal is even heavier than it looks. While it appears to be quite the prize, its true nature is unknown to you. Someone with knowledge in geology could say what you've really found.>",
[90854]="Livin' out in da wild for five years done take a toll on our supplies. We had to make dis place from scratch! We could use your skills as a leatherworker.$B$BI need to repair some of da tents and buildings, and patch up some armor. You bring me a pair of Rugged Armor Kits and a Cured Rugged Hide, I help you turn it into something special.",
[90865]="Just north of here lies the ruins of battles past. A dwindling scourge presence remains.$B$BThough the mindless undead are a threat themselves, the watchers maintain a vigilant eye on those entering the area, making removal of the scourge threat even more difficult.$B$BRemove the threat by taking from these watchers that which they value most.",
[90902]="I am proud to welcome another newly risen paladin to our ranks. As you begin to reconnect with the light you may notice that certain abilities that were once second nature to you may cause you considerable pain to use now, particularly those involving channeling the light to heal yourself or others.$B$BThe only way around this problem is--unfortunately--to go through it. Like any other muscle that has atrophied, you must push through the pain and exercise the flesh for it to return to full function.",
[91208]="Not all of our fellow Paladins who rise again are quick to acclimate to our new reality. Some struggle to reconcile that they are now, in a way, the very thing they spent their lives fighting against.$B$BThese individuals often simply need a kind gesture and a sympathetic ear. Unfortunately, many others are quick to turn violent. Find the frightened paladin who fled into the hills directly west of this chapel. Extend a hand in friendship. Lead them back into the light if you can.",
[91209]="Lordaeron may not be what it used to be, but our home still needs protection from all manner of threats and it's time for you to go out and face the world. Your next stop should be the town of Brill in central Tirisfal Glades. Go and meet with Shari Stilwell there. She can see to your continued training.$B$BOne last bit of advice before you go--take extra care as a paladin traveling through Forsaken lands. There are many in the Dark Lady's service who distrust us and our proximity to the light.",
[91282]="It is encouraging to see my newly risen brothers and sisters thrive as you have. It is only through community and shared faith that we can truly realize our full potential however, and to that end we've begun to form a new paladin order right here in Tirisfal.$B$BIf you wish to learn more, you should visit our monastery on the edge of the Whispering Woods. It is called Bandarion Keep. It's on the bluffs just northwest of the Solliden Farmstead, and should be hard to miss.",
[91285]="Normally we'd show our newcomers a bit more hospitality, but we've got a bit of a murloc problem at the moment.$B$BA tribe of murlocs used to use the keep as their spawning grounds. They've been a problem since we moved in and kicked them out, but now it's starting to get out of hand. You look like you've seen some action. Do you think you could help us drive back some of these pests? You'll find them lurking in the bluffs along the road to the east, and in the camps around the lake to the west.",
[91294]="Now that the immediate threat of the murloc attacks is under control, I'd encourage you to show yourself around our stronghold. It isn't much yet, but it's home.$B$BWhen you are done exploring, seek out Danitha Morr, our leader. She can help you get settled in.$B$BI'm very glad to have met you, $n. May the light be your guide.",
[91316]="This far from the Undercity, logistics are challenging and we have a dire shortage of building materials needed to help restore this fortress. I'd like your help with that.$B$BThe ruined village of Shadowvale can be found in the Whispering Forest, just southwest of here. One of the buildings has an old root cellar used to store all sorts of things. There are likely to be usable materials down there. Scavenge what you can and return to us.",
[91317]="Not all risen paladins have acclimated well to our new existence, as you may have seen yourself already. Some have carried forward their prejudices from life, and continue to visit violence upon their fellow Forsaken.$B$BAs it stands we are mistrusted by our people who remember well the persecution inflicted by the living in the name of the light, and these attacks do not help. A number of these tarnished have taken up residence at Shadowvale to the southwest. End them and bring me their leader's head.",
[91488]="During our last skirmish with the blood elves, my tent was badly damaged. For three nights, I have been at the mercy of the elements.$B$BIt can be repaired with a few mosshoof hides, but a lack of sleep has left me unable to hunt them myself.$B$BThe easiest mosshooves to hunt are west and south of here, but the hide of any mooshoof will do.",
[91497]="<The seal of the first crystal bears the mark of a sword. Its energy must be channeled by an expert warrior.$B$BThe seal of the middle crystal bears the mark of a glaive. Its energy must be channeled by one of both martial and magical prowess.$B$BThe seal of the last crystal bears the mark of a talon. Its energy must be channeled by one at home in the wilds.$B$BIt's likely that some of Rimtori's officers are carrying these seals to aid her in the spell. Taking them would no doubt be troublesome for her.>",
[91500]="<Seeing how the energies of the crystals are attuned to the seals, you reason that destroying a seal, thereby releasing its energy all at once, could cause its crystal to do the same.$B$BThe explosive results would certainly draw Rimtori's ire. It would also present the perfect opportunity to attack her while she's flustered.>",
[91531]="Return to Belgrom in Orgrimmar. He will want to see her head for himself!$B$BAh, this is indeed a good day. Thank you for your help, $n.",
[91538]="Rimtori's tome still sits atop its pedestal. Who knows what secrets its pages could hold?$B$BPerhaps it would be best not to leave such a powerful artifact out here in the wilds.",
[91547]="You were wise to take this, $n. More than killing Rimtori, keeping this out of the blood elves' hands will ensure they are powerless to retaliate against us.$B$BAs for deciphering the tome itself, I have a contact in Orgrimmar who dabbles in such things--a warlock named Zevrost. He can be found in the Cleft of Shadow.",
[91548]="I do not speak Thalassian, but these diagrams are familiar to me.$B$BKnowing the blood elves' addiction to mana, I'd say they were trying to summon demons to drain them of their fel magic.$B$BSimply consuming such powerful energy is a waste. We could harness it for a much greater purpose.$B$B<Zevrost bookmarks a page in the tome>$B$BThere is an Altar of Storms in the Blasted Lands. Perform this ritual there to summon the demon Vek'zol. His heart will make a potent reagent. Think of the power we could have!",
[91564]="We've been stuck here for five years, and we've had to build everything from scratch! Do you know how much I've had to improvise just to do any engineering?$B$BHey, if you can help me out with some materials, I can make it worth your time! Build me a couple of Mithril Casings and a Mechanical Repair Kit so that I can fix up some stuff, and I'll show you a few things I've figured out.",
[91568]="What the beaches here lack in looks, they make up for in value!$B$BMost of the ruins here have been picked clean, but there's some serious loot under that sand. Problem is, it's all scattered, and the naga make a long search a bit impractical. So, what's a girl to do?$B$BEnter the Treasure Trowel 3000! The all-in-one treasure detecting shovel! A personal invention of mine.$B$BTake this baby down to the eastern shore, and bring back whatever you find. Then, we can split the profits!",
[91569]="Listen kid, everyone out here's scramblin' for the same thing. Belgrom, the elves, the naga, they all wanna piece 'a that ancient highborne magic.$B$BMe? Couldn't care less, but I know a seller's market when I see one.$B$BI've seen blood elf arcanists carrying special wands. They're used to extract magical energy from artifacts the elves find. The arcanists stay at a camp east of the elves' base camp, along the cliffs. Get me one of those wands and I'll put you on to the score of a lifetime!",
[91607]="<The large hunk of crystal is even heavier than it looks. While it appears to be quite the prize, its true nature is unknown to you. Someone with an eye for valuables could say what you've really found.>",
[91608]="There are few luxuries out here on the frontier. A barrel of good drink would surely boost the camp's morale.$B$BIn my younger days, I took a recipe for a delicious brew off the corpse of a dwarf I killed. All I need is some honey. Fortunately, the wasp nests to the west are overflowing with it.$B$BTake my pellet gun. This will allow you to knock the nests out of the trees. Be warned, however, it will do little against the wasps themselves.",
[91610]="Meat is well and good, but a varied diet makes the body stronger.$B$BWinter squid are in season, and can be fished from the coasts here in Azshara. I never took to angling myself. I much prefer the safety of land. Although, were you to fish some up, or obtain them via some other means, I would greatly appreciate it.",
[91611]="If you wish for a true test of angling prowess, there are bigger fish than you can catch with a rod.$B$BMammoth Sharks lurk in the deepest waters of the northern and southern coasts. They swim far out, right before the sea floor drops away into the great ocean.$B$BThey are massive creatures. I would advise you to bring a hunting party.$B$BIf you do go after one, bring me a cut of the meat.",
[91685]="When we first got here, I did some surveying for any untapped resources. Y'know, typical prospector stuff.$B$BI didn't see nothin' special 'til I searched Lake Mennar, to the south. There, I saw a huge rift floating above the water's surface. I couldn't get close, but I think it was an open leyline.$B$BIf I'm right, we can use this wand to siphon magic straight from the source! Bottle that up, sell it to the highest bidder, and bam! I'm rich!$B$BIf you go and siphon that rift for me, I'll cut you in.",
[91688]="You've managed to cut a swath through the undead that have kept us trapped here for so many years, and for that we can never repay you.$B$BI have one more favor to ask, on behalf of us all. We know that there are druids at the summit. They protect Nordrassil and the Well of Eternity.$B$BWhy did they never come help us to escape?$B$BFor five years we have been trapped here. At last we have a glimmer of hope... but why didn't the druids come for us?$B$BLet someone know that we're still alive!",
[91696]="Deadwood set on my pup and his sire. He stood fast, fought to the death as our guard. We must go home, but the way is dark and full of jaws.$B$BStay near, guard us well. I will lead, you will fend, and we will see den safe.",
[91697]="Thank you for helping gather bear berries. Small steps build trust! With the aroma of berry resin on you, the Elders should be more welcoming of you.$B$BGo and speak with Elder Mistpaw and Elder Pinespeaker.",
[91698]="<A matriarchal furbolg speaks to you from within the cage>$B$B\"Deadwood trap me and my cub in tough cage. Key hang on Deadwood Warden belt. You hunt them, take key, lift latch, set us free. Do this, and Barkskin know your heart true.\"",
[91723]="Blast it! Every time I try to calibrate these sensitive arcane instruments, they get thrown off again by a surge of energy.$BThe surges seem to be coming from the north, where those primitive Kobolds have been practicing their crude magic. Could you clear some of them out, so I can continue my work?",
[91724]="Almost there, and... By the Nether! Something is still disrupting my instruments.$B$BThis is most frustrating, $n. I have heard rumors that the local bandits have been practicing spells near Stone Cairn Lake. Maybe if you stop them, these disruptions will finally cease and I can get some work done?",
[91725]="I was sent by Master Theocritus to pick up some enchanting supplies from the trading post, but on the way back I was ambushed by a pack of gnolls!$B$BI dropped the package and escaped, but if I return without it, I'll be cleaning up after the polymorph experiments for weeks as punishment! Do you think you could find the supplies for me?",
[91732]="Good steel is in short supply after the war, and our tools have suffered for it. The Jasperlode miners used finely-crafted picks, and I imagine some of them are still there in the depths of the mine. Could you retrieve some for me, and I'll see if I can repurpose the steel?",
[91733]="I was bringing back a supply shipment from the trading post, but my wagon tipped over and the supplies fell in the river! Before I could catch them, they had already washed downstream.$B$BBetween the murlocs and wolves down there, I don't stand a chance of retrieving the supplies on my own. You seem like the hardy sort. Do you think you could find them for me?",
[91734]="<The Forsaken sways unsteadily>$B$B'ey! <hic> Do me a favor ... would ya?$B$BGo to uh ... Azshara 'n ... tell <hic> Jediga ...$B$BExpectin' a ... 'mportant deliv'ry <hic>",
[91735]="Listen, $c, you'd best not be hangin' round here for long. But since you are, perhaps you can do a little favor for me?$B$BI be expecting a certain something from a Jediga, in Azshara. She and some orcs be havin' a camp out there. Go and tell her Jes'rimon sent you, and I'll owe you one.",
[91737]="My duties occasionally require reagents from the farther corners of Azeroth. However, I am always needed here in Thunder Bluff, and so I am in need of competent aides.$B$BTo that end, I am awaiting a delivery from an orc named Jediga, in Azshara. If you care to make yourself useful, find her camp, and inquire as to when I can expect it to arrive.",
[91740]="This murloc has no doubt been terrorizing the local roads for some time. You suspect the nearby watch guards will want to know of its demise.",
[91741]="<One of the kobolds dropped this book. It looks like the kobold might have tried to eat it.$B$BBrother Paxton inside the abbey has a small library he maintains. The book must have come from there.>",
[91743]="Those awful kobolds are eating my books! You have to get them back before they devour my whole library.",
[91745]="Go talk to the new mining apprentice, Kelsey Fargo. She works right outside the mine and has probably seen what the kobolds are up to. Maybe she can teach you a thing or two about mining while you're at it.",
[91751]="Are you looking for an opportunity to practice skinning? My husband usually helps with hunting wolves, but he's busy up by the abbey. I could use a hand collecting more pelts to finish the orders I'm working on.",
[91752]="Every once in a while, a kobold comes through yelling \"Picture for Narf!\" I don't know who Narf is. Maybe one of the head kobolds at the back of the mine? I bet he has a whole sack of books by now.$B$BGo get those books and bring them to our local law enforcement, Marshal McBride. You should find a friend to help. Those kobolds inside the mine are a lot meaner.",
[91753]="Academic rigor is of course essential to the enchanter's craft, but a practical foundation can pay dividends. Consider, as an example, the lowly Kobold. Lacking formal education, they nevertheless demonstrate a sort of innate aptitude for simple cantrips and enchantments.$B$BObtain some of their wax effigies and deconstruct the enchantments bound within them. You may find it elucidating.",
[91754]="I haven't seen |5$r like you in years!$B$BOh, I don't know what to do! My friend Fraxinus is sick, and I can't leave him alone!$B$BCould you please fetch me some Untainted Soil from the uncorrupted land southeast of here? I can make some poultices that may help him to feel better.",
[91755]="Have you seen those nasty tainted shrubberies wandering around this valley?$B$BThose plants are mean, but some of them are not entirely toxic. Their leaves can have medicinal purposes.$B$BWould you be so kind as to fetch me some Verdant Leaves? You'll have to do a little pruning, of course.",
[91758]="You're not done with those kobolds yet. We just got word from Kelsey that a kobold left the mine carrying a large sack of books. I need you to track down this kobold so we can retrieve the books for Brother Paxton.$B$BGo talk to Tordrin Sternblade. He's the new Hunter trainer that just arrived from Ironforge. You can find him behind the abbey, near the stable. He can help you track this kobold thief.",
[91770]="With the ingredients you brought, I can make some simple medicine. This poultice should aid Fraxinus. He is old, you know, and he was badly burned during the wars. His bark hurts and his limbs ache. He is my best friend and I just want him to feel better!$B$BTake this poultice and apply it liberally to all of the places where his bark is split and his sap is weeping.",
[91772]="Alright. Take this kobold tracking kit. It'll let ye' track the kobold that Marshal McBride is concerned with.$B$BFollow the tracks and bring what ye' find to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire.$B$BI have a feelin' these varmints are up to somethin' outside Northshire. So ye'll be needin' Dughan's help.",
[91775]="While you're investigating the Fargodeep Mine, see if you can find any of Brother Paxton's books to return. In particular, Paxton is very concerned about a book titled, \"Fun with Elementals\". He thinks even a kobold could use it to summon an elemental servant. Be warned, the depths of the mine are fairly dangerous. You should bring friends.$B$BTake this book bag to protect the books when you find them!",
[91777]="There are just two books left missing on Brother Paxton's list: \"Geomancy for Curious Young Wizards\" and \"Arcane Explainer: Magical Stuff in Simple Words\".$B$BThe kobolds must have taken them to the Jasperlode Mine. Please track down those two books and bring them back to Brother Paxton.$B$BBut I'm afraid it will be quite dangerous. If the \"apprentice\" kobold was summoning an elemental, who knows what the master can do. I'd bring some friends if I were you.",
[91794]="We been stuck up here for years, always fighting against de Scourge, but we never lose hope. We fight to survive. We fight for da Horde. Da Alliance shares dis fight, but we never forget dat we still got history. Still got blood.$B$BFar to da east, at Dae'gun, dere are Horde flags from da war. Da demons carry scraps and remains as trophies from da battle, especially da tough ones. Bring me a flag and some heraldry so I can put it up and show da Alliance dat da Horde is still strong!",
[91858]="A most unfortunate turn of events in Silverpine has presented a unique opportunity for us to prove our worth in the eyes of the horde.$B$BA pair of dignitaries from the Earthen Ring went missing in Silverpine Forest en route to Tarren Mill. We don't know much else but rumors say that this is becoming quite the diplomatic incident. If we can recover these missing persons, it could help gain us the legitimacy we so dearly need.$B$BWe have a man at The Sepulcher, Trevan Rol. Travel there and speak with him.",
[91859]="Cutting straight to it, these \"dignitaries\" are no ordinary diplomats. One was a Tauren. Ordinary enough for the Earthen Ring, but the other--and you'll scarcely believe this--was an elf. A *high* elf. They were cloaked, but I've seen quel'dorei before and I'd bet my good pinky finger that's what I saw.$B$BWhy was an elf accompanying a Tauren through horde territory? Well, your guess is as good as mine. That's as much as I know, so I'd suggest speaking with Deathguard Baldren near the entrance to town.",
[91860]="Out on patrol last night I spotted a group of gnolls dumping a very large body onto a pyre on the shores of Fenris Isle. I didn't see an elf or any smaller corpses, but I'd say this doesn't bode well for them.$B$BIf you are brave or stupid you are welcome to charge into Fenris Isle to learn more, but if you ask me, it's a lot of work to find some snooty elf that's probably long dead.$B$BI know you paladins love swearing oaths and taking on lost causes, but this one isn't worth it. Trust me.",
[91861]="<The fact that you found only one body is a hopeful sign. Perhaps the High Elf that Trevan and Hadrec described is still alive somewhere deeper inside the nearby fortress?>",
[91862]="Quel'dorei? No, I am no \"quel'dorei\". I am Lumina Windsinger and I am shen'dorei. One of the Windshaper Skyborne.$B$BI came to these lands as a guest of the Earthen Ring. My companion Banon and I were passing through Silverpine to reach the Arathi Highlands so that we could study the elemental convergences there. Clearly, we didn't make it.$B$BWe have no time for this now though. Kill the gnolls nearby. Retrieve the key to this cage and free me. I will tell you the rest once we are safely away.",
[91877]="Not many demon hunters remain on Azeroth now, but a few of us continue to hunt the most dangerous or hidden threats.$B$BA colleague of mine, Maerion Thaelemaches, headed to Hyjal to investigate rumors of demons there. While there are many demons in the dangerous Darkwhisper Gorge, there is suspicion that the demons that assaulted the mountain during the last war might not be completely defeated.$B$BThis bears investigation.",
[91881]="With the warlocks under control, I'd say this area's well in wing.$B$B<The crow nods sagely, looking pleased.>$B$BThough our work here is done, there are other areas that could use your help and as an underwing of mine I would like you to go see what all the fuss is about.$B$BFollow the path northwest up the road to the old tern outpost. An old friend awaits!",
[91882]="Years ago, the Horde and the Alliance put aside their differences to fight a greater threat--the Legion. On Mount Hyjal, the Grand Alliance forces battled Archimonde and his minions to a halt.$B$BThe retreat from the mountain was perilous, however, and some brave fighters were left behind.$B$BNow that the way up the great mountain is again open, perhaps some of these heroes remain alive in the wilds? Go to Mount Hyjal and brave its dangers. Find what became of our forces there.",
[91883]="While fighting off the Wormwing harpies I was brutally ambushed by a harpy named Zarrat who patrols this area. She snatched my spear and carried it off before I could recover. To what end she desired to possess it, I cannot say.$B$BThat spear has been in my family for generations and is of great importance to me. If you spot Zarrat among the harpies, slay her and return my spear. She is stealthy, and will not be easily found, but I would be grateful to have my spear returned.",
[91920]="I wouldn't dare to question the effectiveness of Apothecary Renferrel's formulae, however I would be lying if I said that the potion made any noticeable difference.$B$BAlong the shore of Lake Lordamere are a swarm of murlocs, and of note, murlocs have eyes. I suspect the apothecary's willingness to try new things is suppressed by his recent obsession with hearts. Bring him a few.$B$BIf my choice is to inevitably die a second death or have Renferrel kill me for questioning his methods, I choose the latter.",
[91921]="Here is the new potion to aid in Quinn's recovery, made with love extracted from six whole hearts.$B$BNow, please excuse me before your presence necessitates more paperwork.",
[91923]="The mountain is overrun with wild growth, inflamed by the fel energies that rained down so long ago. Now the weeds and plants are angry, corrupted, poisoned.$B$BThere is a great thorn-bush called Celastrus that lurks about the slopes to the east. It kills animals, lashes out at other plants, feeds on the bodies of the dead. It must be destroyed!$B$BThe weeds must be cleared so that the mountain may regrow.",
[91952]="So much corruption rains down into Felwood from above. When the waters run high from Hyjal, they are filled with fel taint. It soaks into the ground and diseases the trees and plants.$B$BThere was a druid who lived in the wild, a hermit named Ketharas, who had a deep knowledge of the mountain. If anyone knows what has happened on Hyjal, it is he.$B$BI think that Felwood cannot heal until the problem on Hyjal is resolved.",
[92008]="Another new face?$B$BI shouldn't be surprised with the strength of our so-called wards these days. How's the fel down there? I haven't been away from this workshop in weeks. Say, while you're here, I do have some favors you may be able to help me with if you find yourself in the mood for errands.$B$BYou wouldn't believe how tricky it is to get proper parts all the way up here, let alone general building material for engineering. Nami in Everlook has a parts order waiting for me - care for a winter sprint?",
[92009]="There's something you should know about this order. There's a few inverted mana cells padded as well as I could at the bottom of the box. The cells have a tendency to discharge when they get bumped, and when not stabilized in time. It takes about two hours for the contents to fizzle.$B$BKaylaena will know what to do when she receives them, but I suggest going slow if you're going to ride saddled up Mount Hyjal.$B$BIf you need a refill, come back and I'll top off the canisters. Be careful, you know?",
[92011]="I'm going to need some time to sort out which plans to build first. Something I've been meaning to do is hike up to the old Horde base and see what kind of treasure can be made out of whatever trash is laying around there.$B$BIf you are heading up there, and have the space to carry it, keep your eyes peeled for scrap metal, wire, or chunks of bat... droppings! Look, it has its uses okay!$B$BYou can find the remains of the horde encampment far up the mountain, even beyond the Elderwild settlement.",
[92014]="Every time I take my attention off the supplies I've lugged up here for more than a few minutes, one of nature's finest thieves is pilfering and rummaging through it.$B$BThe damned foxes seem to have made a burrow beneath the boulders nearby. Apparently, me digging out this hole gave them an idea of their own.$B$BI'm working on a solution. Tell you what, bring back some of their fox tails. That'll teach them a lesson, and I'll hang the tails around the perimeter to scare the others off!",
[92015]="You say you want to help? Alright, I've got a task for ya.$B$BEver been skunked on a hot day? Nothing worse, I tell you. Bloody things cover everything within spittin' distance in the most vile lingering stench!$B$BA family of skunks have started making their home behind my equipment crates. Help me gently expel them from our perimeter and I'll think about sharing some of this gear, once we can get to it...$B$BI can't stress this enough: don't attack them - they WILL spray you!",
[92016]="The roots of Nordrassil stretch far and deep, thicker than riverbanks and older than memory. Such great size carries a great hunger. In healthy times, they drink of decay and renewal alike, drawing strength from the endless turning of the natural cycle.$B$BBut Hyjal has been wounded, its soil fouled by demonic venom.$B$BDescend into the deepest depths of the Well of Eternity. Study the roots there closely. We must know whether they have drawn in too much corruption... or if the World Tree may yet endure.",
[92017]="The flying creatures of the Summit still draw breath from the highest currents, where the corruption has not yet fully taken hold. Hippogryph feathers and chimaera hair drift through these winds, absorbing what the air remembers of an unspoiled land. I need these remnants to anchor and strengthen my purifying incense.$B$BGather them for me, so I may concentrate the wind's knowledge into cleansing smoke before we begin the ritual.",
[92020]="I've been taking notes and making drawings in my sketchbooks of all of the creatures living in Un'Goro Crater, and I made a few copies so that I can send them to people who might be interested!$B$BI have a sketchbook copy here that I've been meaning to get into the hands of the druids on Mount Hyjal, since I know that they love to study the natural world.$B$BHyjal's a bit of a trip, though. Do you think you could take it along in case you go there?",
[92064]="Let's try something else. You see that branch up there? Yep! That one. I need you to break it for me. I've got plenty of ropes tangled elsewhere, so there's no chance for catastrophic failure... I hope.$B$BTake a safe step back and take a few swings at this branch, would you?$B$B<Fenwick gestures at something above his head.>$B$BPlease be careful!",
[92065]="Will you aid us in our final battle, $r, and be a savior to the Blackmaw?$B$BVarrox Bleakhoof, bane of the Blackmaw: a demon whose appetite for destruction will never be satisfied. His corruption consumes all that it touches. Even now, he and his underlings continue to lay waste to our burrows.$B$BWe've come far in our fight against the Legashi, but for the Blackmaw to ever have a future, Varrox must fall.$B$BFind him in Blackmaw Hold, and strike him down. Only then can the Blackmaw finally be at peace.",
[92066]="When the Legashi invaded, many precious things were left behind in the commotion. Of particular value to me are two totems. They depict legends of our twin gods, Ursoc and Ursol.$B$BI know our immediate survival is of greatest concern, but we must also think of saving our people's history.$B$BThose totems are likely still in our former hold. If they are, you would be doing a great kindness by returning them to me.",
[92069]="Two behemoths patrol the place the Blackmaw once called home: Bonesnout, the Unbroken and Withermaw, the great bear. Generations of hunters have tried to fell them, and all have failed.$B$BI take no joy in asking you to slay these magnificent beasts, but my people need to be able to return home. The least I can do is ensure their deaths are not in vain. If you bring me their remains, I will fashion a weapon in memory of their strength.",
[92070]="The necklace is adorned with miscellaneous charms: scraps of feathers, acorn shells, and colorful pebbles. Its leather strap is torn. The ornamentation suggests it belonged to a Furbolg, while its small size and rough quality indicate a child's handiwork.$B$BThere's a chance the necklace is of some sentimental value to one of the Blackmaw. It may be good to find the owner and return it.",
[92094]="My brother Fenwick and I recently finished a successful rocket test, the only problem is, he hasn't come back yet! I lost sight of him floating off to the south after his parachute deployed.$B$BIt looks like he may have landed in Hyjal!$B$BIf you help him find his way out of where he landed, I'm sure he'd find a way to thank you. I'll be grateful to have my brother back!",
[92100]="<A spirit materializes before you, recovering from a full-body yawn.>$B$BYou have no ranks with you... and you are not dressed as a soldier. We repelled Archimonde then?$B$BIt's been so long. I had almost forgotten what I once was, but you... you must be one of the first to walk these craters in years.$B$B<The veteran glances at his surroundings.>$B$BLet us continue our conversation at an overlook with a view I remember vividly, just west of here. Long ago, I left my scabbard to rest there.",
[92101]="Hyjal is difficult to bear. Nightmares and murderous memories linger among the craters.$B$BBut you carry warmth from Kalimdor within you! My friend Tobin also enlisted and joined up with me, but I fear the worst for his soul.$B$BThe Alliance company gave us steeds to break in and bond with for our upcoming deployment. We took them on a joy ride through the Barrens. Carved our names into the bottom of the Great Lift in Thousand Needles.$B$BSee if the marks remain? It will bring ease to a weary soul.",
[92102]="Going so far out of your way solely for the fading wishes of a lost soul--thank you, $n. The presence of a hand contemplating the carvings, with the fragments of history that you know so far, was enough to bring me here. My presence, now, is tied to the strongest bond with the still-living.$B$BI beat Tobin to the salt flats, and he smoked me on the raceway.$B$BI recall clearer now. Meet me in Mourning's Rest--the site of our last battle--next to the broken cannon near the destroyed tower on the cliff.",
[92109]="Erm... 'Ello, $Gmister:miss;. I'm not supposed to talk to strangers, but... Hey, what are those shiny bottles sticking out of your backpack for? Are you an alchemist? That's so cool!$B$BWhen I grow up, I want to be an alchemist too. Daddy won't let me play with any of his herbs; too dangerous, he says.$B$BWell, I want to start learning now. Could you maybe get some supplies for me, pretty please?",
[92110]="Wow, my very first potion! Did you know that mixing those two herbs together would change the potion to a bright red color when you first started?$B$BThat was fun, but mixing a few flowers doesn't seem like the kind of alchemy Daddy does. He uses other ingredients too.$B$BI don't know what else to use, so let's try the first thing that comes to mind! Let's see... maybe murloc eyes? That sounds so gross, but I bet something will happen.",
[92111]="I see you try, and try is more than most. We give you good will with time, if you do the same.$B$BEnter our den and talk to Osi. She has open paws, will give you more chance to help.",
[92124]="We need to take stock of how many books are missing!$B$BGo talk to my useless assistant, Daniel. He can do a quick inventory and let us know how serious the problem is.$B$BHe's obsessed with the various trade professions in Elwynn Forest. The boy keeps focusing on those instead of his important work helping me.$B$BDon't let him prattle on about tradeskills, and find out what's happened to my books!",
[92147]="I am one of the last of the Highfeathers, the true followers of Aviana. We respect and revere the Matron of the Skies, and we call the Druids of the Talon our allies.$B$BThe Wormwing harpies have overrun much of this plateau. They reject our protector Aviana, and seek only to despoil the lands around us.$B$BBlood has been spilled and must be repaid. Scatter their feathers to the wind.",
[92169]="The Blackthorne Pact. That's what they call themselves. Apostate druids that have taken over Hyjal Summit. Violent, and extremist. They blame Malfurion Stormrage for robbing them of their immortality, and have sworn to reclaim the power that they were forced to relinquish. I did not understand the magic that empowered them before, but it's becoming clear now.$B$BTake the staff, use it on the Blackthorne druids around the mountain. It should respond to and dispel the wards protecting them.",
[92171]="To defeat Ve'han, we require a touch of the sky. A bit of the divine, where one's upward-turned face yearns to fly.$B$BHead to the Shrine of Aviana and seek out Skylord Omnuron. As the leader of the Druids of the Talon, he can assist in adding a touch of Aviana's grace.",
[92189]="Och, we had to make this village from scratch with what we could scrounge up after the war. All of the fighting has taken a toll on our weapons, not to mention the need for tools!$B$BI can always tell another blacksmith. Think you could spare the time and materials to make me some Dense Sharpening and Dense Grinding Stones? We could really use 'em!",
[92317]="So, the hermit druid seeks a force to balance the 'life' in this magic of his? Then the answer is death, naturally. You have come to the right place for such a thing.$B$BNo doubt you've seen the undead crawling all over my domain. They are fueled by stolen power that animates them even in death.$B$BThat stolen power is exactly what is needed in this spell you speak of. Kill the undead and search through their skulls for a coalesced Drop of Stolen Life. Return it to Ketharas once you have it.",
[92328]="With the extra supplies you brought back, I have enough materials on hand to finish up Yaely's original plans for this Glaive Thrower. I've been fixing this thing up for the past... well, it feels like forever!$B$BIf you can help me out and be a second pair of hands, it'd make this whole project go a lot faster! I can walk you through it, most of the hard stuff should be out of the way...$B$B<Kaylaena crosses her fingers.>$B$BThe driving system and the energy cells powering it are nearly set up.",
[92329]="There is a fel chimaera terrorizing beasts and travelers along hills. It is known to the Cenarion Circle as Ghansurok. I'll handle the aim and firing of the glaive thrower. Go to that drum by the cliff side. Let's see this blight driven from the mountain for good.$B$BI'll only have a chance of shooting it down if you can draw its attention. Once you have the beast by the ridge, find some place to hide!$B$BYes, I promise I have a full bag of maple seeds!",
[92335]="This magic you seek is as complex as it is wild. It needs a reagent that can provide a stable source of continual energy, and I know of just the thing.$B$BWhen Archimonde met his well-deserved end here, many of his lesser minions were also killed. His chief lieutenant, Azgalor, was slain--by mortals like you, no less!$B$BYou'll find the last physical remains of Azgalor in the middle of the ruins here. No need to bring all of that ash back to Ketharas. Just a pinch should be more than enough for his needs.",
[92343]="The burrow you speak of is a tunnel to Blackmaw Hold. In the past, the furbolg have guarded it fiercely, making it inaccessible to outsiders. With this satyr situation, however, we can get inside.$B$BSo close to Nordrassil, there would be actively growing roots. Older roots can be seen on the world's surface, but newer ones can only be found deep underground. Little is known of their magical properties.$B$BIf you were to bring me some samples to study, the druids of Thunder Bluff would be in your debt.",
[92344]="The burrow you speak of is a tunnel to Blackmaw Hold. In the past, the furbolg have guarded it fiercely, making it inaccessible to outsiders. With this satyr situation, however, we can get inside.$B$BSo close to Nordrassil, there would be actively growing roots. Older roots can be seen on the world's surface, but newer ones can only be found deep underground. Little is known of their magical properties.$B$BIf you were to bring me some samples to study, the Cenarion Circle would be in your debt.",
[92345]="You may have noticed the furbolg and satyr north of here fighting over a burrow. The conflict does not interest me as much as what could be inside. That burrow seems to lead beneath Nordrassil.$B$BI don't think I need to tell you how this could be of interest to the Kaldorei.$B$BWe have our hands full here as it is, but the druids of Darnassus should be informed. Find Mathrengyl Bearwalker in the Cenarion Enclave. He can decide if this is something worth pursuing.",
[92346]="You may have noticed the furbolg and satyr northeast of here, fighting over some burrow. The conflict does not interest me as much as what's inside. That burrow seems to lead beneath the world tree, and who knows what could be under there?$B$BWe're spread too thin to investigate ourselves, but I know a tauren who may appreciate the tip. Her name is Nara Wildmane, a druid in Thunder Bluff. Tell her Jediga sent you. Always good to have someone owe you a favor.",
[92432]="I bring ill tidings from Dalaran. Something has disrupted our leylines, causing erratic and destructive behavior from our constructs in the city.$B$BWe know not yet what is causing this mayhem. The high council has ordered us to keep this matter private so as to not bring shame to our order. But we cannot keep up this charade forever. The city is being overrun as we speak!$B$BArchmage Modera has dispatched me to solicit outside aid. Seek her image out near Dalaran beside Lordamere Lake.",
[92433]="Hey! I'm pretty busy trying to turn these scraps into something edible. You wanna help out? I could really use some more variety for this meal! It sure would be nice to have something different on the menu.$B$BThere's a goblin in Everlook who has this recipe for Savory Stag Sliders... perfect for tiny hands like mine. If you could cook up some of those, that would be great! You can get stag meat from the stags here on the mountain.",
[92434]="Whatever caused Dalaran's barrier to lower has left the city in turmoil. With you having dealt with their patrols, there is no better time than now to make our way inside and discover their secrets.$B$BTake the key you found at the internment camp and seek out their sewers along the northern border of the city. With luck, those mages had no reason to put a ward over such a... disagreeable point of entry.",
[92446]="South of here, among da forests where I sometimes hunt, dere is a great and cunning bear. We call him Head Scratcher, as his paws have caught more dan one unsuspecting villager. He ambushes hunters who are returning with prey, striking da heads by surprise and knocking dem unconscious, then stealing da catch and running back into da forest.$B$BHe is wise to me, he knows dat I track him. But he may not know your scent yet.$B$BTake dis carcass and lure him out. Finish him and bring back his claws.",
[92449]="Ever since we escaped the war we have struggled to secure our safety, surrounded by foes on all sides, beset by constant danger.$B$BOur old holdout to the east is overrun with undead. These scourge meander mindlessly--a sad but dangerous remnant. Without the guidance of their commanders, they are lost... but still deadly.$B$BThough we've tried, we have yet to succeed in eliminating their presence. At the very least, with your help, we can push them back to secure our safety... for now.",
[92454]="Welcome to the World of Warcraft!$B$BAs special thanks for purchasing the World of Warcraft Collector's Edition, turn in this gift voucher to Dalia Windbreeze in Thendal Grove. You'll then be given a gift: a little companion to join you on your quest for adventure and glory.$B$BThanks again, and enjoy your stay in the World of Warcraft!",
[92459]="The council will not be happy to learn of our subterfuge, but they cannot deny results. The city is calming down, and we are free to lower our wards.$B$BI think it's only fair you deliver the good word. Take this mote to Archmage Celindra within the Violet Citadel.",
[92460]="Look at you, bright eyed and ready for adventure! We need all the help we can get here in Thendal Village and your arrival is most welcome. I imagine you are brimming with nerves for what is to come. After all, you only get to come of age once in a lifetime.$B$BGo, seek out our village leader Rorian the Dayseeker at the entrance to the greatfather tree just west of here. He will get you started on your journey.",
[92463]="If the forest is as thick with these insects as it sounds, simply killing the workers won't be enough.$B$BGo deeper into the forest and find the queen. She'll be close to the hive and surrounded by bigger and more aggressive soldiers, so be careful.$B$BPut her down and return here when it's done. That'll be one less problem to think about around here.",
[92466]="While we owe much of our prosperity to the elements of wind, the path we walk requires that we obey the call of all four of the primary elements and undertake a trial for each. Before you begin your first trial in earnest however, you must prove the strength of your resolve.$B$BTravel to the standing stones to the east. A force of Al'Aketh converts has been spotted there and they must be driven off. Confront the cultists there and bring me one of their signets as proof of your deeds.",
[92467]="A sapta is a drink created to bind our spirits to the elements. Fused with magic, the potion will allow the strong willed to see the elements as no one else can. Your spirit will be connected to the element the sapta was created for, and only a select few shaman know the recipe.$B$BThe sapta is always drunk in a sacred place, and never anywhere else--remember that.$B$BSeek out the Rise of Spirits up the pass east of here. Drink your sapta there, and... well, you will see what you need to see.",
[92468]="Take this Rough Quartz from me and bring it to the one you call Windshaper Boro as proof of our meeting. He will craft a totem for you, and this shard will be the heart of it. As small as it may seem, you will come to find that size does not matter, and that even the smallest of things can outlast many others.$B$BBe patient, $n. Remain strong. And seek wisdom. This is what the elements ask of you. In the end, you shall become one with the earth--respect it as it shall respect you.",
[92469]="You've done enough here, $c. I'll stay and clean up any stragglers down there.$B$BHead back to the Village and tell Rorian about the cult's presence. He will not be pleased.",
[92470]="Rorian informed you that I've been watching you. I now offer you a test of resolve. However, be warned--it will send you into great danger.$B$BGo to the caves to the west. Thin out the ursera's numbers there, and find their matriarch, one the rangers call \"Urs'anah\". Put her down and bring me proof of her demise. Once you have done that, you will have taken an important step on your path.",
[92471]="You may not realize this but everything you've done has been a trial of sorts. A test for what is to come for you. It's a big island out there, and Zephras needs spirited young adventurers such as yourself if we are to survive the trials our people face.$B$BThe one called Aetheen of the Gales is one of the leaders of our people here on Zephras Isle, and she has been watching you. She has a task that you must complete. Speak with her to learn more.",
[92472]="One of the most pervasive threats on Zephras Isle is the Al'Aketh Cult. They are religious zealots devoted to the worship of the supposed elemental ruler of Skywall, Al'Akir the Windlord. They are brutal, single-minded, and their power and ambitions are growing more deadly by the day.$B$BYour path will soon take you to Shen'dar Village to the south. Present yourself to Constable Aonda when you arrive. The cult threatens Shen'dar and they are in need of aid. Tell Aonda that I sent you.",
[92473]="The ursera den to the southwest is rapidly becoming a problem. Just last week the rangers had to kill an adolescent ursera who wandered too close to the village and attempted to attack a boy playing near the base of the elder tree in the center of the village.$B$BWe were fortunate that the boy escaped with his life. Hunger and desperation makes these beasts too dangerous to be left unchecked. Go south and put the scrawniest among the ursera down. Bring me their claws as proof when it is done.",
[92479]="I was asked to bring this to your attention as soon as you returned from the kobold camps, $n. It appears to be a letter sealed with the mark of Tordrin Stemblade, our local hunter trainer. Take a moment to read it before you go about any other business here in the Abbey.",
[92481]="While you were away dealing with our vuldren problem, our resident mage trainer--Dorii Brightwhisper--left this recall crystal for you. It contains some sort of message for you, so give it a look. Afterwards, you can find Dorii in the structure just behind me.",
[92482]="While you were away dealing with our vuldren problem, our resident hunter trainer--Tai'ree Farsight--left this note for you. You can find her just over yonder near the center of the village. Read the note then seek her out.",
[92483]="While you were away dealing with our vuldren problem, our resident rogue trainer--Akeri Duskblade--has requested to speak with you. He left this note, so read that first, then seek him out inside the watchtower, here in the village.$B$BHe's a shady fellow, but then again, so are you. I think you'll get along well.",
[92484]="While you were away dealing with our vuldren problem, our resident Shaman trainer--Windshaper Boro--left this recall crystal for you. Please examine it, then speak with Boro just over yonder near the center of the village.",
[92485]="While you were away dealing with our vuldren problem, our resident druid trainer--Xyton Silverwind--left this note for you. Read it as soon as you can, and then seek out Silverwind on the ground floor of this great tree just behind me.$B$BHeed his words and his counsel, he can teach you much.",
[92500]="Since the shrine of Aviana has fallen into disrepair, the Wormwing harpies have snuck in and stolen the last of our druidic relics. One of these, the Jewel of the Horizon, is a sparkling blue stone blessed by the feathered goddess herself. The touch of Aviana may have just the magical power that you need for your task.$B$BThe Wormwings have doubtless hidden it in or near one of their nests. When you find it, take it to Ketharas.",
[92514]="You've got that \"Windshaper\" air about you. Something about how I can feel a tiny bit of static on my skin when near someone spirit-touched that gives it away. Before I properly put you to work around here, you should check in with our resident Windshaper elder, Illaya Amberwind. She's just outside, near the center of town.$B$BOh, and check in with Coriella Calmbreeze as well, she runs the local inn and can provide lodging and supplies, should you need them.",
[92515]="As if bandits and mad cultists weren't enough, the hills are thick with prideclaws as well right now. They are starting to encroach on the village borders and growing bolder by the day. It's only a matter of time before someone's pet or child is taken. It would be a mercy for us to cull their numbers now rather than after some tragedy occurs.$B$BBring me a dozen or so of their pelts. I can turn them into all sorts of goods that will be of aid to the village.",
[92516]="A flock of Hippogryph have recently established nesting grounds southeast of Shen'dar Village and they've been wreaking havoc on travelers on the road. I need someone to head down there and thin them out for us.",
[92517]="There's a cave not far to the north, hidden behind a waterfall. It's well known to me that there's a group of bandits that are operating out of that cave. They were a problem for us before the cult arrived, but now they are a real terror. I can't spare the people to go and clear them out, unfortunately.$B$BI need you to go there and take care of them for me. Kill as many as you can, and if possible, take out their leader, the one they call \"Badwind\" Bennic. That cave is dangerous, so be careful.",
[92519]="Apothecary Jorell was supposed to bring us a case of antidotes and elixirs days ago, but we're still empty handed. That fool has probably poisoned himself again by brewing in that poorly-ventilated shack he calls his lab.$B$BIf you want to further help our ward, you would be a far more reliable individual for this job.$B$BFollow the road to Go'shek farm, south and a bit west of here. You'll likely find it packed and ready to go, with Jorell either missing or unconcerned with his obligations.",
[92521]="You know I'm a warlock, right? Now reduced to squalor and meat-cutting, but once a mighty magician!$B$BMy imp keeps wandering off and while I could just call him back, I'm kinda curious about what he's doing. He's been sneaking off to talk to a bound satyr at a tower to the southeast of here. If you wouldn't mind, I'd like to know what they're talking about.$B$BI'm sure it's nothing to worry about, but you can never tell with demons, right?",
[92528]="The faithful of Al'Akir grow ever stronger with each eager new recruit like yourself. As you can see, our strength gives form to the storm itself!$B$BNormally I'd send you straight to Skypriest Aanders for assessment, but he is occupied at present receiving a guest at the inn on the north side of town. Please avoid that place for now. An unshaven recruit like yourself in the presence of such a guest would be inappropriate.$B$BFor now, just don't get in anyone's way.",
[92529]="It gladdens my heart that you wish to serve Al'Akir. Our current trials as a people stem from our own complacency. We grew prideful and took the bounty of the winds for granted. The stagnation that followed is the reason the spirits of the wind abandoned us.$B$BOnly through acts of contrition may we feel the wind's caress once more. If you seek the fellowship of like-minded shen'dorei, go to Falaath Village and find Missionary Jasaan there. I will mark you so that the faithful will know you as a recruit.",
[92532]="While you were gone our warrior trainer--Blademaster Ren--requested that we send you their way when you returned. She dropped this note off for you as well.$B$BGive it a read, then find Blademaster Ren inside the village watchtower.",
[92533]="I have worked iron my whole life, and I can feel when a weapon has twisted away from its purpose. The Blackthorne cult forges tools meant to wound the land as much as flesh. Slay their cultists and bring me what they carry: one of their staves, and a ritual dagger.$B$BThey do not merely kill with their blades, they are poisoning them with intent.$B$BBy studying the marks left by their corruption, we can learn how their influence spreads. Perhaps, we will learn how to stop or even reverse it.",
[92550]="Our best defense here might just be a strong offense. The advantage we now have is that we expect an attack is coming. What they won't expect is for us to hit them first.$B$BI've already asked a lot of you, but please head back over to Falaath Village. Kill as many cultists as you can and if you can get close enough, kill the commander and bring me his head. I'll stay here and organize the citizens and our few peacekeepers to prepare a defense... just in case you don't return.",
[92551]="I overheard you might be going to Falaath Village? While you are there, please keep an eye out for our stolen supply caches.$B$BThe Al'Aketh have been raiding our supply caravans carrying various goods such as food and windstones to and from the lowlands for months. They've been blaming the bandits, of course, but we all know that it all ends up in the same place. If there's any of that stuff left in Falaath, it would be a huge help if you could recover it.",
[92553]="Up for a bit of work? I could use a bit of muscle from a strong adventuring-type such as yourself. With how dangerous things are getting around here, no one's had much time to hunt or forage of late, and I need someone to get out there and source me fresh eggs and strider meat to keep this village fed.$B$BI'd be happy to teach you one of my famous recipes if you can bring me what I need. What do you say?",
[92579]="For now it seems the pylon and the village are safe, so I'd like you to deliver this report to Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar, at the southeastern edge of the island. Valennia is the leader of the peacekeepers on the island and she needs to know what happened here.$B$BThe cult is expanding rapidly and the peacekeepers have avoided direct conflict until now, but those days are over. Valanaar will need to be ready for a fight.$B$BAt any rate, thank you. You'll always have friends in Shen'dar, $n.",
[92591]="We've tried to escape the mountain, but our attempts have always been thwarted by the Scourge. A powerful lich reanimates the remains of those we destroy and sends them against us again. So long as that lich endures, we'll never be safe.$B$BThe lich has a pile of bones from which it rebuilds skeletons. Take this torch and set fire to the bone pile in the ruins. The lich will be sure to respond.$B$BBring me its amulet, so that we may destroy it and be rid of the lich for good.",
[92592]="We've tried to get off da mountain, but da Scourge always stop us. A powerful lich reanimates da remains of da ones we destroy and sends dem against us again. Dat lich is da reason we can't win!$B$BDa lich has a pile of bones dat it uses to rebuild skeletons. Take dis torch, go to da ruins, and burn da bone pile. Da lich be sure to respond.$B$BBring me its amulet, and we destroy it and get rid of it for good!",
[92593]="Well, you've shown you're capable enough to handle the busy work. Now we can see if you can be trusted to handle greater threats.$B$BSetting up an intelligence station here is only step one of the job. If you want to help lay the foundations for what's to come, carefully enter Dae'gun, the remains of the Horde base.$B$BFind a high point suitable for an outlook's post. Report back with details about the area, and we'll see about getting you properly briefed.",
[92594]="While you're traveling around the mountain, I can't resist asking for another small favor...$B$BDid you see all those fel shrubberies and plants littering the hills down below? It turns out they burn rather well, which is both good, and bad. Handy for feeding into a small furnace, but also a risk when it twists together and binds up gears...or bootstraps!$B$BThin their numbers on your way down, and I'll pick up the weeds myself once they've dried out.",
[92595]="<Illaya smiles warmly at you.>$B$BI am glad you returned to speak with me, child of the winds. I knew it the first moment you walked into my presence, that you were strong in the skysight. Do you find this surprising? Even those who have not trained as a Shaman may possess the gift.$B$BCome, let us speak about the mandate of the Windshapers, the nature of our struggles on Zephras, and the plight of our people.",
[92597]="Here in the elemental plane, we derive much of our arcane strength from leylines that still run through the ground under our feet. Of late, these leylines have begun to pierce the surface, giving us more direct and powerful access to these latent arcane energies.$B$BGo to the standing stones to the northeast. There is a leyline there. Tap into your birthright and draw in its energy.",
[92598]="As a Windshaper, you have the ability to use the sacred skysight gifted to us by the elemental spirits. Travel to the standing stones to the northeast of the village. Find the elemental convergence there and use your gift.$B$BYou'll find that you may draw upon the skysight anywhere, but its boon is much more powerful if you do so in the presence of an elemental convergence. You may at times receive other bits of wisdom from the spirits that are drawn to such places of power, as well.",
[92609]="We been tryin' ta leave many a time, but keep gettin' pulled back ta defend our brothas an' sistas. Wit our defenses dwindlin', it's time we get ta restockin'.$B$BToday we be needin' arrows. Lots an' lots o' dem.$B$BFind dem big, beautiful birds and bring us back dem long feathers for da straight shootin' arrows.",
[92612]="<Ketharas takes the branch and studies it. He begins to whisper a druidic incantation and the branch begins to glow brighter. The sickly green crystal begins to react as well, seeming to draw in the light surrounding it.>$B$BThe secrets this branch holds are regrettably beyond my ability to discern. But I do sense... something.$B$BTake the branch and go to town of Nighthaven in Moonglade. Ask Dendrite Starblaze for assistance.",
[92640]="Since engaging the cult in the open is not viable, our best chance is going to be to use this opportunity to attack the shrine itself. We can take Lorthuna herself off the board before she can finish her part of this scheme.$B$BIt so happens that Valennia has been preparing a strategy for a potential assault on the Shrine for some time now. The only problem is, we will need help.$B$BSpeak with Valennia for the details.",
[92642]="Valennia only sent one person to help repel a full-scale assault... by the winds.$B$BYou don't look like much but I'll take what I can get. We need to inflict as much damage as possible to stop this soon. My people can't hold out much longer.$B$BGo down the hill and disrupt their logistics. Their healers are keeping the attackers coming, if we take them out we might be able to rally and push them back. Any other cultists you kill while you are out there are helpful as well.",
[92643]="There is a turncoat amongst the Al'Aketh. They claim to know the cult's true intentions for the island and want to come in, but will only do so with assurances of protection.$B$BThis defector is hiding at a secluded residence just northwest of Valanaar inside the highlands. I need someone who can discreetly go there, find the traitor, and escort him back to us. This might be a trap, but if this information is as important as this traitor claims, it's worth some risk.",
[92644]="<You reach beneath the still-warm body of the turncoat cultist and recover a small, glowing blue crystal. It appears to be damaged, but it may still be important. High Elder Shadowsong may be interested in this.>",
[92645]="This attack is going to be hard to repel unless we can take out the cult commander. Belguilos \"the Breaker\" they call her, and she's a veritable terror. She used to be a peacekeeper before the cult got out of control, and even then she was... off. As a cultist I can only imagine how much worse she could be now.$B$BI might just be sending you to your death, but someone needs to take Belguilos out if we are going to survive here. You can find her at the villa at the hill's base. Good luck, $c.",
[92646]="Lorthuna fled up to the spires above using some sort of portal. Ayessa and Elaadrin went in after her. That was just a few moments ago.$B$BI'm afraid I took one too many hits and this is where I stay. Go through the portal, find Ayessa and help them stop Lorthuna.$B$BUnless that help that Elaadrin and Ayessa said they sent for arrives soon, you are on your own from here. Good luck, $c.",
[92679]="H--Hello, stranger. You have the look of a capable adventurer about you. I...$B$B<The Skyborne man winces, clearly suffering terrible pain>$B$B...I was wondering if you were seeking employment? I came here to Valanaar to recruit fighters to help save my farm. If you are interested, please go find my wife Aamelia Windfield at our orchard to the west of Valanaar, in the lowlands.",
[92682]="Oh, so you've got more courage than sense, then? Fine, I won't argue.$B$BFerauu and his goons aren't due to pick up their take of the harvest just yet, so I'm going to put you to work for your meals until they arrive.$B$BHead outside and gather today's batch of stormapples for me. Oh, and the bandits lurking around the stormapple trees... They think they are sneaky. They aren't. Kill them for me.$B$BLet's see what you've got in a fight.",
[92683]="I'm sure you've noticed the giant flutterflies out in the outer fields near the orchard? They are pleasant to look at, but they also have other benefits; namely their wing dust. It can be a mess, but if you can gather it up in large amounts, it has useful household applications.$B$BTake this Flutterfly Swatter and give the big bugs a good swat for me. They'll usually just get scared and flee, but sometimes they'll take some offense. Either way, they'll give their rumps a shake and drop a pile of dust.",
[92684]="As if the harvest wasn't light enough this year already, the galestriders in the area have been getting into the orchard and stealing my stormapples. Think you can head out to the fields and cull them for me?$B$BTake care though stranger, these lowlands galestriders are bigger and angrier than the highlands variety. Watch yourself. A well-timed kick is all it takes to put you down for good if you aren't paying attention.$B$BBring me some of their meat and I can make us a hot meal with it as well.",
[92685]="The bandits have camps all over and there's a small one in the hills just north of here. Head up there and start cracking skulls. If we can catch them off guard and take them out before they come for us, we might just even the odds enough to stand a chance.$B$BBring me their masks. The bloodier the better.",
[92693]="You've done a lot to give us a fighting chance. Even if we die today, we'll at least know we gave it our best shot.$B$BThis is your last chance, stranger. If you want to head back to Valanaar and live another day, I wouldn't blame you.$B$BOn the other hand, if you really have a thing for lost causes just let me know when you are ready to go. We'll walk out there with our heads held high and whatever happens, happens.",
[92698]="<You lean in close to try and hear the words coming from beneath the giant construct's armor plates.>$B$B...Function error...$B$B...Question...$B$B...What is....$B$B...Function...$B$B<These fragmented words and phrases seem to just repeat. Maybe someone nearby knows more about this construct?>",
[92699]="Now that you've arrived in Valanaar, you'll likely want to check in with the other members of the High Order here. The current Supreme Magister, Elaadrin Evengale and his people operate out of the lodge on the far southeastern part of Valanaar.$B$BYou should also take care, the High Order and Windshapers don't get along very well here. Be careful and give the Windshapers a good, wide berth. We've got enough to worry about with the cult, I won't tolerate faction violence in the streets of Valanaar.",
[92700]="Now that you've arrived in Valanaar, you'll likely want to check in with the other members of the Windshapers here. The current Grand Skyseer and her people operate out of the lodge near the center of Valanaar.$B$BYou should also be aware, the Windshapers and High Order don't get along very well in these parts. Be careful and give the High Order a good, wide berth. We've got enough to worry about with the cult, I won't tolerate faction violence in the streets of Valanaar.",
[92701]="For now it seems the pylon and the village are safe, so I'd like you to deliver this report to Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar, at the southeastern edge of the island. Valennia is the leader of the peacekeepers on the island and she needs to know what happened here.$B$BThe cult is expanding rapidly and the peacekeepers have avoided direct conflict until now, but those days are over. Valanaar will need to be ready for a fight.$B$BAt any rate, thank you. You'll always have friends in Shen'dar, $n.",
[92702]="<Fenwick struggles to rock back and forth and gain some swaying motion.>$B$BHey! Hey you! Grab a stick and see if you can reach me, please? I've been stuck here so long my suspenders are chafing! I've got good things--GREAT things--to share with you! Fenwick Togglespring never gives false promises!$B$BIt's my rusty brother back at the launch pad who clearly miscalculated a few things in our rocket launch capabilities! He's mister false promises!$B$B<Fenwick fails to grab an object out of reach.>",
[92703]="I guess it doesn't feel quite right to keep calling you stranger after all of this so... thank you, $n.$B$BIf you wouldn't mind and are back out that way, please let Alvarion know what happened here. Also, tell him that once he's up on his feet he needs to bring a windshaper back here to look at that construct for us to make sure it's safe to have around our... our family.$B$B<Aamelia touches her belly gently.>$B$BHe doesn't know about this part. Let's just keep that bit between us for now.",
[92706]="Calling all anglers!$B$BA giant shark has been circling the waters near the shipping dock, attacking sailors and small boats. Dockworkers have given it the nickname \"Bruuz\". A hefty reward will be given to whoever brings me its fin!$B$B-- Gazlowe",
[92707]="Wrenched from its hulking corpse, the goliath's bracers are massive. Your whole arm, up to the shoulder, can fit through one without touching the sides.$B$BYou should bring these back to Hammerfall, as a warning. Drum Fel ought to know what he's up against.",
[92708]="The Windshapers have been hard at work trying to respond to the current crisis on Zephras Isle. We have made several surprising discoveries in our search for the missing wind spirits, and we are developing a plan of action that could help us gain the means to save the island.$B$BWe'll need strong young adventurers like yourself for this to work however. Please, if you have a moment, let us speak on this further.",
[92709]="Your highborne lineage shines as clearly in your eyes as the sky above. You are one of us, and it's youths like yourself that will help us save our home. But first, let me tell you more of our mission and plans here on Zephras... and beyond.",
[92727]="Seeking knowledge is the primary mandate of the High Order, but this work has never been more dangerous than it is now on Zephras.$B$BOne of our scholars--Fillion Flamebreeze--was en route to the Shen'dar Highlands to gather data on the windborne magic that congregates in some areas there. Regrettably, he has not returned and we fear that something may have befallen him on the road.$B$BIf you can, please locate him for us. He was last seen on the road leading west from Valanaar towards Shen'dar Highlands.",
[92741]="The Shadowgale Forest is incredibly dangerous and is usually off limits to normal adventurers. In recent months there's been an explosion in the shriekling population and they've started to expand their territory outside the woods, which is a potential problem. I have an interest in the alchemical properties of shriekling talons, so a much-needed culling also presents an opportunity for scholarly gain.$B$BTravel to Shadowgale Forest and hunt the beasts. Bring me as many of their talons as you can.",
[92754]="Our clanmates continue to venture further south, to and beyond the cursed Valley of Bones.$B$BDespite your standing with our clan, I do not trust you enough to share the details of their ventures. They would be boring to you anyway, outsider.$B$BWhat matters to you is our need for Greater Shadow Protection Potions, in bulk, to ensure their continued survival. Bring some to me, and I will put in a good word for you.",
[92755]="With each passing day, our scavengers return with fewer and fewer armaments from fallen adventurers.$B$BWhile we cannot use these pieces directly, we do salvage them for scraps. The most magical of the armaments go to me, as I can disenchant them and make use of the mysterious remnants to enchant our weapons, particularly those of our windchasers.$B$BI am in need of Greater Mystic Essences if I am to supply our next raiding party with worthwhile equipment.",
[92814]="My mate, Halea, is tasked with ensuring our armaments are empowered with appropriate magical energy.$B$BThe whole concept of enchanting is far beyond my understanding, but as the centaur whose job is to keep our village well supplied and equipped, I know that Halea is often behind on her duties--to no fault of her own.$B$BI would like to gift her some simple clothes to practice her craft on. I see some adventurers wandering through sandstorms with simple facemasks. Could you get me a few of those?",
[92817]="Convincing my Gelkis clanmates to put on armor is nigh impossible, despite the numerous losses we have suffered with blades or bolts through the chest.$B$BI have been tasked with designing a vest that offers some reasonable protection, without the supposed 'itchiness' that they complain about. Supplies are scarce, so I dare not waste precious leather on junk.$B$BOutsider, would you bring me a harness fit to a brutish centaur? I would like to learn from your technique.",
[92818]="WE NEED MORE WEAPONS.$B$BMORE. WEAPONS.$B$BHOW ELSE IS THE MAGRAM GOING TO SMASH PUNY GELKIS?$B$BI WANT TO SEE WHAT YOU CAN MAKE, OUTSIDER. BRING ME AXES. BIG, NO, MASSIVE ONES.$B$BHURRY UP.",
[92833]="Ve'han now claims the Nordrassil Lodge, under the boughs of the great tree, as his lair. It is time for us to put this magic to the ultimate test.$B$BTake the staff and bring it to bear against Ve'han. Dispel the magic protecting him and bring him to justice!",
[92834]="When the cult began their campaign of violence, the Peacekeepers and Windshapers responded with posturing. I saw this as foolish escalation so I advocated for peaceful dialogue. Yesterday I dispatched my friend Belathaan Brightwish to the Shrine of Akir, hoping to establish that dialogue.$B$BA box just arrived containing Belathaan's tongue, dipped in silver pigment.$B$BIt's clear to me now that there is no reasoning with the cult. Kill any cultists you see, and bring me the prayer charms that they carry.",
[92840]="Fillion was sent to the Overlook Standing Stones with a special device used to measure and study the elemental energy there.$B$BTake this--an Index Esoteria--and use it to extract data from the massive windstone formations that form there. Be on your guard however, as the Windshapers are likely to be jealously guarding this site now.$B$BShould any attempt to obstruct you, well... do what you need to do. I have no more patience for their interference.",
[92841]="It is time, outsider, for you to learn of our great discovery... but Warug will not be the one to tell it!$B$BHead south to the other end of the village. Look for a big, stinky centaur named Orgrul.$B$BYou will know when you get there.$BYou will know when you see him.$BIf he thinks you deserve to know, you will know.$B$BAnd if he doesn't? Well. You can be happy knowing Warug has a new crown.",
[92842]="I have a cousin who, some time ago, mentioned a plan to visit Mount Hyjal and see what has been happening there. Foolishly.$B$BHyjal is a world away; it could take months for mail to reach him, if he can even find a mailbox.$B$BIn the unlikely event that you find yourself on that side of the world, I would appreciate someone looking in on my fool of a cousin.",
[92844]="Some sort of necromantic energy has permeated throughout the Valley of Bones, for reasons we have yet to understand.$B$BThose reasons are also of no importance to us. The magic is ours now, and those who do not fight with blade or mallet are trained in this new magic.$B$BIf you think I intend to start you off with a challenging task, think again. For now, go into the Valley of Bones and fetch some bones for me. I am sure you can handle that.",
[92846]="Have you noticed the puny centaur stomping about around here? Those are of Gelkis descent.$B$BWe Magram have already established a foothold deeper into the canyon. When the Gelkis took notice of our presence here, some among them chose to follow in our footsteps. I know not whether they wish to join us or attempt to overthrow us, but I do know that their clanmates have sentenced them all to exile.$B$BThey're lone wolves meddling in powers that do not belong to them. I want them dead.",
[92847]="Outsider, did you notice the weapon that the outcast necromancers held in their hands? We will ensure the Gelkis will not live long enough to master the ways of necromancy, but their methods of channeling caught my interest. They even use those same crystals Warug asked you to steal.$B$BI think we can use this technique to our advantage. Venture back into the valley to recover some wood from the accursed trees, and see if Warug will part with some of his crystals. I will make staves from them.",
[92849]="<Judging by what you've just found, it's very likely that Fillion befell some misfortune here. He may still be nearby, and he might be in need of aid. You notice a cave just to the north of your current location. You should continue searching for him there.>",
[92850]="I am feeling much better already. I have some skill with the arcane arts and we are but a short distance from Valanaar. I can make it on my own. More important than my safety, however, is how close to Valanaar these shrieklings have nested and the danger they pose. If you would be so kind, please head back inside and take the head of that beast!$B$BAfter it's done, you'll find me back in Valanaar. I need to report to the Supreme Magister what occurred here and the status of my mission.",
[92858]="By order of General Feathermoon:$B$BA bounty is being offered to whoever slays the ogre known as Ohk'zi. While not as pressing a threat as the naga, the Gordunni ogres are a similar menace to the lands of Feralas.$B$BOhk'zi was last seen at the Gordunni outpost east of here. The reward will be given upon proof of his death.$B$B-- Latronicus Moonspear",
[92859]="Folks have been trying to get onto Mount Hyjal since the end of the war, but there's one big problem... all the demons in Darkwhisper Gorge!$B$BI think I have the solution. A concoction made from locally-sourced ingredients might be able to make the drinker blend in with the Winterspring surroundings so that creatures here can't see you as easily.$B$BI'd love to test this theory, if you're game for bringing me a few small things!",
[92860]="The High Order have done our best to avoid direct conflict with the cult, but that is clearly no longer an option. Their hostility has been clearly demonstrated, and now there are rumors of larger-scale cult movements around the island. They are clearly gearing up for something and whatever it is can't be good for the people of Zephras.$B$BReport to Valennia Stormfist and inform her that the High Order offers our full support in Valanaar's efforts against the Al'Aketh, should the need arise.",
[92867]="Our heritage may be crumbling, but this is not our final redoubt. We have more in reserve, and it must remain hidden for its own protection.$B$BSupport grows for preserving our remaining sculptures and sacred burial grounds. The rabble that have taken up residence in our old kingdom have no notion of the vengeance coming for them.$B$BDrive back the Boulderfist and Syndicate. They must learn Stromgarde is not merely fist, eagle, and stones.",
[92871]="Valennia Stormfist and her peacekeepers have ever been the protectors of Zephras, and we've done our best to lend aid where we can. There are rumors of larger-scale cult movements around the island, and they are clearly gearing up for something.$B$BReport to Valennia and reiterate to her that the Windshapers offer their full support in Valanaar's efforts against the Al'Aketh, should the need arise.",
[92872]="We eternally guard this tomb and the knowledge of ceremonial rites used to honor these fallen souls.$B$BNow that you've descended three levels below the earth, you take your first steps toward returning to the sunlit world with sacred wisdom.$B$BEach season, we carry some of the dust from this tomb and spread it to the oceans of Azeroth. A symbolic act of renewing cycles.$B$BTake this small satchel. Travel to the cliffs behind Stromgarde Keep and cast it into the sea.",
[92873]="We already know these crystals are capable of more than sundering the ground--the Gelkis have proven that they can be twisted for necromantic power. Do you remember the bones I had you collect? I assembled them as best I could just up the hill. There was enough for two workable skeletons.$B$B<Orgrul hands you a newly made staff.>$B$BI will deliver the Necrokhan's staff while you play with your new toy. Return only once you can prove that you know how to use it.",
[92878]="<The forsaken points to his missing lower jaw. He then hands you a piece of paper with a hastily scrawled message.>$B$BCan't talk. Lost jaw in fight. Attacked by Grimtotems. Led by a druid. Namida. Camp to northwest.$B$BShe must pay.$B$B<The last sentence is underlined twice.>",
[92880]="I suspect it will take a bit of time for us to mop up what's left of the attackers, but our chances are far better now. Head back to Valanaar and let them know that we are stable here now.$B$BI can't thank you enough for your help. We'd be in much worse shape without you. I asked for reinforcements and it seems that I got a burgeoning hero instead. I'll take that.$B$BMay the four winds bless you, $c.",
[92881]="The attacks on both the western and eastern watchtowers are not a coincidence. Based on what you told us about what occurred at the western watchtower with that skypriest, our best guess is that the cult is trying to do something to the anchor pylons.$B$BPlease speak with High Elder Shadowsong. He will tell you about a lead that could prove to be promising.",
[92893]="As you tread further into the Valley of Bones, you will find Gelkis wanderers that dared to enter our territory. I instructed they be kept alive so they could feed the bone worms burrowing about, but they seem uninterested in their prey being alive.$B$BThis task is simple. Find the prisoners, then snuff out their life. Don't give them a brief glimmer of hope for freedom.",
[92894]="I can see the excitement in your eyes, outsider. Do you grasp the potential of necromancy yet?$B$BOf course you do. And that is why I am ordering you to hone your skills further.$B$BAs you venture deeper into the Valley of Bones, you will see the remains of failed attempts at raising the dead. Gelkis attempts, no doubt. Hardly able to claw out from the dirt. Funny, were it not so pathetic.$B$BI have imbued your staff with greater power. Use this to grow our army, and crush the ones that fight back!",
[92909]="Oh no... I'm in for it now!$B$BI heard about the harvesters terrorizing the fields of Westfall, so I traveled all the way from Ironforge to see if I could recalibrate them. But they're far more aggressive than my calculations anticipated, and they chased me into this stable!$B$BIf I had some isosprings and gyrostabilizers from the harvesters, I could build a device to cover my escape. Could you gather the parts for me?",
[92914]="<You approach the strange crystal, guarded mere moments ago by emaciated mana elementals.$B$BIts pedestal, though ancient, is noticeably less dilapidated than the elven ruins it is built upon.$B$BA weak hum of power radiates from the fractured gemstone, but with its magic so heavily depleted its purpose will ultimately remain a mystery for the time being.$B$BPerhaps there is more to discover nearby.>",
[92947]="Everyone is here, good. I've just sent a few of my best fighters in through the front of the shrine to cause a bit of trouble and serve as a distraction, while I lead the the bulk of our forces in from the flank.$B$BIf all goes well, we should be able to punch through quickly and take out the High Priestess. As for you, get in there and start cracking skulls. Meet my second, Hyusaa Quickbreeze, near the steps to the shrine after you've caused some trouble.$B$BWinds guide you, $c.",
[92959]="This corruption... seeps into my limbs, my roots. I am not the only one. Other ancients... have felt this corruption as well.$B$BOne of my oldest friends... Sunderbark... the corruption has broken him, made him a creature of rage and pain. It is... too late to save him, now.$B$BGo to the corrupted pool to the east... strike the corrupted tree and he will come.$B$BTake this seed... and plant it in his remains when the deed is done. With care... something good can still grow from this sorrow.",
[92960]="A lingering demon presence remains to the east. Among them are the hellish beasts responsible for ravaging our kin, siphoning their power to use it against our allies.$B$BPenetrate their camp, locate these beasts and slay them. Retrieve any samples that remain.$B$BPerhaps there is something we can learn from these efforts.",
[93016]="You will have to forgive me for sending you on such a series of tasks without providing any context. I hadn't considered how suspicious this may have seemed, more so now that the skies have taken on such a dramatic appearance.$B$BI will gladly answer your questions.",
[93030]="I once was a knight like you--bound to the service of the light. Then, I died. It seems that we both have that much in common.$B$BUnlike you, however, I am bound to this place by a purpose unfinished, an oath unfulfilled. If you would listen, I would tell you of my quest... and my failure.",
[93034]="One of our scouts returned to the village while you were away, with news that confirmed my fears.$B$BThe Magram are up to something, $n. It is not good.$B$BThe Valley of Bones far to the east is a cursed land that few centaur dared to enter and fewer still ever return home. Our enemy has found something there, something evil, and we need to learn what it is.$B$BSeek out the scout Nerlokh at the southern entrance, but you may have to prove yourself further to the Gelkis.",
[93035]="You need not peer far to see the undead shambling about ahead of us, but have you noticed something unusual about them?$B$BThey walk on two legs, not four! These skeletons are not even our fallen kin. The Magram must be defiling the bodies of those who died long before the Desolace was our domain. I cannot imagine how they justified turning their backs on Mother Theradras and took to desecrating corpses that have rested here for centuries.$B$BPut the undead to rest, $n.",
[93036]="You may or may not be aware of this, but Sania Silverstream over there is a \"missionary\" for the Al'Aketh. They like to play at being a normal religious order and send non-threatening emissaries around to recruit. We've tolerated Sania so far to avoid direct conflict with the cult, but it's obvious the illusion of peace won't last much longer.$B$BYou are new here and unknown to most, so I'd like to see if you can use Sania to get close to the cult and find out what their plans are for the village.",
[93037]="While I waited for your arrival, I peered a bit further between the arches and noticed something I need you to confirm for me.$B$BI cannot bear saying it aloud. Not until my suspicions have been proven true.$B$B$n, while you are getting your bearings in the valley, slay some of the necromancers that look weaker than the others. Tear off their ritual garb, carefully, and bring it to me. I must know whether I am of clear mind and vision.",
[93041]="This discovery is devastating for our clan, but it is in our best interest to keep this only to those who need to know. Uthek is one such person who needs to be aware of what is going on here. I suspect she will know how to proceed.$B$BTake this to show her. For good measure, we should also bring evidence of the necromancy itself to her. Find a skull that looks recently cursed. I suspect they may be hoarding them in the maws of one of the goliath's skeletons.",
[93044]="When you return to Nerlokh in the Valley of Bones, it will not be empty-handed.$B$BGo inside the cave at the heart of our village and seek out Mulara. Ask for Tears of Theradras on my behalf. Our supply is low, but it is our best hope against the Magram's foul necromancy!$B$BI will prepare a ritual. We will create a weapon to disrupt their spells.",
[93058]="There was a brief battle between a few of the necromancers just around the hill, and I used that to take a closer look inside.$B$B$n, not all of our recent losses were defectors. There are Gelkis being held captive further in the valley! I was not able to investigate their situation because a hulking Magram brute started charging my direction. I consider myself fortunate he lost interest quickly.$B$BYou must go back into the Valley of Bones and free them. The Gelkis stand together.",
[93062]="About this staff of yours. I recognize it as one of Uthek's, and you mentioned it was constructed with Theradras' Tears, augmented with a Draenethyst Crystal, and that it can dispel dark magic?$B$BI noticed that there are skeletons stuck just underneath the rocky soil further into the valley. I believe these are failed summons from the Outcast Necromancers, doomed perhaps forever to an existence smothered in dirt.$B$BLaying them to rest again would be good for our cause, and their spirits.",
[93065]="The Peacekeepers are mobilizing and we are all gearing up to head out. Make whatever preparations you need to make and meet us at the eastern road leading north out of town. We'll have one final check-in with everyone before we move out.",
[93066]="On the other side of the valley, we have established a small foothold to prepare to march into the forest nearby. Before you head straight there, I want you to deal with a recent Bristleback intrusion along the way. They seem to have arrived right around the same time we did, but managed to secure an artifact from the nearby temple that has kept us at bay.$B$BThis task is simple. Look for the thorns and the pigs. Kill a bunch, indiscriminately. Then report to Hagiak at the camp I mentioned.",
[93072]="There is a second centaur village out here, to the southwest. That one belongs to the Gelkis. You expect me to send you over just to spill some blood, right? Good. That had best be your first thought, else I would cast doubt on your allegiance to the Magram!$B$BWhat are you waiting for? Go! Kill!",
[93089]="Please extend my thanks to Elaadrin for all that the High Order and your new friends from this \"Kirin Tor\" have done for Zephras Isle. I'm aware of the High Order's plans to leave the island, and your order has my blessing and well-wishes in this expedition.$B$BI can only hope that whatever arcane solution the High Order finds can truly provide us with the stability we've lacked these past years. If you plan to go with them... well, this mission will be all the stronger for it.$B$BWinds be with you, $n.",
[93090]="Please extend my thanks to Ayessa for all that the Windshapers and your new friends from this \"Earthen Ring\" have done for Zephras Isle. I'm aware of the plan to take the Windshapers' shamans and leave the island, and your order has my blessing and well-wishes in this expedition.$B$BI can only hope that whatever solution the Windshapers find can truly provide us with the stability we've lacked these past years.$B$BWinds be with you, $n.",
[93122]="We have all underestimated the power and presence of the Magram clan in this area, but this could prove an advantage.$B$BWith so many of their own distracted and their refusal to accept other clans' exiles, who is left to defend the village? What of their Khan?$B$BI need you to go into the valley, deeper than you have gone before, and look around. If the Magram are as well fortified here as they seem, they may have left themselves vulnerable at their village...",
[93125]="You! I saw you outside fighting the outcasts. I know not where you come from, but I need your help.$B$BI was lured here by my Gelkis brethren with an assurance of safety. I knew the war in the Desolace was escalating beyond our control, but I never imagined my own people turning to necromancy in a convoluted bid to defect to the Magram clan. When I spoke out against this, they threatened to kill me if I ever stepped hoof outside this tent!$B$BPlease help.",
[93127]="The Wild King may have a numbers advantage, but we can outmaneuver him with tactics.$B$BEmpower our living sentinel stones across the encircling hills, they can track Blackthorne movements for us. The northern ridges, the southern slopes, and the western high ground all have drained stones that will activate upon detecting your allied presence.$B$BTread carefully as you work, Blackthorne patrols crowd these paths, and their presence is precisely why we must bring this land under vigilant surveillance.",
[93128]="As much as I would like Uthek or Khan Shaka to give the order, I fear our window of opportunity is short. Too short to consult those at Gelkis Village.$B$BI believe with the situation unfolding here at the Valley of Bones that the Magram have left Khan Jehn with minimal defenses. If there was ever a time to attack another clan's Khan, it is now.$B$BBut $n, a Khan is not to be trifled with, least of all Jehn. If you are brave enough to make your move, you must be swift but do not underestimate him.",
[93129]="Since you seem overly eager to help our clan, I am sure you would be willing to fetch some supplies while you are over in the Outcast Hideaway.$B$BFelling our foes should be enough motivation for a Magram, but I see no reason why we could not profit from the endeavor, too.$B$BWhen we have the exiles dealt with, we can secure this place for the Magram and raise an army to bring the other clans to their knees!",
[93159]="Uh, um... h-hello, I mean to say, hi! Greetings, even! I'm sorry... it's um, been so long since I've actually spoken to another person. I'm afraid I'm a bit rusty at this.$B$B<The strange hooded figure shifts uncomfortably before you.>$B$BSo er, um... how is your day going?",
[93160]="I do appreciate you stopping by to talk with me! I-If you do want to help out, I could use a bit of help gathering up acorns from the forest floor. I've gathered most of the ones close by but there sure are a lot of raptor-bird things in the forest. It's dangerous out there and I'd rather not become a giant bird's lunch!$B$BSo if you want, you could maybe gather them for me? I'll make us something tasty if you do!",
[93163]="Built and destroyed again; the heart of Iodax the Obliterator rests in your hands. The golem was likely an invention of the dark iron dwarves, or of something before them. As such, the dwarves at Thorium Point may be interested in your discovery here.",
[93165]="The Al'Aketh have visited great tragedy upon our enclave, and blood must be repaid with blood.$B$BI have an offer for you, stranger. Should you find conflict with these accursed cultists, bring me the ears of those you kill. I will reward you for each that you return with in both coin and, in time, access to the Nightclaw's secrets should you prove yourself to be a true friend.",
[93172]="Most of the elves on this island seem to think that these woods are haunted, and they aren't wrong.$B$BAt the old ruins to the northeast, a strange type of ghost-like spirits gather. Some nights, you can almost hear them \"singing\". It's not like any song I've heard before, but it's definitely a song and it's... just so sad.$B$BI'm not sure why, but I think something terrible happened there at some point, and the spirits are trapped there somehow. If you are feeling brave, maybe you can help set them free?",
[93176]="Admiring my little menagerie, are you? They are my un-life's work. I've spent countless hours studying them: their anatomy, their diets, even their social rituals.$B$BDo you wish to join me in the hobby? Here, take this package. The notes and materials contained within should get you started. If you lose it, you'll have to purchase another one from me for a small fee.",
[93188]="You have done enough on the front lines. We can handle ourselves.$B$BTell Orgrul that you have served your purpose. The Magram Front is stronger now, and we have our sights set on the outcast encampment as our next settlement when another fleet of fighters joins the fray.$B$BWell? Get going!",
[93196]="The leader of our clan, Khan Jehn, was slain by a band of outsiders much like you. They were acting on behalf of the Gelkis Clan.$B$BYou can stop feigning your surprise. An assault on Magram Village while our attention was elsewhere is a predictable war strategy, especially for the Gelkis.$B$BDo you know why I am showing no rage or remorse, outsider?$B$B<Orgrul hands you a familiar weapon, imbued with even greater power than the last time you held it.>$B$BThis is why.",
[93197]="With all of the fighting and the retreat from the Nordrassil Lodge, we've been terribly shorthanded out here.$B$BIf you are traveling back and forth between here and Everlook, I have some mail that needs to go to the town for distribution, and we need any waiting mail brought back up. I have a stack of parcels ready for transport, if you would be so good as to help.",
[93224]="It likely comes as no surprise to you that both of the centaur clans are hesitant to accept aid from anyone outside of their clan. This is especially true for folks like you and me - you know, non-centaurs.$B$BOne thing we all have in common is an understanding that money is power, and we have learned that the local centaur barter with carved wood. If you bring me a few samples of their designs, I can put in a rush order for similar etchings. Perhaps we can buy ourselves an advantage.",
[93225]="I have noticed that centaur from different clans sometimes gather away from settlements and engage in trade. I have observed this across numerous nights and seemingly with every clan; most importantly I have seen the currency they use: carved totems.$B$BI believe we can turn the tides in our favor with either the Gelkis or the Magram if we deliver a heavy bundle of totems right to them. I have already begun carving some, but I doubt they will be easily fooled without a few authentic ones.",
[93226]="Siding with the Magram would be my choice. There is no question that they are the dominant clan in the present day, regardless of their previous struggles. I have heard reports that they are brutally hostile against the Gelkis.$B$BI sympathize with both warring clans and especially the Gelkis, but this is their war; not ours. We ought to side with the faction that poses the least risk to our cause. I believe that to be the Magram.$B$BBring this to their quartermaster in Magram Village to the southeast.",
[93227]="At first glance, I would wager that the Gelkis are struggling. Their numbers are far fewer than the Magram, and I rarely hear of them stomping around from our scouts.$B$BNonetheless, they are one of the dominant clans in the Desolace and survive to this day. They must be doing something right.$B$BIf you want to make peace with the Gelkis, take this tote of totems with you to Gelkis Village far to the southwest. Primitive as they may be, they are likely to have a treasurer of some kind.",
[93269]="Now that you've recovered all the mail, you can take it all back with you to Mount Hyjal!$B$BShould be no problem, right?",
[93317]="Are you familiar with Windsong Crawlers? You see, these crabs are native only to Windsong Lake here on Zephras, and they are only able to be harvested a few weeks of the year.$B$BWith all of the cult activity of late, I've not been able to get out to the lake to harvest them, and our window is rapidly closing. I'd be appreciative if you could go and gather some for me. They can generally be found along the shorelines around the lake and in rivers.$B$BDo be careful though, they are meaner than they look!",
[93318]="By order of Constable Aonda of the Peacekeepers, a bounty is hereby placed upon the scourge of the highlands, Vulgara the Insatiable. Last spotted on a hilltop rise just southwest of Shen'dar Village, the winged vuldren terror is highly dangerous and should be approached with caution.$B$BDeliver the beast's head to Danarii Bellowveil to receive your reward.",
[93319]="We are relying on windstones more and more for day-to-day living here on Zephras so we try and maintain a cache of them in reserve for emergencies. Lately I've noticed some go missing from our stores.$B$BWe've found windstones on bandits we've captured recently, and I suspect they are behind our shortages.$B$BIf you find yourself near the bandit cave to the north, mind knocking a few heads together and reclaiming some of our pilfered windstones for me?",
[93320]="I've just received word that the cult is attacking the pylon watchtower just outside of town! I've sent the few extra peacekeepers we have here to try and break through the enemy back line to relieve the defenders, but any additional help could mean the difference between our people there living or dying.$B$BPlease leave immediately for the east watchtower and provide whatever aid you can.$B$BMy lieutenant Yorana Windyreed led the relief force. If she still lives she can tell you how best to help.",
[93341]="As the garden's caretaker, it was my responsibility to ensure it thrived.$B$BI knew there would come a day when I could no longer maintain it, so I enchanted a necklace gifted from my daughter to transform a new generation of saplings into treants, so they could watch over the garden in my stead. I placed it on an enchanted pedestal, sheltered within a small shrine.$B$BThe garden was in great hands. I must know what happened.",
[93362]="Please spare the details of how the life may have been twisted there. My heart is broken enough with the loss of my necklace.$B$BBut while I weep, the plants suffer.$B$B$n, I would like you to go back to the garden and cull some of the angered flora. Please be swift and merciful; they can feel pain, and they have been hurt enough. If you intend to go hunting for my necklace as well, I would ask you to prioritize that before visiting the gardens again... in the unlikely chance you find it.",
[93383]="A sturdy backpack stuffed with survival equipment and radio receivers lies between prickly bushes. There's a flashing indicator light on one of the radios.$B$BYou reach for the bag and the radio strapped to the backpack buzzes to life.$B$B\"Pilot present! Gnomal Positioning System establishing uplink!$B$BConfirming contents to dispense: Aviator's Survival Kit, Three Day, One Size, Quantity One$B$BPlease stand by while security mechanism discharges safely before opening.\"",
[93394]="I suspect your curiosity is luring you toward the grand structure now, yes? Good!$B$BThe Shen'dralar there are unlikely to welcome you with open arms, but so long as you tread respectfully, I do not think you will run into any trouble.$B$BWith any luck, my old friend Kirandis might be easy to find. Of everyone, he is the most likely to be amicable to your presence.",
[93404]="I am the ancient. Towering above us. That which still burns despite many rains. I feel its flames in death. Forever burdened by my last mistake.$B$BI do not know why I am cursed to haunt this place. I do not understand why death was not the end.$B$BPlease put out the flame. Seek pristine water from a sacred ravine. Such a place exists across Mashan'she. I have heard murmurs of the place in the wind.$B$BMaraudon.",
[93406]="So you need to bring the return mail back to Mount Hyjal, eh? There's a little problem...$B$BY'see, someone came through here and ransacked the outgoing mail just a few days ago! Probably looking for money in the mail. Ran off into the hills somewhere north of here and never came back. Probably got torn apart by a yeti or something!$B$BAnyway, if you wanna bring back the mail, you're gonna have to go get it first!",
[93407]="We need to improve our defenses here, and we lack the resources to construct fortifications. We do, however, have all of the bounty of nature.$B$BSearch the forest for thorn bushes and bring their seeds back to me. With the power of nature, we will grow our own defenses.",
[93422]="The Wild King listens through shadows older than Hyjal itself. His scouts move with purpose now, stirred by the renewed advances of both Horde and Alliance in these sacred lands. The Blackthorne Pact feels the pressure of our resistance and grows more crazed each day.$B$BHunt down the Blackthorne Courier and end her trail before she carries their important information back to her master.$B$BShe moves between camps. Watch her path, and strike her down. Bring what she carries back to us.",
[93429]="Although they are our kin, the Lost Ones of Fallow Sanctuary have become beings of pure violence and hatred.$B$BThere can be no redemption or salvation for them. They are doomed to wander this swamp as mindless, hateful creatures for all their lives.$B$BTheir suffering must end. Someone must put them out of their misery. A grisly task, I know, but would you do it to protect those of us who remain?",
[93430]="Now they've really done it! As if those wretches weren't already enough to deal with, one of them has stolen my lucky lure!$B$BI was just out fishing this morning, when one came up out of the muck, cut my line, and ran off with it. The thief is almost certainly one of the Lost Ones' own fishermen, hoping to use the lure themselves.$B$BWell, our supply of fish depends on that lure, so I need it back. The Lost Ones fish along the banks east of here. Find that thief, $r!",
[93443]="<A handwritten label appears on the side of the crate. On the right side is a map with a large red circle along a southeastern shoreline north of a poorly drawn temple surrounded by water and some kind of winged creatures. On the left is a note in massive font.>$B$BPROPERTY OF FRIZ FRAZZLESPARK$B$BPOWDERFUSE PORT$B$BWARNING: NOT for tampering. Do NOT open without supervision.$B$B<An additional note appears at the bottom of the label.>$B$BIf lost, return to Friz Frazzlespark. Powderfuse Port. Riverglades.",
[93444]="The most vicious fel chimaera of Hyjal is known as Ghansurok. It likes to swoop in and prey on wildlife caught out of their burrows. Not only that, it's making hippogryph travel in and out of Hyjal more stressful than usual!$B$BFirst, hunt down one of the Nightsabers hiding in the Summit's shadows. Next, place meat from the fallen cat somewhere on the northern ridge where chimaeras feed.$B$BLure Ghansurok towards it. Slay the beast and return with its heart. Marn will study it to help heal Hyjal.",
[93450]="Being corporeal has its challenges, as you know, but being INcorporeal is a whole other situation. Will I fall through THIS chair? Will I trip over THAT cat? Worst of all, however, it makes everyday work impossible!$B$BDo you see this sword on my anvil? I began work on this thousands of years ago, but met my demise before it was finished. Now it taunts me, AND takes up precious real estate! I cannot work with it! I cannot MOVE it!$B$BI need you to help, uh, \"ferry\" it to the spirit realm. What do you say?",
[93461]="You've got that \"High Order\" look to you. Those with Highborne ancestry always seem to have a slight twinkle in their eyes that gives it away. Before I properly put you to work around here, you should check in with our resident High Order elder Rathiril Sunlance. You can find him here in the main lodge, just around the corner from me.$B$BOh, and check in with Coriella Calmbreeze as well, she runs the local inn and can provide lodging and supplies, should you need them.",
[93464]="Allow me to admit something, $n. While draenethyst is sacred to us, and keeps us sane, none here fully understand it.$B$BI recall a mage who once came to the Harborage, from Desolace. A human by the name of Azore. He feared the power of the draenethyst; said it shouldn't fall into the wrong hands.$B$BAt the time, we drove him away to protect what was ours. Lately, however, I find myself wondering what exactly he knew.$B$BI ask that you find this mage, $r. His knowledge could be of immense value to us.",
[93465]="I suppose it would be more accurate to say I know someone who knows a thing or two about draenethyst.$B$BYou see, the warlocks of the Burning Blade have been studying it. It is a substance from beyond the dark portal, so it follows that those involved with darker arts might wish to harness it to their own ends. We cannot allow this, obviously.$B$BThe specific warlock you seek is named Gimashi. She can be found atop her tower, which is in a ravine to the southeast. Her notes will have the answers you seek.",
[93510]="It's a heavy thing to stand in Hyjal, where so many companions met their unnatural ends. The land itself echoes with grief. Craters filled with ash, memories too bitter to forget.$B$BYet you carry a spark from the Eastern Kingdoms, a warmth that defies this gloom! My childhood friend Tobin enlisted alongside me, and though I hold hope, I fear for what remains of his soul.$B$BWe'd spend afternoons skipping stones as kids across Lake Everstill in Redridge. Look for a shoreline anchor, and honor our pastime?",
[93521]="Ve'han's research notes describe his attempts to steal the power of the Wild Gods, following the ambitions of his leader, the Wild King. His successes were few, and hapless. Had he been a more powerful druid, he likely would have quickly devoured the essence of Jereman and gained even more power still.$B$BThe Guardians of Hyjal at the summit camp will definitely want to know about this.",
[93546]="Finally, FINALLY I can use this anvil for something other than a monumentally heavy table. I am delighted to finally hone my craft again after centuries of missed practice.$B$BNow, you are probably thinking, \"Vindael, this sounds like you are setting the stage for another request.\" And you would be correct!$B$BI need to replenish my supply of iron, but your iron has a similar predicament to my blade. Fortunately, the solution is MUCH simpler.$B$B<He hands you a ghostly pickaxe, without a chance to refuse.>",
[93547]="We are constantly under threat here, both by the Blackthorne Pact and by the hostile creatures of Hyjal. But we can use the thorns to our advantage! With a little help from the power of nature, we can grow new thorn bushes to help protect our enclosure.$B$BPlant thorn seeds near the road to help create barricades by the inn, the storage tower, and the grouping of trees near the road.",
[93551]="You went out of your way for the fading wishes of a lost soul--thank you, $n. The sight of another spirit at the lake, thinking of two friends competing to see who can throw further--it's enough to draw me to this moment. Presence clings to the strongest bond with the living.$B$BWe never did skip a rock from one side to the other...$B$B<The ghost gazes across the lake.>$B$BI recall. Meet me in Mourning's Rest--the site of our last battle--next to the broken cannon near the destroyed tower on the cliff.",
[93552]="Windstones are a critical resource on Zephras Isle as they contain the raw, concentrated energy of the winds themselves. The wind elementals who used to live here on Zephras with us vanished a number of years ago, and since then, the magic that sustains this island is slowly fading. Not without limitations, the windstones are still a reliable energy source, and are incredibly valuable to us.$B$BYou'll find raw windstones scattered around the grove. Think you can help me harvest them?",
[93567]="This mountain cliff to the southeast... the remains of the tower. Seared into my mind, their harrowing screams still echo forever in memories.$B$BAllow me to unburden myself and tell you of my defeat.",
[93568]="<You hold a grimy collar retrieved from the belly of a slain creature. The material is of a high-quality leather, clearly stitched with care.$B$BA tag dangles from a corroded buckle. You swipe away the gunk and can see Thalassian text, though the letters are stylized beyond readability, perhaps even to those familiar with the language.$B$BNow, you are presented with a choice. Do you disregard this and move on with your life, or do you attempt the impossible and seek to bring closure to its owner?>",
[93572]="You may have brought Kum'isha a draenethyst sphere, but that only shows Kum'isha you are lucky, not skilled. If you wish to earn your reward, you will aid Kum'isha's brethren in returning home.$B$BKum'isha will use this sphere to open a rift, while other draenei will go through. Whatever dangers come out, you will fight. If any of Kum'isha's brothers and sisters are harmed, you can forget about that reward.$B$BAre you ready, $r?",
[93574]="<With a terrible crunch, you removed a piece of the worm's carapace upon its demise.$B$BDespite its enormous size and hefty weight, it is disappointingly ordinary. This creature was seemingly not the result of a cruel experiment nor carefully bred to be an all-devouring beast.$B$BIt is simply an impressive shell, likely desired only by collectors. Perhaps you could find one, though other than the centaur, who else might be alive around here?>",
[93584]="The lands surrounding the Well of Eternity are overrun with followers of the Wild King. Many once stood beside us, bound by the same oaths, but their devotion has curdled into reckless zeal. They actively hinder our efforts to tend Nordrassil and protect the Well.$B$BI will not pretend this is easy, nor that my hands will be clean. Still, we cannot allow them to harm our land or strike our flank when the greater incursion begins.$B$BThin their ranks swiftly, and may Elune forgive what necessity demands.",
[93585]="Oh thank goodness, someone civilized!$B$BI came here on behalf of the Church of the Holy Light to make contact with the draenei of the Harborage. The Alliance has no foothold here, you see, and a bit of diplomacy with the locals may help us in that regard. The Light welcomes all into its fold, after all!$B$BHowever, the road past this bridge is crawling with the draenei's more savage kin. If I am to make it to the Harborage safely, I will need protection. Would you aid me, $c?",
[93594]="Among the treants borne of the necklace, one in particular stood above all the others to have received the gift of life and sentience. I suspect if they have fallen, he may be the only one that remains.$B$BHe spent his days tending to each and every bloom and bud, and his evenings rooted in the ground to serve as a nest for the smaller critters.$B$BIf he is alive, and I pray that to be true, then he may know what happened.$B$BI am holding out hope for my good friend, Woodwyrd.",
[93601]="If you wish to recover the woman's gift, march north into the Valley of Bones.$B$BIt was stolen. The quilboar are to blame. I saw it. With my own two eyebulbs.$B$BThey are why this garden is doomed to die.$B$BDo not forgive them.",
[93604]="Big $R heard of Razorfen Downs? <Snort.> Of course not! Big place in Barrens. Lots of thorns. Can't miss it.$B$BAgamaggan died there. Important place for all quilboar. Now bristleback not allowed. Belong to sniffle-snorting Razorfen. Razorfen disrespect quilboar history!$B$BAgamaggan's blood feeds the valley. Grow thorns. BIG ones. Bigger than puny elf necklace ever could!$B$BGo to the Downs. Fetch Kog'thug blood. Stale blood from the kraul won't work. Need GOOD blood!$B$BGive blood, get necklace, win.",
[93606]="Quolga the Wise is Kog'thug's life mate. Quolga great thornweaver, that why Kog'thug like her. Quolga also has necklace Big $R seeks.$B$BProblem? We not on squealing terms. She mad we stole necklace in first place. Then why use it? That what Kog'thug want know!$B$BBUT! Quolga like flowers as much as thorns. Know where we can get flowers? Where we got necklace!$B$BMaybe she not be mad at Kog'thug if Big $R bring flowers and this blood for him? Maybe she trade necklace!$B$BTell her Kog'thug sorry.",
[93609]="<The necklace you have been seeking is at last in your possession, but unfortunately the magic contained within has been entirely depleted. While not ideal for your current situation, at least it made its acquisition from the quilboar relatively easy.$B$BIt is probably best to bring this back to Mithera.>",
[93615]="Oh, a tasty morsel...$B$BFear not, I jest. Though I could snap your spine like a dry branch. I am a demigod of the wilds, after all.$B$BIf you would gain my favor and avoid my appetite, perhaps I could burden you with a task?$B$BMy litter of young have wandered off to entertain themselves. Little on this mountain could threaten them directly, but there are dark things afoot near the summit, and I'd leave nothing to chance.$B$BWould you check on them? In return for my not eating you, of course.",
[93617]="The hierarchy of the Wild Gods is bent. Now, all is in motion, and the nature of the world is as malleable as clay!$B$BNo more will my kin suffer the fangs of predators, for now, we shall prey upon all who have devoured us!$B$BTremble, fragile creature, for you have neither the strength nor the speed to dissuade us!",
[93644]="<Found near Shen'dralas, this dirty old tome no longer holds most of its knowledge.$B$BOf the text that remains, individual letters are difficult to distinguish from words. It may prove challenging to read at first, but one of them appears to be a surname.$B$BPerhaps its author, \"Evenshade\", may be found nearby.>",
[93663]="The draenei of the Harborage are skilled fishermen, and willing to trawl more dangerous waters than I. We occasionally trade. They give us some of their catch, and I offer some of our extra supplies.$B$BI'd sent a goblin courier to deliver my latest shipment, but he never returned. A crocolisk likely made a meal of him.$B$BMore importantly, my business reputation is at stake. That shipment must be found, and delivered to the harborage. Please, find it if you can. Check near the waters along the road.",
[93678]="I've prepared a transcription of Gimashi's notes on draenethyst. It appears the shards possess some degree of energy, but a pure sphere of the stuff is vastly more powerful. That seems to be what the Burning Blade was after.$B$BMany of Gimashi's notes allude to portals and demonic summoning rituals. Portals to where, or to summon which demons, I cannot say for sure.$B$BWhile my answers are not definitive, please take these notes back to the swamp with you. I hope you'll understand if I don't come along.",
[93679]="It is good to see you again, $n. I have been reading the notes you brought to us, and speaking with Onku, our eldest seer, about the matter.$B$BHe has recently been granted a vision that may lead us to the draenethyst sphere. We would like to share the revelations of that vision with you, if you'd join us for a moment?",
[93684]="While I know of no other settlement like ours, I have seen lost ones south of here in the Blasted Lands. They are much like the ones of Fallow Sanctuary--hostile and mindless. I assumed that was the fate which befell all of our kind there.$B$BHowever, if Onku's vision points to a lone draenei wandering a wasteland, then perhaps I was wrong.$B$BI am calling on you once again, $n. Find this draenei and aid them however you can.",
[93685]="Can your miniscule brain comprehend the rarity of a flawless sphere of draenethyst, $r? Draenei have spent lifetimes in search of just one of these crystals, only to meet horrible fates, their purpose unfulfilled.$B$BSo you stand before Kum'isha, knowing what Kum'isha has requested and still wish to assist? Very well, $r... At any time during your travels across these lands, should you find a flawless sphere of draenethyst, return it to me and I shall reward you with riches beyond your wildest dreams.",
[93689]="This is excellent news! With Dalaran returned to peace, I can see no reason the Kirin Tor would not welcome you with open arms!$B$BPlease, report to the council with great haste. I'm sure they will be looking forward to meeting the city's savior.",
[93735]="Historically, the Windshapers have seen to the tending of the magical instruments and devices that were gifted to us by the spirits of the wind. This includes the myriad of magical constructs around the island. Since the spirits left us, only a scant few of these are still functional.$B$BOne of the few remaining working constructs in Valanaar has become damaged. One of our artisans was dispatched to help, but he may be in need of aid. Travel to the west end of the city and offer any assistance you can.",
[93736]="The paramount concern of the Windshapers is to better understand why the spirits left us, and what we may be able to do to bring them back. One curious fixture of Shadowgale Forest to the north is the presence of a curious form of wind sprite that some call \"hollows\". We know little of them and why they are there, but we do know that they first started to appear after the spirits of the wind left us.$B$BI need you to go there and disperse them. Gather the remains and bring them back here.",
[93737]="Oh, hello. Ayessa sent you to assist me? Very well then.$B$BNot sure what an obvious novice like yourself can do, but if you give me a moment to pull my head out of this construct's innards I might have a few ideas of things you can do to help.",
[93738]="Brightwish, eh? So the High Order wanted to remove these components for some reason. But why though?$B$BThe High Order has always been meddlesome, constantly wanting to experiment with the wind spirits' magic. They are too bold by a mile, and we've strictly forbidden them from meddling with knowledge under Windshaper purview, but lately they've been testing our patience.$B$BI think you should report what you've learned back to Ayessa Dawnsinger. She can instruct you further on what to do.",
[93739]="Azeroth is a large world, and the territory of the Horde is vast. The Undercity, Orgrimmar, and Thunder Bluff all have very unique people and culture.$B$BIf you are to be a guest of the Horde here on Azeroth, it would do you good to visit each of our capital cities in turn. Speak with my advisor Nazgrel for directions.",
[93740]="A number of our Windshaper novices were found dead in the Highlands this morning. We can't be certain but there is a strong chance that the Al'Aketh are responsible. Windshapers trade blood for blood, every time.$B$BHead north and kill any Al'Aketh you encounter. Bring me their windstone prayer charms as proof of the deed. We do not forgive and we do not forget.",
[93746]="The High Order has been warned of the consequences of meddling with the Windshaper's affairs. I think we need to make an example out of Belathaan and send him back to the High Order with a few bruises and a healthy respect for the boundaries we set.$B$BBelathaan was seen leaving town, traveling north towards the Shrine of Akir. I don't know why he was going there, but confronting him alone on the road is the safest option. Find him, and put a bit of fear into his heart.",
[93747]="The old hulks of the war are decaying and rusting, but we can speed the process of reclamation.$B$BTake this bag of the seeds that you collected before. I have given them a small helping of magic to speed their growth. Place them near the old war machinery and let them grow over and cover them. The memories of the war will fade into the past and nature will reclaim its space.",
[93759]="You have done well and helped me, and the mountain, greatly.$B$BI am just preparing some stew, and I would be glad to share it if you would help me gather some of the ingredients.$B$BWhile I am loath to slay any among the wild animals, the cycle of life requires sustenance. A balance of ingredients would serve us well. A few Hyjal Venison Cuts from the Hyjal Stags would pair well with the starchy roots of the Scarlet Dart Tuber plants that grow in the green places nearby.",
[93773]="It seems that Ve'han has successfully stolen at least a portion of the power of a Wild God. Such a thing seems beyond belief to me, but here we are.$B$BAnd what is this \"Pact\" Ve'han spoke of? $n, you must return to Ketharas. Tell him what you've learned.$B$BI'm sorry to say but it is likely well beyond your abilities to put a foe such as Ve'han down. Only the power of--well, the Wild Gods themselves may be able to counteract this magic.",
[93786]="Does your blade thirst for human blood, $n?$B$BSome years ago, the human defectors laid claim to a small farm to the southwest across the river. With the area rich in lumber and stone, it was only a matter of time before they expanded their reach to the keep along the eastern shore known as Farholde.$B$BOur first skirmishes would have ended in our favor if we'd had the numbers. It's time to remind them of our presence.$B$BDisrupt their farming efforts. Take no prisoners. Send them a clear message.",
[93787]="Humans within these lands have long enjoyed the warmth, comfort and sustenance these lands provide. It's time we start denying these humans such pleasantries.$B$BSeek out the supplies of our enemies at the farm to the southwest. Take whatever you find.$B$BIt won't bring pleasure like bloodying a blade, but slowing them buys us time to plan our next move.",
[93788]="With the human presence to the south and Twilight to the west, the battle for resources has become difficult. But why gather resources amongst our enemies when their blades will suffice?$B$BFollow the river south to the mill. When you hear the whistling of woodworkers among the trees, tread lightly. When the opportunity presents itself, strike hard and fast.$B$BI'll stay behind to keep the forge running hot. Gur'dok will break down the blades while I fashion weaponry forged of their own materials.",
[93791]="$n, it is clear your skill with magic is growing and I believe it is time for you to partake in one of the High Order's oldest traditions for young and aspiring mages. It is time for you to craft a spell focus of your own.$B$BSeek out Belann Windwood in Valanaar. He has been crafting staves and wands for the High Order for over a century, so you will be in good hands.",
[93797]="It is a time-honored tradition for young mages to create their own spell focus when they have shown a certain degree of magical proficiency. This is typically done by gathering a fallen branch from our oldest trees, as they have some lingering traces of elemental wind.$B$BI have found the most ideal ones to be near the wind shrine, just south of Falaath Village. Go and bring me back a large branch and I will teach you about the traditions as we create your spell focus.",
[93825]="You wish to learn from us? The trees of Hyjal speak to us. Their bark holds life, and on it grows the moss we call Moonveil. It is soft, green, and strong with the mountain's soul. We need this moss to heal our hurt and bless roots.$B$BGo, gentle one. Seek the old trees where the mist clings and the sun hides. Take Moonveil moss from their bark and bring it back to me. With it, we will mend what pains us.",
[93826]="The old ways are lost to Deadwood. Their claws rip the wood, their hearts burn with rage. They strike at us, and the wilds shake.$B$BYou, friend of furbolg, can help. Go to their den. Show them the wild will not bow to greed. Slay those who foul the roots, and come back when their cries fade from the trees. Bring an end to their wise, but sad, sages. They twist fel and foul vines.$B$BDo this, and we will speak to the spirits of your name.",
[93827]="The mountain winds bring dark signs. Harpies nest high where our paws do not go. The gems they wear hold strong power. Bound with our charms, they guard us from curse and bind the spirits to our wards.$B$BBut the climb is hard, and the harpies strike with claw and storm. If you are strong like they say, go to the high crags where the wind screams. Harpy grounds are in mid land Hyjal, we see them fly above us, in the north east. Take the charms from the sky witches and bring them to me.",
[93828]="The mountain's breath is damp here by the spring, and my herbs will not dry in this thick air. When our kin return from the wild, they hang their packs wherever the roots allow good air, spread through the den.$B$BGo now. Find the strands of dried herbs hung round our home and bring them to me. With them, I will weave wraps and wards to keep our spirits strong.",
[93830]="The Deadwood dwell by a pond born of Mount Hyjal's snow melt. That water is pure, strong with the mountain's breath. We use it for our draughts and to save roots from death.$B$BHere, the springs run slow. Our source must be saved, and used with care. But their pond flows with life, it could fill our den twice over. Bring me a skin filled with that water, friend. Spirits will bless your steps, and our den will drink deep of the mountain's gift.",
[93831]="You smell like mountain winds, strong and free! I have a task, if your paws are not full.$B$BWe love bear berries, they're round, red, and sweet as honey after frost. Look for them near the shade of trees. Too many sharp rocks and mad wings for us to get the ripest bush.$B$BBring me a bunch, and I make Sweetpaw Jam! My best treat, and I will share a taste.$B$BDeal?",
[93832]="High slopes hold stone wings. Rock-beasts. Half-live, half-dead. Foul hands carve them. Do not trust their still pose. These eyes wait for one wrong step.$B$BOur young do not know the risk. One paw too near, and stone wakes with claw and fang.$B$BGo, smash these cursed forms. Break their wings, crush their shards, and let the mountain breathe free.",
[93833]="The owls of Hyjal are more than feathers and flight. Their talons, their plumes, even the bones whisper of the wild. We use these gifts to craft talismans, charms that bind the spirits and shield our kin.$B$BBut the owls do not give freely. You must take what the mountain offers. Kill $1oa owls and bring their carcasses to me.$B$BYes, we ask you to return the whole body to us, as we waste nothing provided by such graceful creatures.",
[93834]="Burrow beetles! They're a bane... and now they dig in our den more than their own. We beat them back and swing clubs when we see them skulk by, but they are quick, and to hide in the dark is their shield.$B$BIf you spot them as you climb our den, squash them! We will take their crushed shells and make a meal, so it is not all bad.",
[93835]="Lorthuna fled up to the spires above using some sort of portal. Ayessa and Elaadrin went in after her. That was just a few moments ago.$B$BI'm afraid I took one too many hits and this is where I stay. Go through the portal, find Elaadrin and help them stop Lorthuna.$B$BUnless that help that Elaadrin and Ayessa said they sent for arrives soon, you are on your own from here. Good luck, $c.",
[93836]="Muln has told me much of the elemental lords and I am afraid that we have good reason to fear Al'Akir. Now that the wards that have hidden Zephras from his view are down, we are utterly defenseless. If he chooses to attack us, we stand no chance against him here in his own domain.$B$BHigh Elder Shadowsong needs to know of the danger we are in, and more importantly, what our intentions are for our mission to Azeroth. We will find the means to save our home. I swear it.",
[93848]="The magic that Ketharas was able to craft to counteract this threat was vital to this victory. Our druids should be able to replicate the magic and use it to dispel the wards empowering the Blackthorne Pact at scale.$B$BYou should go back to Ketharas and let him know what transpired here. Tell him that he has the thanks of the Guardians of Hyjal and the Cenarion Circle. He should know that he is always welcome amongst us should he desire a place alongside his fellow druids once again.",
[93926]="Whatever reason the cult has for attacking the tower, it's not worth losing our people over.$B$BI'd like for you to head to the southwest and check in on that watchtower for us. Find the peacekeepers there and tell them to head back to the village. Holding that tower is not worth the lives it would cost and I'd rather concentrate the defenders we do have here to protect our citizens.$B$BPeacekeeper Vaaniel is in charge; let him know to head back here as quickly as possible. Hurry!",
[93927]="<As you inspect the body of the dead peacekeeper, a bloody note falls free of his hands. Picking it up and reading it may give you a clue as to how to proceed from here.>",
[93948]="Since you are going to Valanaar anyway, please deliver the signet ring you recovered from the tower to Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.$B$BHe will want this back, and more importantly, he will want to learn the fate of his nephew. Talaanis is the High Elder of Zephras Isle and more importantly, he is a good man who is well loved by the people, despite our current hardships. It pains me to think of how he will react to this news. Please express my condolences for his loss.",
[93949]="We've been bugged.$B$BIt's skyhopper season in the lowlands, which means the pests are everywhere. One of the High Order mages reported that one of the insects that they killed had an enchantment of some kind placed upon it. When we inspected it closely it seems to be some sort of listening spell.$B$BWe suspect that the cult is using these enchanted insects as spies. Go and exterminate them for us. You won't be able to tell which are enchanted by looking at them, so you'll just have to kill them all.",
[93951]="The hippogryphs that have taken up residence southwest of the village can be a nuisance, but they also present a rather unique opportunity to obtain their feathers. Many skyborne love to adorn their hair with vibrant plumes and the down feathers of a hippogryph are exceptionally vibrant and, more importantly, silky soft.$B$BIf you are heading that way, try and gather as many of the fallen feathers as you can from around their nesting grounds. Do be careful, as wild hippogryph are not tolerant of guests.",
[93952]="Barkskin stand on weak roots. Deadwood claw at our land, each day their rot digs deep, sinks more. We cannot hold alone.$B$BDeadwood Den guards are the brunt of their strength. If you seek our trust, strike down those who foul the wood. When their Guardians fall, the rest of their tribe will weaken. We even our odds.$B$BBring them down, for balance, and help keep Hyjal whole.",
[93958]="Valennia's forces just breached the inner sanctum. The fighting was thick in there at first, but it's grown... unsettlingly quiet. Go in there and do your best to link up with Valennia and her forces... if any of them are left.$B$BI'll stay here and watch your back.",
[93963]="Stormwind, Ironforge, and Darnassus all have unique peoples and cultures. As a guest of the Alliance here on Azeroth, you should take some time to visit each of our capital cities in turn.$B$BSpeak with Randal Emerson in the southern antechamber for directions to get you started.",
[93971]="<The report is sealed with the sigil of Farholde. This information may be of interest to Krom'rosh at Rog'mar.>",
[93976]="While Gur'dok and I continue our work, we did fashion a particular blade for a friend--perhaps friend is too strong a word--for an acquaintance down at the docks. This particular individual is well known and connected all across the Kingdoms and beyond.$B$BTake this. When you deliver it, let her know I sent you. And tell her we're even.",
[94003]="I am all that remains of the line of Skybreakers here on Zephras Isle. The rest were murdered by the Al'Aketh.$B$BThe only thing that outweighs my sorrow is my shame. My family's ancestral shield--the Skybreaker Bulwark--is now in the hands of a cultist named Zaal Stormshield. Family lore holds no harm may befall a worthy wielder of this shield.$B$BZaal is not worthy, of that I am sure. Find this man at the Shrine of Akir and reclaim my shield from him. Do this and I will teach you the Skybreaker Defense.",
[94004]="<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Elixir of Ogre's Strength, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>",
[94006]="Greetings, $n. You have progressed in your druidic studies far enough that I think it is time for you to meet one of the great spirits that reside here on Zephras. Urs'endris is a wise and noble spirit, who has taught druids how to take on the ursera shape for generations. Unfortunately his domain has begun to wither and fall into the sky like many other areas of Zephras.$B$BTo find him, travel northeast near the waterfall in the shadow of the Shrine of Akir. He should be able to instruct you further.",
[94007]="Now that you've gained a level of comfort in the wilds of the highlands, I believe it is time for you to seek your very own animal companion.$B$BGo to the port of Valanaar to the southeast, and speak with Quel'ana Quickgale there. He will instruct you in the art of beast taming.",
[94013]="You've returned triumphant from taming two beasts. It's time now for your last trial. The winds of Zephras whisper of greater challenges ahead.$B$BTake this Taming Rod and journey to the Gustberry Lowlands. There, tame a Vuldren Alpha and prove your mastery.$B$BComplete this lesson and you'll be ready to learn the deeper ways of the hunter.",
[94050]="You now have the power to tame a pet, but you must also gain the skills to train it. For this, there is none better than my sister, Quel'dora. She will give you the ability to train your new pet.$B$BGo with the winds, young $c.",
[94212]="<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Elixir of Wisdom, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>",
[94213]="<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Lesser Mana Potion, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>",
