[94369]="Ansirem has told me much of the elemental lords and I am afraid that we have good reason to fear Al'Akir now that the wards that have hidden Zephras are down. If the Windlord chooses to attack us, we stand no chance to defend ourselves while we are here in his domain.$B$BHigh Elder Shadowsong needs to know of the danger we are in, and more importantly, what our intentions are for our mission to Azeroth. We will find the means to save our home. I swear it.",
[94373]="Aye, the time's come, young shaman. Ye've grown stout and sturdy, like the stone beneath our boots. Takin' up the shaman's path shows ye've got the wisdom o' the mountain, even before ye've proven yerself. Ye've the grit of stone to walk the earth's path.$B$BBut to earn its favor, ye must face it proper. South o' here, the Frostmane trolls live in a cave.$B$BBring me two of the necklaces they wear, crafted from the Iceclaw bears. Then we'll speak more of yer future.",
[94374]="Aye, sapta's a brew forged with magic, bindin' our spirit to the elements. Only a few shaman know the recipe, and it's nae for the weak-willed. Drink it, and ye will see what others can't. Hold true--it's only to be drunk in a sacred place.$B$BHead north to the Spirit Stone, tucked at the end of a hidden path up the mountain. Drink it there... see what the earth has to show ye.",
[94375]="Take this rough quartz from me and bring it to Teo Hammerstorm as proof o' our meeting. He will craft a totem for ye, and this pebble will be the heart o' it. As small as it may seem, ye will come to find that size does not matter, and that even the smallest o' things can outlast many others.$B$BBe patient, $n. Remain strong. And seek wisdom. This is what earth asks o' ye. In the end, ye shall become one with the earth--respect it as it shall respect ye.",
[94411]="Be warned, members of the High Order have been seen in the vicinity of the standing stones north of the village. We have warned them time and again to not meddle at our sacred sites, but they are growing more bold in pushing us. Prove your resolve to us by going to the standing stones and dispersing them.$B$BI am loathe to condone outright bloodshed, but do what you must to drive them off. Return to me when it's done.",
[94413]="The recent emergence of the leylines on the surface of Zephras has been profound for our order. We have more direct and tangible access to the energies that permeate this place and it has increased our understanding of said magic greatly.$B$BThe Windshapers, however, view these emergences as scars on the land that must be \"healed\". This is an affront to our order and is something we simply cannot abide.$B$BGo to the leyline in the forest to the southwest and drive off the Windshapers you find there.",
[94427]="A key tenent of being a paladin is the pursuit of divinity. This is not the pursuit of godhood, but merely the pursuit of good itself, for good's sake. We've all arrived at this place due to tragedy of one form or another, and it would be easy to lose that grace that defined us as paladins in life.$B$BGo to the Undercity and seek out Tanis Alderwood in the Trade Quarter. They are in need, and they could benefit greatly from some grace.",
[94434]="Wait, you want to... help? Why would a paladin want to help a beggar like me?$B$BWell, I suppose that you could be of some assistance.$B$BIt's my wife you see. She, well... she's falling apart. I mean that literally. The apothecaries can stitch her back together right as rain, but they are about the Dark Lady's business and none are available to help. If you could perhaps bring me some fresh cloth then I could at least make her a wrapping to hold her together while we wait for the apothecaries.",
[94435]="I don't know why you'd go out of your way to help me, but I appreciate it. If someone sent you my way, tell them I appreciate them too. You'll always have a friend in Tanis Alderwood, $c.",
[94440]="These Scarlet Crusaders often carry satchels with their deployment orders. We know an attack is coming, but if we can recover their orders, we can warn the rest of the Deathguard and prepare an ambush.$B$BYou are clearly an impressive paladin. Kill these scarlet animals and retrieve a copy of their orders and bring them back to Deathguard Billmuth. He'll take it from there.",
[94441]="Please give my thanks to Danitha Morr and tell her that the rest of the Deathguard will hear about the service that the paladins of Bandarion Keep performed for us.$B$BYou have a lot of promise as a paladin, and I am proud to have those like you among the ranks of the Forsaken. Dark Lady watch over you, $n.",
[94449]="It's been long since ye were last tested, $n. Ye've shown patience, aye -- but now it's time ye learned of chaos... of destruction. Fire's call is loud, and if ye're ready to pay its price, it'll speak to ye.$B$BSeek out Bruegs Kindleborn, far east in the mountains. He dwells in a cave above South Gate Outpost. He'll know if ye're truly ready.",
[94465]="Aye, ye've the strength to bear the totem o' fire, lad--but strength alone won't make ye ready.$B$BBeyond the Valley o' Kings, in the crags of Loch Modan, lies a hidden path to one o' our sacred peaks. There, Braldir Ashmantle guards the Shrine o' the Dormant Flame.$B$BTake this torch to him--it shows yer intent. Return it burnin' by the shrine's brazier, and I'll see ye earn the totem proper.",
[94466]="Bah, ye didn't trek all this way for tales, did ye, $n? Ye seek the Eternal Flame and the fire totem.$B$BFirst, ye'll need a sapta to bind yer spirit to the flame.$B$BI'll craft it--but I'll need two things: fire tar from Tunnel Rat Geomancers in the kobold caves up north, and a reagent pouch from a Stonesplinter Seer lurkin' in the southern hills. Dangerous work, but worthy of the flame.",
[94467]="The fire sapta's ready, $n. Now ye face the flame. Use it at the shrine, then climb to the peak. There, ye'll see the spirit--he'll not strike 'til ye do, but he'll know ye see him.$B$BStrike fast, lad. The longer ye wait, the stronger he burns. When he falls, take his glowing embers and place 'em in the brazier. Light the torch and earn the fire's favor.",
[94468]="Torch firmly in hand, you turn away from the brazier and look out over Loch Modan. You feel an excitement tugging at your spirit as the wind picks up and forces the flame to dance violently.$B$BYou start off down the path back to Dun Morogh in search of Bruegs Kindleborn.",
[94479]="Picking up the rusting metal, you see another, shinier, engineering component. It looks like anything else of use has been picked clean.$B$BPerhaps somebody nearby recognizes this part or who might want to salvage it.",
[94480]="The humans of these lands are only one of many threats. With the encroaching Twilight and snarls of gnolls echoing from the hills nearby, battle may call at a moment's notice. Maintaining the strength of our allies may be the difference between Rog'mar's success or our removal from these lands.$B$BDeliver the goods you've gathered to Gorg. He'll make sure our allies are well fed.",
[94481]="This hearty stew keeps our trainees fed, enough so that our enemies remain at a distance.$B$BBring this and feed our trainees to the west. Don't listen to any complaints. With how difficult defending our supply lines has become, they should be so lucky we're not feeding them dirt.",
[94483]="Our scouts have reported training camps by the river to the south. If I'd received word sooner, it would have saved us both the hassle of locating and removing the human filth in a timely manner.$B$BContinue your efforts, $n. Holding back the humans to their precious little keep will buy us time to focus on other matters at hand.$B$BBe swift about it.",
[94484]="A moment if you will, $n. Are you headed towards Shadowgale Forest? There is a druid conclave there in a cave to the northeast. I have been waiting on word from them but their correspondence is long overdue.$B$BWith Ban'aethall in ruins and all the unrest lately I worry something dire may have happened. Please, if you are able, go seek out Elegael Thornpaw and put my mind at ease.",
[94485]="If we are to save my fellows in the Nightclaw Den, I am going to need some ingredients for a poultice. The first and most important is a spindly moss called Lady's Tear. It typically grows on the base of the trees here in Shadowgale.$B$BThis moss secretes a sticky substance that acts as an antiseptic and is perfect for binding open wounds. I have gathered what little I can reach but I know there is more in this forest.$B$BGo and be swift. We are going to need a lot if the injured I left behind still live.",
[94486]="The other ingredient I need for the poultice is feathers from the Shadowgale shrieklings that roam this forest. In their juvenile form, the shrieklings have insulative feathers which would be ideal to put over the moss. These feathers will prevent the antiseptic sap from drying out and will provide at least some protection against the elements.$B$BBe warned, the shrieklings are normally docile but they have been incredibly hostile of late. Their large talons can easily disembowel you if you aren't careful.",
[94487]="The Al'Aketh Cultists ambushed us with no warning, though their motives remain a mystery to me. I knew these cultists had clouds between their ears, but I never imagined they would upset the delicate balance here on Zephras with such brutality. Go, slay as many as you can and take their heirlooms if they wear any.$B$B<Elegael spits.>$B$BThese storm-cursed cultists don't deserve to be called shen'dorei. The beasts of the forest can have their bodies. Their ashes don't deserve the winds.",
[94488]="The reason for cultists' presence here still baffles me, but I smell a familiar scent over the bloodshed.$B$BOne of our circle druids, Haalien, disappeared months back. It appears he's thrown his sorry hide in with the cultists.$B$BShow him what happens when he spills the blood of his kin! Take his head and return it to me.",
[94489]="I have finished the poultices. Quickly, take them to the druids in the cave, north just across the clearing. I know my brethren are in much more dire condition than I. They are likely too injured to heal their own wounds. There are so few of us shen'dorei druids that every life is precious.$B$BBefore you go, I have a selfish request. My mate, Jorel Windsinger was in dire condition when I left. Please, see to his wounds if he still lives.",
[94490]="<Tucked behind one of Haalien's bracers is a note that's been slightly torn and bloodstained in your fight. It looks like it contains useful information about the cultist motivations for the attack on the druid den. Elegael would be interested in this intel.>",
[94491]="It would appear that there is a correspondent hiding somewhere in Valanaar feeding information to the cult. I am clearly in no shape to make the journey, but Lotheluum needs to know what transpired here.$B$BHe should also know the fate of those who are no longer with us. Thanks to your help I think we can handle the rest of the situation from here, though the damage has been done.$B$BPlease go swiftly, $n. I hope our paths will cross again someday. Until then, I have cultists to slay.",
[94493]="Thank goodness our message got to Lotheluum. Wait, where are the rest of the reinforcements? Surely it is not just you they sent?$B$B<Elegael pales as you explain yourself.>$B$BSo the message did not get to Valanaar. We are in dire straits indeed then.$B$B<Elegael sighs deeply then looks resolute.>$B$BThen we must handle this on our own. Time is of the essence.",
[94494]="Long has it been since ye were last tested, $n. Ye have shown patience thus far in yer studies, but the time has come for ye to learn about the purity of water.$B$BSeek out Norric Lochthane in Loch Modan. He is along the north western edge o' the lake, south of Stonewrought Dam. Ye will find him there at his burrow hut. Good luck to ye, $n.",
[94495]="If there's one truth ye need to learn about water, it's this: water means rebirth. It carves stone, cleanses filth, and heals the weary -- but only when it's pure. Taint it, and it'll ruin all it touches.$B$BIf ye seek the water sapta, find Hervdana Saegrund in the Wetlands. Her family dwells in a cave beneath the southern falls.$B$BGo on then, don't let the river outrun ye.",
[94497]="Ah, so ye've come seekin' the sapta, have ye? Well then, listen close, love. To find understandin' and earn the sapta, ye must seek water in its various forms. As ye gather the samples, keep yer eyes open. Watch the beasts that guard it, the land it nourishes, and how it changes lives.$B$BWe'll start simple: fill this skin at the base o' the falls, where the fresh meets the brackish. Go on now, and mind the marsh.",
[94499]="Aye, Redridge drinks deep from Lake Everstill, but by the time the waters tumble down Stonewatch Falls, somethin' has seeped in. The murlocs down there are big, twisted brutes. Not like the ones ye find here or in the Loch. Lucky for the townsfolk they keep to the base o' the falls.$B$BBring a sampling to me. I've a mind to find out if it's magic, venom, or somethin' worse that's taintin' the waters near that old fort.",
[94500]="Take this waterskin and journey deep into the emerald shade o' Ashenvale. Astranaar rests cradled by waters untouched by corruption. Ruins litter the bed o' the lake, hinting at a bygone era. Bring back a sample from the lake. Pure, ancient, and possibly enchanted water.$B$BIt's the last liquid I need before I send ye back to Norric.$B$BBoard the boat in Menethil to Auberdine. It stops in Southshore on the way over.$B$BAnd mind yerself... the forest's got eyes, and they don't blink.",
[94501]="Norric will have one more task for ye before rewarding ye with the water totem rites. The vial of water I've given ye is necessary for whatever that task is. Go now and find him. We shall meet again some day.",
[94502]="In Westfall, outside o' Moonbrook lies Stendel's Pond. Once a pure spring, now touched by dark forces. The spirits there 'ave gone silent.$B$BYe must drink the water sapta, then face the corruption that fouls the waters. Take its bracers and the last drops o' Hervdana's potion, then place 'em on the shrine. That'll call forth a spirit, cleansed and true. Speak with it, learn what ye can.$B$BBring me proof the deed's done, and I'll grant ye the totem.",
[94503]="Light erupts as the final word leaves your lips. The hiss of water turning to mist fades into silence, and your senses reel as the corrupt spirits around you unravel, their essence scattered like ash in the wind.",
[94504]="Some may speak with you now, but not all. For more of our tribe to be what you know as friend, you must not rush.$B$BStay by our side, work with our young and old, and guard us from those who wish us harm.$B$BWhen you have more to bring to us, we will have more to share.",
[94505]="Take shard. Take shard and give life.$B$BGive life and understand. Understand water is life... corruption stops life.$B$BYou protect and give life with water's power.",
[94532]="Though the gnoll presence has dwindled with the Twilight's encroachment, the threat remains.$B$BThe hills to the southwest are infested with their kind, disrupting trades and travelers alike.$B$BClear a path for our allies by removing the threat.",
[94533]="Among the cackling inhabitants of the Bristle Hills southwest of here is an elder gnoll by the name of Snargl. The sounds emanating from this particular gnoll are quite unpleasant. Their presence inspires those around, creating a problem for allies and scouts who enter the area.$B$BA trophy as a memento of our having dealt with this most unpleasant gnoll fiend would fit nicely with my collection.$B$BBe swift about it, $n.",
[94535]="Our allies mining ore from the hills to the south reported several attacks by gnolls in the area.$B$BTravel south, locate their camps and retrieve the stolen ore. Take it from their dead bodies if need be.",
[94556]="Jom-jom came looking for friend. Now Jom-jom want to go home.",
[94568]="The turncoat clearly was afraid of what the cult had planned, enough so to defect and seek our aid. It's truly unfortunate that he is dead and took his secrets to the grave with him.$B$BWe must discuss this further to determine our next steps.",
[94613]="Our warhorses come from two nearby farms. One of them, owned by the Wheeler family off the road just outside of town, has apparently lost all of their stock. The cause of this is currently unknown.$B$BWith no horses, we have no cavalry, and without cavalry, our campaign against the Horde stands no chance.$B$BThus, you see, this situation must be resolved with utmost haste. Of where to start, however, I am less sure.$B$BGo to Wheeler's Grange and speak to Benjy. See what he has to say for himself.",
[94614]="You seen those murlocs down by the river, just west of here? Nasty things. Bad for my animals, and bad for the wildlife. Not to mention, they've settled right on top of my favorite fishing spot!$B$BThere ain't a soul in the Riverglades who wouldn't appreciate you getting rid of a few, that's for sure.$B$BPlease, kill any you see. You'd be doin' us a whole heap of good.",
[94615]="I've got no idea what happened to our horses. I got up one morning to feed 'em and they were all gone, just like that.$B$BLife outside Farholde's a bit rougher. Anything could've got 'em--animals, murlocs, orcs, you name it.$B$BIf we wanna narrow down our list of culprits, we oughta search around the stables for clues.",
[94617]="There's a pack of coyotes livin' in a den west of here. We can see 'em sometimes from across the river. They used to hunt fish on the shore, but I guess the murlocs pushed 'em out of their usual feeding ground, and so they've taken to eating horses.$B$BThe leader of the coyote pack's a bigger one with dark fur. We'd nicknamed him \"Sootfur\". I reckon if you kill him, the rest'll scatter.",
[94618]="From what you found, it seems like the coyotes got most of the horses. Still, there's a few not accounted for.$B$BThose that didn't get eaten probably ran off scared someplace. I don't know how many of those horses there are, but we'd better find 'em before the coyotes come back.$B$B<Benjy holds out a sack in front of you.>$B$BHere. If you find one, give it some of our feed. That'll get it to trust you so you can lead it back here.",
[94638]="You have come to me in hopes of learning to take a shape of strength. I have a task for you, though it lies heavy on my heart.$B$BMy mate, Ur'endra, has lost herself to madness and has begun to attack her own kin. Without the magic of the winds, many creatures have begun to lose themselves... Ur'endra included. She makes her lair in a cave to the west of here, in the bluffs along the border between the Shen'dar Highlands and the Gustberry Lowlands.$B$BEnd her suffering and I shall grant you my blessing.",
[94668]="You smashed weak Twilight ogres. But they weak.$B$BToday you show Bloodmaster and little goblin friend you belong.$B$BTomorrow, maybe we meet again if you still breathing.",
[94669]="First things first. I'm gonna need a deposit for your, uh... safety.$B$BLook, I don't make the rules here. It's required.$B$BNow if you should choose not to pay I'll be forced to tell old Clugfist our new friend wasn't so keen on proving their strength to our warm, welcoming friends here.$B$BThat would be a real shame. Catch my drift, bub?",
[94670]="The battle of the Bloodmaster's Ring begins!$B$BWe'll start you off easy here, pal. This flighty fiend'll take you down, then pick ya clean.$B$BNow quit standin' around and step into the ring. Fame awaits!",
[94672]="Humans are not our only adversary within the Riverglades, $n, nor are they our most dire.$B$BA cult known as the Twilight's Hammer has begun a campaign against those they deem heretics in the eyes of their twisted gods. The ravaged remains of a human settlement to the west are but the first to fall to their conquest. No doubt Rog'mar will be next.$B$BWe cannot afford to let them establish a foothold so close to our doorstep. Go to this so-called Sunnyglade and thin their numbers.",
[94678]="The gnolls have been a thorn in our side ever since we arrived. While less a threat than the Twilight's Hammer, they are aggressive, persistent and, worst of all, numerous.$B$BThe hills beyond this post are infested with them, making passage to the north dangerous, and posing a threat to those living outside the walls of Farholde Keep.$B$BIf we are ever to make these lands safe, removing the gnoll threat is imperative.",
[94679]="Gnolls value strength above all else. By killing their strongest, we not only lessen the threat they pose physically, but also strike fear into their hearts.$B$BIn a den among the Bristle Hills is a notorious gnoll by the name of Snargl. His death would no doubt sow panic among the Redridge's ranks.$B$BBring me his snout, and be quick about it.",
[94680]="There have always been small pockets of Twilight's Hammer cultists here and there, but never have I seen them in such numbers. They seem emboldened by someone, or something, to expand their influence.$B$BI would know more of these cultists and what they seek. Their shadowmancers are blessed by the dark powers and are likely the most trusted within their order to lead attacks of this scale.$B$BBring me anything you find off their corpses that we may glean knowledge into their campaign.",
[94727]="The Twilight's Hammer are here for more than simple chaos, $n. They appear to be digging throughout the Riverglades for something. As for what they are searching for, I cannot say. A source of power, of course, but what that is still eludes me.$B$BTheir zealots may not be willing to divulge their secrets, but they must have someone doing the digging for them. These are the ones you are to question. Return to Sunnyglade and 'convince' one of their miners to talk. We must get to the bottom of this.",
[94733]="Alright, so you won a few battles. I think you might have what it takes to make it here after all.$B$BBefore I convince our next combatant to jump into the ring with you there's something I need from you first--food for Chub'chob's pet boar, Snufflesnout.$B$BI promised I'd look after it, and, well, this gig here's keepin' me quite busy. Trust me, this'll benefit the both of us.$B$BMosey on over to the east of Clugfist's clubhouse. You're lookin' for a shy fella who goes by the name Gobam.",
[94734]="Gobam know Chub'chob pet love to eat food. Specially good food!$B$BYum yum berry and plant from river make good treat for Snufflesnout. Berry sweet. Best berry from human farm near ocean.$B$BYou find. Bring back. Me help make big treat.",
[94737]="Ok friend. Here is treat. Snufflesnout snort and be happy when she see this.$B$BAnd tell goblin please stop talk so much.",
[94739]="Glad you made it through the first round, I guess.$B$BThis next contestant and I go way back. He ain't the brightest fella, but he's sure good at pummeling anything in his path.$B$BJust head on into the pit and get yourself ready while I make the announcement.",
[94744]="You did well slowing the Twilight's Hammer. Their foothold in Sunnyglade has weakened and you've turned their ogre warriors against them. Now we take the fight to them.$B$BMy brother, Dag'rosh, has already gone ahead with a scouting party. I would have preferred he waited for you, but he is impulsive and overeager--like a true warrior. I'd be honored if you joined him in battle at their stronghold to the west.",
[94745]="Do you see the fortress just west of here? The Twilight's Shroud, they call it. Filled to the brim with Twilight's Hammer cowards.$B$BThey may have walls and numbers, but their pitiful reliance on devilry and ancient gods makes them weak. Show them how vulnerable they really are!",
[94748]="Those Twilight's Hammer dogs caught us before we could properly begin our attack. I was able to fight my way out, but my warriors were not so lucky. They were dragged off by the cult's champions and imprisoned in the fortress to the west.$B$BOrcs do not belong in cages, $c. Free my brothers and sisters, and we will show these mongrels a real fight.",
[94768]="Tran'gul's notes pointed to a leader of this Twilight's Hammer presence somewhere in that fortress. With my warriors free and the cult's numbers in disarray, now is the time to pierce the heart of this infestation.$B$BReturn to the Twilight's Shroud and enter their Stronghold. That is where you will find Overlord Kilgar. That is where we will exact our revenge.",
[94774]="You've caught the attention of our superiors, $n. They've asked you to travel to the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind as soon as possible. Apparently they feel you've proven yourself already and are prepared to further your training. When you get there, find High Priestess Laurena. She will be able to guide you further. Good luck, and may the Light be with you.",
[94775]="Elune bless you, good $r. I hope your Light finds you and protects you well this day.$B$BOne of your priests was here not long ago looking for you. He mentioned you returning to the Cathedral of Light as soon as possible to speak with High Priestess Laurena. It seems you've done well to garner such attention. I wouldn't spend too much time here--your people have need of you.",
[94776]="Time's come for you to head to Stormwind, $n. High Priestess Laurena in the Cathedral of Light wants to speak to you. Gotta be somethin' really good or really bad for the High Priestess to want you there personally, but I'm guessin' you've only done well for yourself and it's a good thing that she wants to speak to ya.$B$BBut don't waste too much time 'round here. I'd head there as soon as you can.",
[94777]="Just a short time ago, one of your priests was here looking for you, $r. He said that if I were to see you, I should direct you towards the Cathedral of Light. He said it was very important, but I would not be overly concerned if I were you. His demeanor seemed positive... as though it were good news. I wouldn't take too long in making my way there if I were you.$B$BElune be with you, good $r.",
[94778]="You're needed in Stormwind, $n. The High Priestess there, Laurena, says it's time for you to prove you're worthy of the next level of your training. Don't waste too much time finding your way there. You can find her in the Cathedral of Light in the center of the city. Give her my regards, and prove how worthy you are of such a calling. The Light be with you, $n.",
[94779]="Praise be to Elune, and to your Light, $n.$B$BAbout this time, many of our order learn abilities reflecting their faith in Elune. If knowledge serves me, I believe the same holds true for your order also.$B$BWhen your business in Darnassus is complete, I would seek out one of your High Priestesses for further training.",
[94782]="With the warlocks under control, I'd say this area's well in wing.$B$B<The crow nods sagely, looking pleased.>$B$BThough our work here is done, there are other areas that could use your help and as an underwing of mine I would like you to go see what all the fuss is about.$B$BFollow the path northwest up the road to the old outpost. An old friend awaits!",
[94789]="The winds o' Azeroth greet ye, and soon ye'll stand among some o' our mightiest kin. I'm proud to see how far ye've come--your future looks bright indeed.$B$BThe element o' air's a tricky one to master, but I've faith your skill will see ye through any challenge.$B$BMake your way north into Arathi Highlands. In its northern hills, you'll find Veyric Thundervein. He'll teach ye more.",
[94792]="Many hunters prefer to travel with animal companions. With a beast at your side, you will find that you can survive even the most dangerous of circumstances. As they say, everything is easier with a friend. However, obtaining an animal companion is something that must be done with care. The balance of nature is delicate, and must always be respected.$B$BTake this Taming Rod with you to the forest. With it, you will be able to tame a Rockhide Boar and practice your skills as a hunter.",
[94793]="You now have the power to tame a pet, but you must also gain the skills to train it. For this, there is none better than Isaac Chan, a lifelong woodsman. He will give you the ability to train your new pet.$B$BGo with the winds, young $c.",
[94819]="$n, your High Priestess Mims would have an audience with you in Ironforge. Make haste, my clever friend, your next test quickly approaches. Although I wish I could bear witness to your race's own special rites, my place is here. But may the Light go with you in your travels. Mims should still be in the Mystic Ward once you reach the city. She will be waiting.",
[94820]="Your race is so very clever, $n. We are proud to call you allies. And as each day's sun sets, you and your kin grow closer to reclaiming your city, but with the burden of keeping your families safe in exile. That yearning for home must weigh heavily on you.$B$BWord came from Ironforge just recently. It asked that you return there and speak to High Priestess Mims in the Mystic Ward. I would not keep her waiting. May Elune guide your travels.",
[94821]="A priest recently visited our halls seeking you out, young $r. He said that he was on a mission to find you and that you should return to the Hall of Mysteries in Ironforge as soon as possible. When you arrive, seek out High Priestess Mims--she will tell you more.$B$BThe Light be with you, $n.",
[94822]="You've caught the attention of our superiors, $n. They've asked you to travel to the Hall of Mysteries in Ironforge as soon as possible. Apparently they feel you've proven yourself already and are prepared to further your training. When you get there, find High Priestess Mims. She will be able to guide you further. Good luck, and may the Light be with you.",
[94823]="Elune bless you, good $r. I hope your Light finds you and protects you well this day.$B$BOne of your priests was here not long ago looking for you. He mentioned you returning to the Hall of Mysteries as soon as possible to speak with High Priestess Mims. It seems you've done well to garner such attention. I wouldn't spend too much time here--your people have need of you.",
[94824]="Time's come for you to head to Ironforge, $n. High Priestess Mims in the Hall of Mysteries commands you to come speak with her. Gotta be somethin' really good or really bad for the High Priestess to want you there personally, but I'm guessin' you've only done well for yourself and it's a good thing that she wants to speak to ya.$B$BBut don't waste too much time 'round here. I'd head there as soon as you can.",
[94825]="Just a short time ago, one of your priests was here looking for you, $r. He said that if I were to see you, I should direct you towards the Hall of Mysteries. He said it was very important, but I would not be overly concerned if I were you. His demeanor seemed positive... as though it were good news. I wouldn't take too long in making my way there if I were you.$B$BElune be with you, good $r.",
[94826]="Praise be to Elune, and to your Light, $n.$B$BAbout this time, many of our order learn abilities reflecting their faith in Elune. If knowledge serves me, I believe the same holds true for your order also.$B$BWhen your business in Darnassus is complete, I would seek out your High Priestess for further training.",
[94829]="If you've come to demand more of our crop, you're too late. No doubt you saw my farm. Destroyed. All of it.$B$BGood folk toiled in these fields for years to feed troops and civilians alike. But when those cultists arrived, where was the military? Where was our promised protection after all the rations they'd taken from us?$B$BIf you've any sense of decency, I beg you. The least we can do is recover their belongings from those cursed raiders. Let my people rest with their kin in the graveyard to the west.",
[94832]="Unfortunately I haven't had much luck with identifying the ring's owner to bring closure to their family.$B$BPerhaps Daythor can be of assistance. He knew the others of our regiment quite well.$B$BI only hope it does not bring back unpleasant memories...",
[94841]="<A handwritten label appears on the side of the crate. On the right side is a map with a large red circle along a southeastern shoreline north of a poorly drawn temple surrounded by water and some kind of winged creatures. On the left is a note in massive font.>$B$BPROPERTY OF FRIZ FRAZZLESPARK$B$BPOWDERFUSE PORT$B$BWARNING: NOT for tampering. Do NOT open without supervision.$B$B<An additional note appears at the bottom of the label.>$B$BIf lost, return to Friz Frazzlespark. Powderfuse Port. Riverglades.",
[94842]="We make our own fertilizer out here. It's a special formula of mine that reeks like hell, but grows trees like they're weeds.$B$BIt's a 1:1:2 ratio of crawfish shells, manure, and murloc heads. Tasty, right?$B$BThe manure's easy enough. We've got the ranch to the south for that. The heads and shells? Those you're going to have to go wading in the river for.$B$BIf you feel like lending a hand, we could sure use your help getting some fertilizer ingredients.",
[94843]="Considering you got yourself wrist-deep in guts and manure for us, it's only right you get to do the fun part too.$B$BThe boys and I gather seeds from the trees as we work. With the fertilizer you've provided, I've made a planting kit to put them in the ground to grow new saplings.$B$BTake it, and find some good planting spots around the work sites.",
[94857]="Stranger, listen to me!$B$BI work as a lumberjack for the nearby logging camp. As you can see, I've been trapped here in an accident. If I don't get out from here soon, I'll either bleed out, or be eaten by wild animals.$B$BPlease, go to the logging camp and fetch help!",
[94858]="There was one more thing I wanted to talk to you about, friend.$B$BWhen the Twilight's Hammer attacked, I put everyone who couldn't defend themselves in the barn to hide. I thought they would be safe. I thought...$B$B<Elbrim's voice cracks as he recounts what happened.>$B$BIf you could do me one last kindness, will you go see what's left of my family? They should be buried here at home with me. I just don't have the heart to check myself.",
[94861]="Well, I guess that explains why Curly didn't come back for lunch break. Looks like I have to bail him out again -- typical. The way he makes me worry, I swear, I'll be gray in a year.$B$BCome on, we'll have to save him ourselves, and it sounds like we don't have much time.",
[94863]="You've already mastered taming a boar. Now it's time for the next lesson. The forest holds fiercer companions, and with care, you can earn their trust.$B$BTake this Taming Rod and seek out a Gray Forest Wolf. Remember, nature's balance must be respected. Prove your skill as a hunter once more.",
[94864]="You've proven yourself by taming a boar and a wolf. Now it's time for your final challenge. Elwynn's balance depends on respect and skill. Take this Taming Rod and seek out a Young Forest Bear. Show that you can earn the trust of even the mightiest companion.$B$BCompleting this lesson will deepen your attunement to beasts.",
[94872]="The fierce Magram are undoubtedly winning the war of territories at the moment. While we can all be thankful the clashes haven't erupted too frequently throughout the desert, every day their village just to the east grows a little bigger; their soldiers a little bolder.$B$BI worry gravely about the consequences of an unchecked Magram clan, but I cannot deny their potential as an ally.$B$BIf you wish to earn their trust, offer this sack of totems to their quartermaster, but be careful.",
[94873]="Either dominant centaur clan is likely to pose a good ally, but I ought to offer a word of caution regarding the Gelkis.$B$BI have trustworthy intel that suggests, between the Magram and the Gelkis, the latter are very much on the losing side. This may work to our advantage--desperation may push the isolated clan into opening up to outside help.$B$BI have prepared a tote of totems for you to take to their quartermaster, assuming they have one, in Gelkis Village. This may work in our favor.",
[94877]="When you look around you, what do you see? A broken home and a tired people.$B$BStormwind has left us to fend for ourselves, and we have less to do that with every day. Many within these walls are refugees who barely escaped tragedy without so much as even their own families.$B$BFarholde is no Stormwind, stranger. We lost a settlement in the northwest to the Twilight's Hammer, but we will not let them keep it. If you wish to fight, go to Sunnyglade and purge those savages from our lands.",
[94879]="You've seen the ruined city to the north, yes? Sunnyglade? Demar tries sending troops, but we're no closer to reclaiming it. I have a better idea.$B$BIn truth, this attack by the Twilight's Hammer is not the first. They seem to be coordinating from a centralized location, and I would know where. While you're out doing what you adventurers do best, see if you can't keep an eye out for any documents they may have misplaced. With enough of them, I should be able to piece together their intentions.",
[94881]="My, what have we here? A brave new $c come to save us from our woes? How charming! Maybe you can help me with something then? I'd quite like to learn more about this cult in Sunnyglade.$B$BLike any cult, they operate in a caste system. Those with an affinity for magic are often in high favor and are given tokens to demonstrate such. These charms are then imbued, and thus have a rich abundance of cultist magic.$B$BI wish to see these tokens for myself. Be a dear and see if you can bring me a few, hmm?",
[94884]="I've had enough of this cave. Once you clear your way out, I'll slip out amidst the chaos.$B$BI'm afraid I'm in too weak of condition to carry those samples, however. Their energy is overwhelming, and I've been trapped down here for Light knows how long. Once we get out of here, please take them to Lady Amberhall immediately. I must rest.",
[94885]="The log is full of meticulous recordings on the comings and goings of Twilight's Hammer forces throughout the Riverglades.$B$BThe author is nowhere to be found, but this information could help shed light on enemy movements.$B$BSomeone in Farholde will want to see this.",
[94886]="As helpful as you've been here in Farholde, I believe your talents could be put to better use elsewhere.$B$BA patrol of ours went missing some time ago. They were in charge of our western borders, but with the information Miss Amberhall has uncovered, I fear they walked right into the Twilight Hammer's central encampment.$B$BWe can handle the cleanup in Sunnyglade ourselves. If the good lady is right, it's critical that we check on our wayward sergeant. He could use all the help he can get.",
[94887]="Field Marshal Ryan is one of our best. His keen eyes and reliable intel have been paramount to our war efforts.$B$BHis final reports refer to a Twilight's Hammer fortress to the west. Find him before it's too late. And take his logbook with you. It may offer more clues as to the whereabouts of our missing marshal.",
[94888]="If Amberhall is so impatient for her report, it would have been nice if she sent more than one $c. Must be hard work hiding in her ivory tower.$B$BLook, every attempt to contact Farholde Keep ends with our runners being captured by Twilight scouts. I can't afford to risk any more troops going into that fortress, but we can't keep my people imprisoned in there either.$B$BYou want us to return? Help me rescue my soldiers first. You should be able to find the keys to their cages off their champions' corpses.",
[94889]="It seems every day the Twilight's Hammer are drawing more into their order, while we haven't heard so much as a word from Stormwind. Sooner or later we'll be overrun.$B$BI don't care what a bureaucrat like Amberhall says. I'm not abandoning this position while an army amasses in our own homeland. If we leave now, we'll only have to deal with these cultists again later. Only next time, on our doorstep.$B$BIf your orders are to babysit me anyway, at least make yourself useful and help me cull these zealots.",
[94890]="With this kind of momentum, we can't stop now. The soldiers we rescued are itching to draw blood, and you've already proven yourself a capable battering ram.$B$BReturn to the Twilight's Shroud and finish what we've started. Their leader, an orc by the name of Overlord Kilgar, hides deep within his keep while his underlings are lost in their panic.$B$BIf we want to put an end to this, bring me the head of Kilgar. These gods-fearing cowards can't make a single decision on their own.",
[94891]="Seems like things are quieting down around here for now, but I want to keep an eye out. You want to send Amberhall a report? Send her this.$B$B<Sergeant Riftan tosses Kilgar's head back to you.>$B$BThat ought to shut her up. At least for a while. Good work out there.",
[94892]="It's too late for me, stranger. I'm not going to be making it out of this one. Take my crest to the Knight Commander. Warn him...$B$B<Ryan's eyes begin to glaze over as he mumbles to himself.>$B$BI'm sorry. I should have come home. Abigail...",
[94894]="Lady Amberhall told me of your exploits with the Twilight's Hammer. I'm impressed. But concerned.$B$BFarholde started its campaign originally to remove the Horde from our homeland. While that remains our primary goal, we cannot take this sudden surge in cultist activity lightly. If our pleas to Stormwind remain unheard, we will be overwhelmed as we face foes on two fronts alone.$B$BWith the evidence you carry, perhaps they can set aside their pride long enough to listen. At this point it's our only option.",
[94895]="<A handwritten label appears on the side of the crate. On the right side is a map with a large red circle along a southeastern shoreline north of a poorly drawn temple surrounded by water and some kind of winged creatures. On the left is a note in massive font.>$B$BPROPERTY OF FRIZ FRAZZLESPARK$B$BPOWDERFUSE PORT$B$BWARNING: NOT for tampering. Do NOT open without supervision.$B$B<An additional note appears at the bottom of the label.>$B$BIf lost, return to Friz Frazzlespark. Powderfuse Port. Riverglades.",
[94896]="You look like a capable adventurer. Do you happen to be headed towards Shadowgale Forest? Ban'aethal lies deep in the forest; that's where we're all from.$B$B<Ealaane gestures to the other refugees.>$B$BWe've recently had to evacuate Ban'aethal, as it began to fall into the sky. It was sudden and in the middle of the night. If you are headed that way, would you please look for any belongings left behind? The forest and village are far too dangerous for us to return to now.",
[94897]="If you are traveling to Ban'aethal, I have a selfish request. My love, Resaan... I believe is no longer a part of this world. He had tried to go back to get supplies even though I begged him to stay. It has been over a week already and I fear the worst.$B$BPlease, if you find him, bring him home. If he has perished then I beg you to please bring me his heirloom.",
[94898]="When our home started to fall into the sky that fateful night, it's as if the elements themselves were waiting to consume us. Wind spirits began appearing as we were fleeing, and to our dismay they began attacking the fleeing survivors.$B$BWe lost many villagers to the sky, but even more to the relentless anger of those wind spirits. I don't know if it was our village falling into the sky, but they are extremely dangerous.$B$BIf you are able, please put them to rest.",
[94901]="[PH] Collect frogs",
[94902]="[PH] Collect grapes from the vineyard",
[94907]="You've been such a good little $c for me, I wonder if I could ask you to do one more small favor.$B$BWith the reagents you collected being so finely attuned to Twilight's Hammer magic, they are perfect for a summoning ritual. However, we'll need to take them to the source of their power.$B$BShould you happen upon a conduit while you're gallivanting about the Twilight's Shroud, see if you can't call upon one of the cult's thralls and capture it with this soulstone for me. For questioning, of course.",
[94911]="Greetings, young $r. I can see that you have much promise in the druidic arts. There is one who you may want to speak with in the city of Thunder Bluff by the name of Turak Runetotem. He will teach you how to reach the stronghold of the Cenarion Circle on Kalimdor, Moonglade.$B$BYou will be welcomed there, and the druids of the circle will impart their knowledge upon you.$B$BAs your people would say--go with the wind's blessing, young one. I wish you good fortune in your adventures.",
[94912]="Greetings, young $c.$B$BHave you heard of the Cenarion Circle? I'd expect not. They are an ancient order of naturalists and practitioners of the druidic arts, much like yourself. In the city of Stormwind you'll find a night elf by the name of Sheldras Moontree. He will teach you how to reach the stronghold of the Cenarion Circle on Kalimdor, a place called Moonglade.$B$BGo now. You have much to learn if you wish to save your home.",
[94913]="All druids are welcomed to the sacred lands of Moonglade. Keeper Remulos--Moonglade's guardian--keeps watch over all druids who hibernate there. I'll teach you the spell that lets you transport yourself there. Cast it whenever you seek Moonglade's knowledge or solace.$B$BAs for your first lesson here on Azeroth, travel to Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven about the path you're now on. Good luck, young druid.",
[94914]="All druids are welcomed to the sacred lands of Moonglade. Keeper Remulos--Moonglade's guardian--keeps watch over all druids who hibernate there. I'll teach you the spell that lets you transport yourself there. Cast it whenever you seek Moonglade's knowledge or solace.$B$BAs for your first lesson here on Azeroth, travel to Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven about the path you're now on. Good luck, young druid.",
[94923]="<Robbie leans in to talk to you, as if sharing a grave secret.>$B$BPsst! Hey $gmister:miss;, I need your help!$B$BMy sister got me a hat for my birthday but I lost it playing in the river. I'm not allowed to be down there because of the murlocs so I can't ask Dad or Ellie for help because then they'll know where I was!$B$BIt's a good hat. I bet one of those murlocs found it and kept it for himself!",
[94924]="The orcish poachers are a bloodthirsty lot. They'll kill anything that moves--be it men, lions, or horses. They are a threat to all life in the Riverglades, and must be stopped.$B$BThey roam the plains in packs, like rabid animals. If you see any, put them down.",
[94925]="Farholde prides itself on its independence, but there are a few things we can only get through trade.$B$BWe've negotiated an arrangement with a dealer at Powderfuse Port. We provide her with goods that are dangerous to acquire, and she provides us with specialty munitions.$B$BCurrently, she's in the market for lion fur. A pride of them live atop a large hill in the center of the plains. If you'd like to make yourself useful, you could aid me in harvesting some of their hides.",
[94926]="Like most ogre weaponry, this hammer is large, unwieldy, and well-worn. A creature of any other race could hardly swing it at all.$B$BTo you, it is of little more use than a trophy, but perhaps someone at Farholde would appreciate knowing of Komuk's demise.",
[94927]="When you're ready, I'll unlock my shackles, and we'll commence the escape. We'll take the quickest route, right through the center of camp. Be prepared for a fight.$B$BOnce we're out, I'll return to Farholde for medical treatment. As a final favor, I ask that you update Cornelius on my whereabouts. Frankly, the last thing I want after all this is to get an earful from that man.",
[94928]="These hides are to be delivered to Powderfuse Port. It is a goblin-run port to the northeast.$B$BWhen you get there, deliver the hides to Friz Frazzlespark. Tell her they're from Cornelius. The details of our trade have already been worked out, so she'll know what they are for.",
[94929]="I know I said that was it, but I promise, I wouldn't ask this if it weren't important. It's a shipment of utmost urgency.$B$BAn old acquaintance resides in a keep within the Riverglades. To get there, travel northeast through the bogs avoiding the deadly creatures within. Along the northeastern hillside sits an old path. Travel its road all the way through the hills and when you hit the fork in the road stay north, then east. You should see Farholde along the eastern shore.$B$BI thank you for your aid.",
[94930]="<A handwritten label appears on the side of the crate. On the right side is a map with a large red circle along a southeastern shoreline north of a poorly drawn temple surrounded by water and some kind of winged creatures. On the left is a note in massive font.>$B$BPROPERTY OF FRIZ FRAZZLESPARK$B$BPOWDERFUSE PORT$B$BWARNING: NOT for tampering. Do NOT open without supervision.$B$B<An additional note appears at the bottom of the label.>$B$BIf lost, return to Friz Frazzlespark. Powderfuse Port. Riverglades.",
[94931]="The boys up at Southern Watch do a good job keeping gnolls out for the most part. Every now and then a few sneak into the camp at night and cause a bit of trouble. They especially like to steal saw blades, which they likely use to make weapons out of the sharp metal.$B$BIf you could get some back for us, it'd be a big help. The gnolls have probably got 'em stashed away somewhere in their camps up in the hills to the west.",
[94946]="I had intended to be the first of us to step foot onto Azeroth, but recent events with the cult have changed my plans. As a result, I will be remaining here in Valanaar for a time. Fret not though, we have several mages awaiting our people's arrival in Dalaran. I'd encourage you to explore Azeroth while we set our affairs in order here. We will call upon agents such as yourself when you are needed.$B$BWhen you are ready, please proceed to the dock just outside this lodge and board the skycutter ship there.",
[94947]="It's a big world down here, and we need our people to start branching out to explore it. That's where you come in.$B$BThe Kirin Tor is a member of an \"Alliance\" of like-minded nations. The de-facto heart of this alliance is the city of Stormwind to the south. Elaadrin has asked me to find someone to travel to Stormwind and meet with the regent lord there, a human named Bolvar Fordragon.$B$BWhen you are ready, the Kirin Tor mages have set up a special portal for the High Order to use to access Stormwind.",
[94961]="<The gnoll pulls a bit of gold from his pocket and waves it at you.>$B$B$R, I offer trade! There is more where this came from. Help me get revenge, and I will show you!",
[94962]="Alright, so you got a few wins under your belt. So what?$B$BYou're a long way from becoming the champ, bub. But I tell ya what--I'll make sure this next battle ain't one you'll soon forget.$B$BHope you're ready for a surprise.",
[94963]="Come, $r. It is time to leave this place. If any try to stop us, we will tear them to shreds!$B$BOnce we are safe, I will take you to your reward.",
[94964]="Let's see if we can keep this crowd's excitement goin'.$B$BThis next contender ain't no joke.$B$BBest of luck to ya! See you soon, maybe.",
[94965]="Alright, so I'll place the treat and then you enter the ring and prepare for what's comin'.$B$BWhat? Why you lookin' at me like that? I said we're gonna feed her. What I may have forgotten to mention was that ol' Snufflesnout gets pretty riled up at the sight of her favorite treat.$B$BYou're in a bit of a sticky situation here, bub. Proving yourself to our ogre friends is of the utmost importance, but boy oh boy would I be nervous inflicting harm to Chubchob's precious companion.$B$BWell, off ya go!",
[94968]="Of the few that managed to infiltrate the cave, most have perished. It seems these Twilight have a foothold much larger than we thought. We will not stand by while these cultists continue to ravage these lands and make sacrifices of our allies. We end this now, $n.$B$BInfiltrate this stronghold, slaughter their forces and bring me proof of their leader's demise.",
[94969]="Don't ask. You wouldn't believe me if I told you.$B$BLet's just focus on getting me out of here! Oh, and you as well, of course.",
[94971]="One of the most important parts of a paladin's arsenal has always been their warhorse. These specially consecrated animals bear paladins and their arms into battle, and are as fearless and bold as the best of us.$B$BWhile our situation has changed, our need for steeds to bear us into battle has not. It's time that you had such a mount for yourself.",
[94972]="With their location revealed, it is likely that within this stronghold are secrets kept well hidden from those we have encountered thus far. It would be wise for us to locate and recover any information that may be of use to our fight against these cultists.$B$BSee what you can uncover, $n. I await your return.",
[94973]="<The moulding appears to be for a key.>",
[94974]="The moulding is crude and worn, but we may be able to fashion a key.$B$BIt may take some time to gather the components necessary. I'll keep these embers running hot while you gather the materials.",
[94975]="Our work here is not finished, $n. These cultists have inflicted unimaginable pain upon our allies and rendered these lands for their taking.$B$BWe will not tolerate these actions any longer.$B$BTo the north lies a hidden cave network, masked by the rugged terrain. Our scouts spoke of cultist movement under the veil of darkness.$B$BSeek out this cave and find where these cultists are hiding. It's time we deliver a message they won't soon forget.",
[94978]="Every hunter begins by learning the bond between beast and master. This is your first challenge. In time, you'll tame creatures from every corner of the world, but for now, start with our rivers and lakes on Zephras.$B$BTake this Taming Rod and seek out a Windsong Crawler.$B$BShow that you can earn its trust, and begin your path toward true mastery.",
[94979]="You've proven you can tame the river's crawler. Now it's time to test your skill on open ground. The plains of Zephras echo with the cries of the galestrider, a proud, winged hunter that runs like the wind.$B$BTake this Taming Rod and seek one out. Travel to the lowlands and earn its trust.$B$BShow you're ready for the trials yet to come.",
[94980]="<The moulding appears to be for a key.>",
[94981]="The moulding is rather crude, but we may be able to fashion a key with the right materials.$B$BI'll keep the embers running hot while you gather the necessary components.",
[94982]="Our scouts mentioned a network of caves to the northwest along the mountains, hidden by natural surroundings. Most who sought information from deep within have yet to return. I fear they may be lost.$B$BThose watching from a distance mentioned a Twilight presence moving in and out of the caves, often in darkness.$B$BLocate this stronghold. If it is what I think it is we must deliver a deathly blow to their leader. Only then may we continue our efforts to remove them from these lands.",
[94983]="The stories our scouts shared were quite horrid. I'll spare you the gruesome details. What we've discovered confirms previous reports of a cultist hideout.$B$BTo the north lies a cave, well hidden by its surroundings. This cave leads to... well, a place we've yet to infiltrate. We believe it's a foothold, nestled deep within the mountains.$B$BIt's time we repay the cultists for their actions against our allies.$B$BVenture north, seek out our enemies, and return to me with proof of their demise.",
[94984]="No matter our efforts, the Twilight forces persist. We've deduced they must be coming from somewhere else.$B$BWith the new pet you brought me, I was able to politely ask our dear Twilight Thrall if it knew anything about where its former masters were coming from. Of note was mention of shadow magics and an ogre by the name of Nar'gurk in a hidden stronghold north of Sunnyglade.$B$BSeek him out. Kill him and recover what you can. There must be something we can learn from these efforts.",
[94992]="<The horse bows its head in your direction then nudges its nose into your underarm. Wherever you go, it may follow.>",
[94997]="We mustn't linger. Take these to the keep at once.$B$BFind Ashe Amberhall. She may be a pain, but she's well respected in her field of study. Perhaps she can shed some light on what energies are contained within these objects.",
[94998]="Quite simple to dispel, really. Remnants of something, that's for sure. What, exactly, I do not know.$B$BWell, I'm afraid I've done all that I can. I'm sorry if you were expecting more from me, but... on second thought, the craftsmanship of these is quite unique. Perhaps they could be of some use.$B$BTake these to Melanie Sable. Tell her I sent you. Let her know they're safe.$B$BShe may have some use for them just yet.",
[94999]="Oh! Sorry, I didn't see you there.$B$BI was just putting together a little something for a friend of mine. Well... more of an acquaintance, really. Have you met Watcher Fredericks yet? He's stationed at Southern Watch just west of here.$B$BHe comes by the ranch on patrol every now and then. I thought it would be nice to give him a little something to show my appreciation.$B$BI'd deliver it myself, but I need to keep an eye on my little brother and tend to the ranch.$B$BI'm sure you understand.",
[95006]="<Orokai closes his eyes and becomes perfectly still as he communes with the branch. You can feel the stinging prickle of magic on your skin as he does so.>$B$BOh my, little mortal. The tales this branch has to tell...$B$BCome, let me show you.",
[95026]="Escapin' war don't mean we be safe here. Dem creatures to da east been plaguin' da area all dis time.$B$BMaybe you be ready for a challenge, eh?$B$BStrike 'em down. Ain't nobody gonna be missin' dem after all.",
[95027]="We always need more arrows for hunting and fighting, and for feathers, we use the white feathers of the Hyjal owl. They're naturally fluffy and soft, but I stiffen them up with a mixture designed to make them perfect for fletching.$B$BYou can get feathers from the owls, of course, but they also leave behind feathers in their nests, which you can find all over to the south of here.$B$BBring back a bundle of feathers, all right?",
[95033]="If you be gettin' tired of dem wide open plains, my old friend Uzer'i always be lookin' for help. He always be twistin' dem magics, but little do most o' dem people know he be quite da hunter too.$B$BIf you's interested, you can find him all da way out at Camp Mojache in Feralas.$B$BTell him ol' Tan'jani sent ya.",
[95034]="I think you should know that it wasn't actually the Gnolls who attacked us on the road.$B$BWe were actually attacked by a giant, wolf-like creature that I now know as a \"worgen\". It dispatched our guards and came for me, but Banon threw himself in its path. I managed to get a spell off which startled the creature, causing it to flee, but Banon was already badly bitten. He insisted I leave him there but I refused.$B$BWe were limping back here when the gnolls found us. What came next was terrifying...",
[95056]="NYI",
[95059]="Time for a special delivery.$B$BKnight Commander Demar Brant at Farholde is waiting for this. For some reason he always makes me say his full name. What an odd fella.$B$BAnywho, you can find him holed up in the keep southwest of here. Massive stone fortress. Ya can't miss it.",
[95062]="Time for a special delivery.$B$BOld Krom'rosh is waiting for this package over at Rog'mar just west of here.$B$BI suggest you get it to him quickly, but carefully. Why, you might ask? It's better to not ask questions.",
[95063]="Ok, listen up. You've showed quite a bit of prowess in the ring. You've managed to upset Chub'chob more than words can explain. Sure glad I ain't you right now.$B$BJust in case you was wonderin', I should remind you that your entry fee does not cover accidental death.$B$BIt's been great knowin' ya, but you're on your own from here on out, bub.$B$BBest of luck to ya.",
[95064]="The orcs have become an encroaching threat ever since their arrival. First, claiming the lands by the river and now their presence grows within the plains...$B$BI'll never understand their kind, nor do I care, truth be told, but I'll be damned if they think there's more ground to be taken.",
[95066]="The message we've delivered is clear.$B$BReturn to Brant within the keep and show him the report. I'm certain he'll be pleased with our progress.",
[95107]="One chief of the Deadwood, Deeproar, barks in the depths of their den. He was once of no burrow, and in a night of bad blood, he fell sway to their spells.$B$BNow, he feeds on their sour sap, with twice the cursed roar.$B$BGo. End his foul ways. Take his staff and bring it here, so I know he holds it no more.",
[95108]="With far sight, we have seen their den. Deadwood brew dark rites in their pots. They feed this foul mix to their young, so bad roots take. Then they learn to fight with vile ways.$B$BGo, stop this spread. Slay the dark ones and smash their stew.",
[95111]="In Tarren Mill there is a weaponsmith known as Ott. By all accounts he is an unremarkable smith, selling simple blades to travelers. I purchased a sword from him myself, and when I took it to the undercity for maintenance some time later, the smiths there were surprised at its quality. They assumed it came from a well-known master smith, but no, it was just Ott.$B$BI'd like to give this orc a chance to do something truly special. Take the materials to Ott in Tarren Mill and offer him the commission.",
[95118]="Murlocs, murlocs, murlocs! That's all I ever hear about; from the sailors, the fishermen, even my own kids! Everyone's on my case about 'em! They're a nuisance, I admit, but I got a port to run here!$B$BHelp a guy out, would ya? Kill a couple 'a those things and I'll make it worth your time.",
[95119]="You know the Eastsea crew? Real unsavory bunch, and that's coming from the guy running a place called \"Powderfuse Port\".$B$BThey're destructive, bloodthirsty, and, worst of all, cutting into my bottom line. They steal cargo, and sink ships, both of which end up costing me the big bucks!$B$BWe gotta take down their whole operation, starting with the ones closest to here. You can find 'em along the beaches to the north.",
[95120]="Sailors and swimmers beware! An especially aggressive murloc, nicknamed \"Old Rot-Chum\" by local fishermen, has been seen attacking rowboats and other small vessels in the waters to the south, near a collection of murloc-infested islands.$B$BA reward is being offered by Wharfmaster Whizzbuzz in exchange for proof of the creature's demise.",
[95121]="Welcome to Fimbo's cafe on the water! Today's menu is roasted boar, and roasted fish...same as every day...$B$BThis menu needs a shake up, badly. I've had my eye on a new seafood stew recipe, but I'm gonna need some fresh meat. A few murloc eyes and some crab meat oughta do.$B$BYou can find both along the beaches nearby. Can't beat some good ol' fashioned local ingredients!",
[95122]="Those Eastsea pirates you whacked, while dangerous, were just the small fries. They've got bigger, badder brothers in arms north of here. They ransacked Windstead--took all the plunder they could, then burned it to the ground.$B$BThey've gotta be stopped before their turf gets any farther inland. Thin out their ranks so that doesn't happen.",
[95123]="As much as I love seeing Eastsea heads roll, we also gotta take out their ships. Can't have 'em running off for reinforcements, now can we?$B$BI've got a plan for that, but we're gonna need some gunpowder. A LOT of it.$B$BThe pirates are probably storing some near the freshly-demolished Winstead to the north. See if you can get your hands on it. I'll fill you in on the rest later.",
[95124]="Now it's time to go after the big man himself: Admiral Lamora. Obviously, I want him dead, but I need a little something extra from him too.$B$BSeeing how all his plundering has been costing me a fortune, I figure it's only right that I recoup some losses.$B$BLamora's on one of the Eastsea's boats northeast of here. Find out which and where on it he's keeping his loot. Bring me whatever he's got. If it's locked up, he's likely got the key on him.",
[95125]="These are some truly fine materials, $c. You honor me by allowing me to forge this blade for you and I only hope that I can live up to your expectations.$B$BPlease, stand back so that I may begin the forging process.",
[95126]="Here's the blade. You said that a paladin named Trevan sent you? Please extend my thanks to him for this opportunity when you next see him. Go with honor, friend.",
[95140]="I see that you have your weapon now, $c. I pray that it will not fail you.$B$BThe locals tell me that Old Fire-Eye hunts in a large area south of here and you can generally find him near the gates to Gilneas. Find him, and use your new blade to end him. When it is done, return and you will have the gratitude of the Windshapers.",
[95141]="Far to the northeast beyond Stonard lies an embattled land along the eastern coast known as the Riverglades.$B$BMany have sought to lay claim to these lands, but few have succeeded. There is one, however, whose experience battling our enemies proved enough to settle a small outpost known as Rog'mar. Through countless attacks, it still remains.$B$BAs ruthless as Krom'rosh may be, his will has served our allies greatly. If it's battle you seek, head northeast to seek out this old friend of ours.",
[95143]="I've been watching you, $n. You handle yourself well out here. Perhaps you'd be interested in helping me locate my brother, Tan'jani.$B$BHe was always searching for something--for what I do not know. I received two messages since he left. The first from another traveler, letting me know he'd run into Tan'jani somewhere south of Loch Modan. The second was a bloodstained letter mentioning Riverglades and somewhere called Rog'mar, even further south. The rest was illegible.$B$BThink you can locate him for me?",
[95144]="Hey, bub. Got a package that needs to go to an old friend of mine. Whatever you do--$B$BDO NOT OPEN THE PACKAGE!$B$BTake this--carefully--to Friz Frazzlespark across the seas over to our sister port in the Riverglades. And before you ask, no I would not suggest swimming. Didn't work out so well for the last guy. Oh, and don't tilt it, shake it, or make any sudden movements.$B$BI recommend heading east to Steamwheedle Port. The ship from there usually provides safe passage.$B$BBest of luck to ya!",
[95147]="You... where did you come from? You shouldn't be here!$B$B<Bolain struggles through the pain--bruised, battered, and a disease-ridden bite wound to his leg.>$B$BTake this to Dalton. Head north up the road and east where the plains open wider than this gash in my damn leg. I'd tell you to tell him he was right, but I won't give him that satisfaction... at least not until after I'm dead.$B$BI hate these damn hills!",
[95148]="As much as I'd like to deliver the blood-soaked message to the knight commander himself, I'd also like to keep my post. I've cleaned it up a bit so it's less... well, bloody.$B$BGiven the recent gnoll uprisings, I'm afraid the task of delivering the news falls upon you.",
[95156]="Our training dummies are starting to show significant wear and tear. If we don't fix them up soon I worry our recruits may be unprepared for battle.$B$BIf you hadn't seen it on your way in, there's a small farmstead just outside the keep run by a man by the name of Wheeler. He may have a few extra bushels of hay he'd be willing to part with.$B$BI'll see to it he's compensated if he's able to spare supplies for our efforts.",
[95162]="With so little land not claimed by the humans or Twilight's Hammer, this ranch is one of our very few sources of food. Ogres aren't much in the way of farmers, but they love a good paletusk roast, and have agreed to let me stay so long as the meat keeps coming.$B$BAs our war advances, the demand for food is only ever increasing. Now I hardly have enough food to keep these ogres from looking at me like I'm their next meal.$B$BIf we want to have enough meat for Rog'mar, I'll need your help with the harvest.",
[95163]="As you can see, there are more pigs strewn about the valley than there are in their pens. Gorgegut has been less than an ideal farmhand, but he keeps the humans away.$B$BSome of the little ones have escaped across the river. They're still too small to be harvested out in the field so we need to return them here. Take this stick and give them a good swat! That should send them scampering back to their pens.",
[95165]="So, here's how we're gonna sink those ships.$B$BI can use that gunpowder you stole and make timed charges. All you've gotta do is hop on each of the Eastsea's boats, and plant one charge in the hull of each. Look for a spot near their cannons, that gunpowder'll make our explosives even more powerful. Once the charges are set, get outta there, and I'll hit the detonator!$B$BThe elegance of the plan is in its simplicity, don't ya think?",
[95181]="Quiet down!$B$B<Azka snaps, adjusting her gaze in your direction.>$B$BI'll have your head before you give away my position to the cultists.$B$BWatch your step and keep a low tone when traveling through these hills. Otherwise I'll be sending a report to Krom'rosh that another of our own has been taken.$B$BNow take this and get out of here quickly... and quietly! Krom'rosh is waiting on this report. You can find him and the others at the outpost inland to the east.",
[95183]="You want ogre weapon? Me know no. You small. Can't hold good.$B$BYou bring Hamur more rocks, me make you tiny weapon. Good for tiny creature.$B$BFind good rocks for good weapon. Hamur has discerning eye. Not just any rock will do. Find rocks near river outside Bolder'ok.",
[95184]="The rigors of training for battle are one thing, but these trainees don't yet understand the difference between a training sword and the well-kept blade of a seasoned veteran.$B$BI think it's time we show our recruits how a sharpened blade can be the difference between victory and death.$B$BIf you can find us a few sharpening stones, we'll put them to good use. There are certain craftsmen known to study this trade. I'd suggest starting there.",
[95194]="Greetings, $n. There's a matter that SI:7 could use your help with. Our man on Theramore Isle tells us that Jaina Proudmoore's marines just brought in a man found washed up on the shore.$B$BNormally this wouldn't be of much interest to us but it seems that this man told the marines that he was none other than the king of Stormwind, Varian Wrynn. Go to Theramore and meet a dwarf named Sully at the inn. He's expecting you and will give you instructions when you arrive.$B$BFind out what's going on.",
[95196]="Listen up. I'm going to walk out that door behind you. Yer gonna wait until I'm good and gone, and then yer gonna meet me behind the graveyard outside o' town. Ensure yer not followed.",
[95198]="Take this. It's a handy bit o' glamour that the mages back home put together to make a quick disguise. It'll make you look like a Kul Tiras Marine which should do nicely for this mission.$B$BSneak in to the tower and do yer best to listen for any mention of the man that washed up on the beach. I warn you though, do not get too close to Jaina. She will see right through this disguise.$B$BCome back and see me if you lose your disguise, I'll set you up with a new one.",
[95217]="So you're looking to learn the blacksmith's trade? Maybe we can help each other.$B$BThe supply shipment's late, and I need materials for some repairs around the camp. If you get me what I need, I'll teach you some of my techniques. Sound fair?",
[95218]="The Light has forsaken me. A purpose served, and now everything... gone...$B$BIt's just a matter of time until the light turns to darkness.$B$BI fought against the demons and scourge forces with a ferocity I did not know the Light could produce... and yet, I sit here, talking to you, feeling... well, I can't quite put it into words. Some reclaim their purpose after loss, yet I struggle... After all, I am only who I am.$B$BNow, unless the commander has one last call to action, I await what comes next.",
[95219]="Got another job for ya, kiddo. How do you feel about traveling the world?$B$BThis here is some of the finest port you ever laid eyes on. Trouble is, it's gotta go quite the distance to one of my customers all the way over to Feathermoon Stronghold in Feralas. When you've reached trees taller than you've ever seen before, you know you've reached the spot.$B$BOne of my guys packed it airtight but there's no telling what might set it off, so handle with care, okay bub?",
[95248]="You cut down so many of da Scourge dat we finally have a little safety. For dat, we be thankful.$B$BOne more thing. We know dat there are druids at da summit. Dey protect da great tree and da well.$B$BHow come dey never helped us?$B$BWe been here five years! Why did dey never even send a message to anyone about us? Let someone know dat we still here, we still alive!",
[95254]="Calling all anglers!$B$BI'm in the market for some crab meat. Not just the usual shreds either, I'm talking whole claw. I've seen a big one crawling around under the docks, stealing bait and cutting lines.$B$BI'll pay a reward to anyone who brings me that thing's pincer. You'll also get a helping of the dish I whip up.$B$B-- Fimbo Greasemitz",
[95260]="The hide is painted with broad strokes of fish guts and squid ink. It appears to depict some kind of sea monster, rising up from the waves, with a long neck. What could this beast be?$B$BThe nearest port is Powderfuse Port. If this monster is real, and lurks these waters, a sailor there has surely seen it.",
[95261]="That monster...with the long neck, just like you said. I've seen 'im around those islands -- out on my boat. I tried <hic> tellin' folks, but ohh nooo, you can't <hic> believe ol' Argo. He's just some...some...drunkard fisherman! Makin' up stories!$B$BWe'll show 'em...soon as I get some bait...$B$BHey! Quit standin' around! I'm gonna need entrails, a LOT of 'em. Any beast from around here. The smellier <hic> the better. I'm also gonna need some Rotflesh mushrooms. Those grow in that cave by Windstead.",
[95262]="Can't say I've ever thought much about Alcaz. Near as I can tell, it's an abandoned outpost from the third war of little significance. Never heard nuthin' about a prison there.$B$BWell, there's nothing for it--we've got to get you in there and see what you can see, especially if there's a chance that the king is there.",
[95263]="<The King is dead--killed in an escape attempt just before the Naga attacked. This is devastating news and will shake Stormwind to its core. You need to return to Sully and tell him what you've learned as quickly as possible.>",
[95264]="Shaw needs to know as soon as possible. Head back to Stormwind and deliver the news. Please, I beg ye, tell no one else. This could be disastrous for Stormwind and it needs to be handled delicately.",
[95267]="The last part's <hic> easy...just take that big ball 'a guts, aaand chuck it in the water! Er...not here though...that'd be a disaster.$B$BGo to those <hic> murloc islands, where ya found the drawing. Look for fresh wreckage in the water. That's where you gotta throw the bait.$B$BSoon as that thing sticks its head up, chop it off! We'll make a decoration of it...for the boat!",
[95273]="Now that we know Deadwood don't foul the water outright with their presence, we can take this sample and cast our wards with sound will. We've heard there is a pool of the mountain's tears within their den.$B$BTravel with force and pour this water into the pool deep in Deadwood Den.$B$BReturn to us when you have learned what secrets the dark depths hold.",
[95278]="The threat is greater than we thought. Rog'mar must be warned.$B$BDo not stop for anyone on your path.",
[95283]="Lok-tar, $n. I find myself in need of assistance with a serious matter.$B$BSome time ago we dispatched a contingent of Kor'kron Elite to Dustwallow Marsh on a special mission. The problem is, we are far past their scheduled check-in with no word from them.$B$BHead down to Brackenwall Village in Dustwallow Marsh and speak with an orc named Nazeer Bloodspike. No one is more knowledgeable about the state of Dustwallow than he. Find out what you can.",
[95284]="A small force of Kor'kron soldiers passed through here a few days ago. Never told me why they were here, and I didn't ask. They bought supplies, took a bit of rest, then moved on.$B$BThe Kor'kron are the elite of the elite and tougher than elekk hooves, but I can't help feeling that something went wrong.$B$BI did overhear one of them mention \"the island\", and there's an island called Alcaz just off the coast. It's a really nasty place. Get some friends and look into what befell these Kor'kron.",
[95285]="<Sergeant Ulka struggles to sit up to speak with you. You offer your hand in aid, but she merely swats it away.>$B$BAlright recruit... let's get you caught up.",
[95288]="You look like you're in the habit of doing whatever other people tell ya. I like that in a lackey. With a little trainin' you could be a great asset. Let's put that to the test.$B$BRecently some of those Eastsea pirates made off with a shipment of MY stolen goods. That's bad sportsmanship. I stole them first!$B$BLesson one, lackey. Never backstab a backstabber. Go show them that they messed with the wrong goblin and take back my stuff. With force, preferably.",
[95293]="Those goods you procured from the Eastsea pirates were supposed to be shipped directly to me. That means ol' Bentcoin thinks he can muscle in on my turf. Looks like he's fixin' to start a trade war. We, however, are civilized people.$B$BLesson two, lackey. We don't need to stoop to their level. Take this crate I made 'specially for the good captain. You'll find him on his ship along the Eastwind Shore. He deserves a reward for his shrewd negotiatin' tactics.",
[95294]="Friz sure knows how to get her point across. Well, you won't hear any objections from me. The Eastsea pirates won't interfere with her business. In exchange, maybe we can come to an arrangement. Pirating's a little difficult when you've got a scorned goblin sending marauding adventurers after you all day.$B$BRun along back to your master, $c. Let Friz know there's a new captain in charge, and he foresees a profitable relationship in our future.",
[95295]="Ya did good with those pirates, lackey. But here's a lesson for ya you may want to remember. What some may call a pirate, others call a freebooter. And you can't spell freebooter without free booty. And there's no better place for free booty than Booty Bay!$B$B<Friz waits for your reply.>$B$BKeep up with me here, kid. I'm sayin' I need you to go to Booty Bay to meet with my contact. He gets goods from the local pirates there-- err, freebooters. Look, just go find Ruzzgot. He'll explain the rest.",
[95296]="Sounds like you're ready for your next lesson, champ. I got some negotiatin' of my own to do here in town, so I need you to run a few errands for me while I'm busy.$B$BAll I need you to do is take the next ship over there by the docks and deliver this crate to my associate in Steamwheedle Port.$B$BDon't gimme that look. It'll be plenty excitin', I'm sure. Gettin' a goblin to pay his dues is much harder than roughin' up the local riffraff, not to mention gettin' through customs. You'll figure it out.",
[95309]="Your orders are simple-- Go into the dungeons beneath the keep and find Commander Folkar. Free him if he lives, and learn what you can about what in the twisting nether is going on here.$B$BThere's an army waiting for you down there and you won't survive on your own. I hope you have allies... preferably strong ones.",
[95312]="I don't have Friz's money. Well, I had her money, but I bet it all on ol' Slugjaw here in Fizbuz's arena in Gadgetzan.$B$BDon't gimme that look. It was a sound investment. I won big! I just haven't had a chance to collect my winnin's yet. If you're Friz's new errand $Gboy:girl;, why don't you go get it for me? I got a bad back, you know.$B$BHey, you don't want to go back to your boss empty handed, do ya? Gadgetzan is just west of here. You can't miss it.",
[95314]="Before the Scourge invasion, the reclusive village of Shadowvale was known for its Whispering Elixir. Distilled from herbs found only in Tyr's Fall, the elixir was sought by apothecaries, mystics, and poisoners alike even after being banned in the city.$B$BI've had requests from a number of buyers eager to get their hands on some elixir. Travel to the ruins of Shadowvale deep in the Whispering Forest to the west. I'm prepared to offer significant compensation if you can recover some bottles for me.",
[95315]="Word from one of our scouts suggests a large force of enemies amassing to the far, far south, well beyond the Wetlands.$B$BEven more curious is there appears to be an alliance settlement out there. Farholde? The name sounds familiar.$B$BLet's not wait on this. Best to begin the conversation before it's too late. We're dealing with enough here as it is.$B$BTake this correspondence and deliver it to whoever claims to be the leader of this detachment.",
[95316]="Alright dirtwalker, you may have noticed the combination of pinecones and fel-infused slime is quite disgusting, if you ask me. It is, however, also very dangerous-- which is just what we need!$B$BTake these pinecones and carefully--I repeat, carefully--make your way to the nearby warlock encampment. Once there, use these items to wreak havoc upon their precious workstations.$B$BI am sure the results will be amusing for you to watch firsthand! This should certainly slow them down.",
[95317]="Listen, $c. There have been some awfully noisy visitors just up the mountain. They are tainting the land with their foul demon magic and experimenting with piles of ash. It's high time we investigate.$B$BBy we, I mean you.$B$BI want you to poke around and investigate their camp! See if you can bring me some notes on what our mysterious fel 'friends' have been up to. Surely with egos that large they've written something we can utilize. Perhaps they are carrying something on their person?",
[95318]="So in order to really disrupt operations here and get me out of this cage, we're going to have to kill four very powerful mortals. This cage has demonic wards on it that won't be dispelled until all four are dead, and that key can't be used until the wards are down.$B$BLook, you seem like |5$r that can hold your own but I'm going to need a bit more convincing that you can actually take on these stupid warlocks before I give you any good info.$B$BLike killing a ton of these warlocks for starters. Easy, no?",
[95319]="Listen, I know you can smell the fel blood pools behind me and I'm sure you've seen the crystals that grow out of them. These crystals have special properties from the ashes of Archimonde that rain down on this side of the hill.$B$BSomething about how they are formed makes them especially good at draining fel energies, which is a big problem for someone like me, but they can still have their uses.$B$BI want you to gather some for me. Try and get a few kinds. I'll know what I need when I see it.",
[95320]="There is a caged demon just up the road near the entrance of the demon caster encampment that has been making a great deal of fuss.$B$BAll this ranting and raving about imprisonment and freedom. Something about scorching bones and revenge?$B$B<The crow leans in and gives you a mischievous look. As if to emphasize, she then dangles an iron key in one of her talons.>$B$BLet's see if we can't make a deal with our little 'friend' and see what he knows about these nasty demon casters.",
[95321]="Tazzik sent you to collect his winnings? That's a joke, right? His slackjaw champion didn't even last two minutes in the arena! That loser didn't earn a single copper.$B$BIt's none of my business, pal, but if I were you I'd skedaddle back to Steamwheedle Port. While you're standin' here talkin' to me, that little rat Tazzik is probably tryin' to hop the next ship outta here.",
[95322]="Your timin' couldn't be better, friend. I was just on my way to collect my shipment from the Bloodsail Buccaneers. They're good friends of mine. Always happy to supply anything Friz is willin' to pay for.$B$BBut, ahem, just in case, it couldn't hurt for you to be my liaison. A good caravaneer knows it doesn't hurt to show off a little muscle. Just as a deterrent, of course.$B$BThey said they left my stuff in a chest on the hill outside of town for safekeepin'. Why don't you take a look for me, eh?",
[95325]="I already spent good coin on that crate. We ain't just going to let them have it!$B$BYou want your shipment? Go to the Venture Co's camp up north and find out who's responsible for this backstabbin'! This ain't about money anymore, $n. This is about justice! And maybe a little about the money.",
[95326]="<The ledger contains a log of each of Ruzzgot's deliveries. The final note marks the heist a success and Ruzzgot's valuables collected by a nearby Venture Co. agent. The goods must still be with him.>",
[95327]="Looks like a deal's a deal. The Venture Co. got their comeuppance, Friz gets her loot, and everybody's happy. Overall a pretty smooth transaction if I do say so myself.$B$BNow scram, I got another shipment comin' in soon from some Southsea Pirates.",
[95328]="Against your better judgement you scrape up and collect the squirming remains of the beast. Someone in Undercity might have a use for them.",
[95329]="There is a watch tower overlooking the plains to the north. It serves as an observation point to track any motion of the Horde's forces.$B$BThe watcher stationed there is named Cornelius. Speak to him and get a status report. He is all alone out there, so I like to check on him with some regularity. Fair warning, he can be a bit...taciturn. It's why he was assigned such a remote post in the first place.",
[95330]="My husband and I have a farm north of here. I come to Farholde after each harvest to sell what we grow. In good seasons, I like to set aside whatever we don't sell to give to folks who need a little pick-me-up. Gotta take care of your neighbors, I say.$B$BThere's a logging camp north of our farm, right on the river. I'm sure those boys could use some fruits and vegetables to give 'em some variety in their diet.$B$BIf you're heading that way, could you give this to the foreman there? Name's Halligan Turner.",
[95349]="The recent events with the cult have delayed my plans to travel to Azeroth and I must remain here in Valanaar for a time. You and a handful of other Windshapers will be our vanguard instead. Alaana Stormwalker will be waiting to receive our Windshapers upon arrival in Mulgore, and I'd encourage you to explore Azeroth while we finish our business here. We will join you soon.$B$BWhen you are ready, please proceed to the dock just outside this lodge and board the skycutter ship there.$B$BBanu-Alah, $n.",
[95350]="It's a big world down here, and our new allies are the key to our survival.$B$BThe Earthen Ring is a member of the \"Horde\", a proud collection of like-minded peoples. The nearby city of Thunder Bluff is a part of the Horde, and further to the east lies the capital of Orgrimmar.$B$BSeek out the flight master in the center of Thunder Bluff. They will fly you to Orgrimmar where you will make contact with the Horde warchief--Thrall, on behalf of the Windshapers. Winds guide you, $n.",
[95378]="It is time to cut off the heads of this hydra, if you catch my meaning.$B$BThere are three leaders who need to be killed in order to slow the operations here. Conveniently, they also need to be slain to remove the wards on my cage.$B$BTyaeha can be found in the House of Diseases by the creepy tree. Dazka is in the Alchemist ward with all the potions, and that fool Frezzlie is undoubtedly next to the slime pits along the northern ridge of the encampment.$B$BGo slay them and bring me their bones!",
[95379]="Brashann Grimdark, Master of Vessels.$B$B<Felflick's mouth curls into a snarl.>$B$BHe was the one to subjugate me at the summit. HE is the reason I am here in the first place.$B$BHis work with these fel-ash crystals are the backbone of this operation. He's been obsessively experimenting with anchoring souls in these crystals and his work has not gone unnoticed by those Blackthorne creeps.$B$BUse this pristine crystal to drain his power, then put an end to him and bring me his soulstone.",
[95380]="Listen here, $c. It seems we're in quite the sticky situation. I knew those blasted demon casters were up to no good, but this is far worse than I had expected.$B$BGood thing I have an idea!$B$BFor this to work I will need fel-slime from the surrounding slime creatures that can be found in the fel blood pools behind me. Not the bones or bits, just the slime! Make sure you wipe your hands after handling it. It seems to be corrosive.$B$BNot to fear, I'm sure you'll find a way to bring it back to me.",
[95383]="<Wharfmaster Steamfizzle inspects the coin you offered him.>$B$BWhoa-ho! Ol' Friz sure is training the new generation right. Apologies for the delay, $Gsir:ma'am;. You're here to deliver a crate to someone in town, right? I don't know anythin' about that, but if I did, I'd go talk with Tazzik on the dock. He seems to be interested in things like that.$B$BBut be quick about it though, yeah? Don't need folks gettin' the wrong idea, ya know.",
[95384]="<The strange symbols on the magical scroll confound you. Though you do not speak the language recorded, you don't sense any particularly volatile forces within. Perhaps a collector of odd magics would find some use for the scroll.>",
[95385]="<Faint magic emanates from the scrap of scroll. The language is unfamiliar, though you intuit that it is not dangerous. Most would find the parchment useless, but there may be a unique collector that may find some use out of it.>",
[95417]="Clubtoe see friends go. Some no come back. Some come back purple. Dat weird. Purple ones no act like friends no more.$B$BWhere others go? Why they no come back? Make Clubtoe think.$B$BYou hit hard. Maybe you go find friends in cave? Maybe you turn purple. Dat weird too.",
[95418]="Me done with Twilight. Clubtoe free ogre now.$B$BMe go find Clugfist. He biggestest ogre Clubtoe ever see. He leave Twilight. Take many friends with him. It Clubtoe's turn. Me join free ogres. They go to the hills. Clubtoe miss hills. No more smashing rocks. Maybe you come sometime?$B$BMe stay here till coast is clear. You take Chogg'Zac's heads back to friends. Well. Maybe one head. Me get one too. Fair trade.",
[95420]="Clearly these wayward ogres are no friends to the Twilight's Hammer. We orcs have an honored history fighting alongside ogres, and it may be time to call upon those old alliances again. And this head may be the key.$B$BThere have been reports of ogre activity in the hills far to the north. If this Clubtoe is to be believed, that must be where this clan calls home. Go to their stronghold and offer this trophy as a token of our friendship. With luck, they will listen to your proposal before they step on you.",
[95424]="Here ogres value strength and blood.$B$BWeak ones leave Bolder'ok. Go back to Twilight's Hammer.$B$BYou no big. Maybe you strong. Show Clugfist strength and smash weak ogres. If tiny creature can.",
[95425]="Klunk once Clugfist's greatest champion. Him strong. Me give Klunk mighty weapon.$B$BBut Clugfist wrong. Klunk weak like others. He leave Bolder'ok. Return to Twilight's Hammer. Take ogres with him to cave east to water. Take mighty weapon with him!$B$BThat Clugfist weapon! Bash Klunk's skull and take back Skullbasher. He nobody's champion!",
[95426]="Supply delivery to this area is no easy feat. All sorts of unscrupulous characters surround us in all directions, each seeking their own piece of the pie.$B$BNow, with that said, perhaps this is an opportunity to slow Rog'mar's growth. What do you say to throwing a little wrench in our orc friends' plans?$B$BHead north of Rog'mar to their training grounds and steal their supply shipments. The recovery time alone ensures our forces remain battle ready while theirs... well, you see where this is going.",
[95427]="Clubtoe friends... dead? Why?$B$BThis Chogg'Zac fault! Dey say they make ogres strong! They lie!!$B$BNo more smashing rocks! Tiny creature help Clubtoe smash Chogg'zac stupid heads instead!",
[95428]="Little $r smash Twilight good. Maybe your Horde stronger than Clugfist think.$B$BYou free to stay in Bolder'ok. For now.$B$BTell other tinies we spill blood again soon.",
[95431]="As I've shadowed our enemy's movements, I have discovered a weakness among their ranks. Ogre dissidents have begun to rebel, seeking the same freedom as their Bolder'ok kin. Word of your deeds has spread. We must exploit this.$B$BI spied a Bolder'ok warrior heading to the caves west of here in search of his brothers and sisters. Find him, and join his efforts to rally his people.",
[95432]="When Crag'rog hear $r-ling free ogres, Crag'og want free ogres too.$B$BWith tiny $c here, we smash Twilight together. Break them bones. Make them scream. Free ogres! Then be home in time for stew.",
[95433]="When Clugfist leave Twilight, one ogre stand in way. Morg.$B$BMorg massive ogre. Nearly as massive as Clugfist. But not massivest. He need tinies to protect him. Clugfist never got fair fight. Now WE no fight fair.$B$BFind Morg. Bring many tinies with you. Kill him. Take mace back to Clugfist. Then Twilight know they challenge us no more!",
[95454]="My good axe arm is broken and most of my elites are dead. The honor of the Kor'kron rests with you now.$B$BWe were sent here to extract a prisoner, but not just any prisoner... We are here for the King of Stormwind, Varian Wrynn. We intercepted information that he was being held here and our Warchief commanded us to bring him back to Orgrimmar alive. The presence of black dragons... complicates things.$B$BI need you to press on and find Wrynn. I will wait for you here while you search for him.",
[95472]="I'm tellin' ya, I can't pay Friz back! I got nothin' left but the shirt off my back!$B$BWhy are you lookin' at me like that...",
[95483]="Thrall needs to know what happened here. I will meet up with Ulka and see to it that he is fit to travel before returning to Orgrimmar, so I am trusting you to bring this information to the warchief in my stead.$B$BGo now, soldier of the Horde. Tell our warchief what fate befell Varian Wrynn.",
[95494]="I need someone with a strong sword arm and some extra time on their hands to help me gather some lion hides. It stings my pride to ask a stranger for this aid, but I took an injury to my leg recently. Until I heal, I'm in no shape to go hunting myself but I have obligations to keep.$B$BThe big ones in this area generally have the best hides, so start with those first.",
[95495]="These hides are bound for a tanner who I often trade with. He is something of a hermit and he lives alone on the top of the ridge behind me. Climbing up a steep hillside isn't something I can manage easily right now so I'd be in your debt if you could make this delivery for me.$B$BOh, and about this tanner's... appearance. You need not be alarmed. In spite of his looks, he is no threat. I swear this is true.",
[95507]="While you are out there, it would be of great help to me if you could check on my traps for me. I've got them strewn all over the valley.$B$BBring back any small game that I've caught. Keep your eye out for the other wildlife, though. This area can be dangerous if you aren't paying attention.",
[95508]="Yes, I used to be a member of the Kul Tiras navy. After Lord Admiral took Theramore and started his campaign in Durotar, I had... \"objections\" to his methods. Particularly the methods involving executing civilians.$B$BThere's more to the story but... wait... what's that?$B$BThere's a group of men coming up the ridge!",
[95511]="Greetings, friend! I see today is a big day indeed; today you will bond with your first saber.$B$BAs you may or may not know these sabers are fiercely intelligent and extremely loyal to their bonded rider. You won't find a more noble and steadfast companion. As such, you have an important choice to make. You and your saber will traverse the world together, so choose wisely! Fear not, whatever choice you make will be the correct one.$B$BGo, examine the sabers and return to me when you have made your choice.",
[95534]="<The note is singed in places, but is still readable.>$B$BRumor has it those old bellows have a mind of their own, springing to life when no one is watching. I don't care if it's a ghost story, you'd better get to the bottom of it before I return.$B$BThere's great power in Strahnbrad, I know it.$B$B< The rest of the note is singed and torn, as if burnt by fire magic. >",
[95561]="<The loud cries of baby Dawnbright echo through Farholde Keep. Tessa looks at you with a tired smile.>$B$BOh, hello there adventurer. Sorry for the noise. Little Emma here seems to be quite fussy today, but I'm not sure why. Maybe some food will help.$B$BDo you think you could help me find something for her to eat? My husband stepped out to get some supplies so my hands are a little too full to get them myself. If you could find a few apples around here I could make a lovely mash for her.",
[95562]="I have a confession to make. Lady Amberhall did send me to collect those samples, but in truth I volunteered. Sunnyglade was my home before the war took it from me, and I could not rest knowing monsters still taint it. Be it horde or Twilight.$B$BThere is no victory here by learning from them. There's nothing to learn. They're beasts, plain and simple, and should be put down like beasts.$B$BWe must slay their master at the bottom of this cave and bring an end to this. Surely my mistress will understand.",
[95568]="You have arrived on Mount Hyjal at a time of changes, stranger.$B$BYou may have seen that the landscape is scarred by the old war and tainted by fel energies. For Hyjal to survive, nature must bloom again.$B$BIf you are willing to help me gather seeds from some of the untainted plants, I would be grateful. Many flowers grow in the wild lands east of here. Look for small red or yellow flowers.",
[95569]="The owls are under threat by the fel corruption that afflicts the mountainside, and the creatures poisoned and enraged by those energies. Many owls have abandoned their nests for safer places higher up the mountain. Others have fallen in defense of their young.$B$BFor the owls to have a future, their eggs must be protected and their fledglings nurtured. Bring the abandoned eggs to me. You may find eggs in abandoned nests at the base of trees north and east of here.",
[95599]="<The key is covered in a thick layer of rust, suggesting that the key has been underwater for a significant amount of time.$B$BThere must be a matching lock somewhere nearby to use it on but you'll have to search for it. Perhaps the pool of water to the southwest of this camp might be a good place to start?>",
[95601]="<This dead ogre must be one of the friends Clubtoe was looking for. The Twilight's Hammer seem to be conducting rituals on their members, empowering some and killing more.$B$BThese ritualists and their monstrosities must be stopped before they spread.>",
[95602]="Me hate smashing rock. All day me smash. Chogg'Zac say so. He big boss. Say we smash tinies, but now we work for tinies. That stupid.$B$BWhy smash rock? Me no know. Find shiny light in rocks. Chogg'Zac like shiny, me guess. Are you here for shiny light too? Others won't like that. They really like light. They draw pictures with it.$B$BClubtoe not get it. Light make Clubtoe feel sick. Me hate light. Me want SMASH shiny pictures! But Chogg'Zac be mad. Squish Clubtoe. That bad. But someone should.",
[95603]="Since brother Lowley and I began serving Farholde in a more secular capacity, the church here has fallen into disuse. I'd like to think that once the fighting is over, we will be able to bring the Light back to this place. Although, I fear that may not be for a long while...$B$BStill, we need to keep the church in working order, in the hope that day will come.$B$BTo that end, a colony of bats has taken to roosting in the upper stories of the church. It would be a great help if you could remove them.",
[95611]="One cannot take without giving in return. This is the cycle of life.$B$BYou have done well, $n. Thanks to your efforts, the wildlife on the mountain will continue to thrive.$B$BNow, it is time we show our respect for these lands by offering the unused remains back to the ground.$B$BTake this bundle and visit the shrine to the west. You shall recognize it as a simple pair of standing stones. Return to me once the ritual is complete.",
[95613]="While we no longer hold service at the church, I feel it important to keep the candles lit on the graves of our fallen in the church's crypt. To me, keeping the candle's flame alive is a symbol that they are not forgotten and their sacrifices were not in vain.$B$BIf you would, bring me candles so that I might continue this ritual. It would mean a great deal to me.$B$BIf you're not sure where to find them, speak with Marla in the house just outside of the church. She's a friend and may have some to spare.",
[95615]="If you don't mind, I'd like you to do the honor of lighting these memorial candles. Go to the cemetery just outside and place a fresh candle wherever you see one that's gone out.$B$BSuch a task is a far cry from the excitement of your other adventures, I'm sure. Think of this as an opportunity for service and reflection--a quiet moment to acknowledge those who left this world before us, so that we might carry on and make it a better place.",
[95621]="This morning I spotted a group of humans searching for something in the valley below. I managed to use my rifle's scope for a better look, and it was clear that they were soldiers sporting the livery of Kul Tiras.$B$BIf you'd be willing to take work from me, travel to where these soldiers made camp near the wrecked caravan to the south. Kill any you find and try to learn why they are here.",
[95642]="You there! Thank the light you've come. Did Amberhall send you to find me?$B$BNo? Figures as much. Ashe Amberhall sent me down here to investigate the Twilight's Hammer. As you can see, they are digging for something within the Riverglades, but I need a sample of their witchcraft to figure out what.$B$BIt's imperative Farholde gets those samples. Please, $c. Take this catalyst. It's enchanted to absorb the powers of the cult. Runes, cultists, it doesn't matter. Just hold it aloft and it will do the rest.",
[95643]="As Lady Amberhall's apprentice in the dark arts, I may not look it but I'm usually quite capable of handling things on my own. I did not, however, anticipate an entire cave of void-infused ogres.$B$BIf you managed to get all the way down here without being captured, you must be powerful yourself. I was not so lucky with those ogres and their masters roaming about. Do the world a favor and kill the hideous beasts. Nothing good comes from a fanatic with a purpose, empowered or otherwise.",
[95737]="From time to time, I correspond with others in my craft--herbalists or eccentrics who study rare plants and local oddities. We trade discoveries, and sometimes warnings of what lies ahead.$B$BOne alchemist in the Wetlands wrote of an excavation team her husband was part of, uncovering signs of a long-lost primordial grass... but she never sent word of its abundance or accessibility.$B$BIf you can, check on Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor.",
[95748]="This is odd. This piece of the tablet you have brought me refers to the lost city of I'lalai as if it is a massive sprawling civilization. But the ruins off of the reef are not large enough to be something of that size.$B$B$n, to the north of the Vile Reef there is an ancient troll ruin on the hills along the coast. A tablet that contains legends of the lost troll city is within. I wish to study this legend further.$B$BTake this hide and charcoal to create a rubbing of this tablet, then return to me.",
[95753]="<The totem pulses with wild magic. The image of a ghostly wolf appears in your mind, beckoning you.$B$BIt appears to be offering you a challenge.$B$BAnother totem--a twin to the one that your hand now rests upon, appears in the distance just beyond the large sun-bleached skeleton nearby.>",
[95766]="The cycle of renewal has finally begun. The ancients... shall rise again, and the power of the natural world take its course... to bloom.$B$BYou... have helped us tip the scales in nature's favor. Perhaps... we can yet make a larger impact... on a more dire situation.$B$BHead west... where the land itself is ashen... and you may find an entity who can help. She may look like just a small bird... but her power is great.",
[95769]="Every day be a challenge when you living rough like we do! Takes a toll on your tools, your clothes, your whole life. Good thing it can't take our spirit!$B$BWe be really hurting from our clothes and blankets wearing out. You do some tailoring, right? So maybe you can bring me some Bolts of Runecloth and I can fix a few holes?",
[95770]="After rereading the legend, it doesn't seem like we are in the wrong place for the lost city, but perhaps there is yet some detail that has been overlooked.$B$BIn my younger years I used to dive in the Vile Reef ruins, but that was before the murlocs settled there. If memory serves there was a cavern there.$B$BI have heard that there are now naga gathering in that region, which is unusual. I want to know what has lured them there.$B$BGo and explore just west of the Vile Reef and return to me with any news.",
[95773]="$C, your arrival is timely. I have just received new reports of naga activity just off of our coast. They seem to be swarming around some old troll ruins near the ocean floor.$B$BWe are already stretched thin defending from the local Bloodscalp and ogres ransacking our caravans. We cannot afford a surprise attack from the sea.$B$BGo and slay as many as you are able, and bring me their tridents as proof of your success.",
[95774]="The healer who saved me could not save her, and she has died in battle. Her name is Olgra, and I will never forget her.$B$BYou did not find her adornments on her body? She wore many jewels of polished bone.$B$BSlay the Razormane Raiders near where she fell, and find her precious works of art!$B$BI will place them with the memorial that I build in her memory.",
[95775]="What I am about to ask you is no small feat, $c, and will likely require strong allies to accomplish.$B$BI want to know more about the ruins on the other side of the cavern the naga are guarding. If my suspicions prove correct, it could indeed be the lost city of I'lalai. The amount of lost historical knowledge at our fingertips could be unrivaled, but I am too old to venture myself.$B$BEnter the ruins and gather etchings of any tablets you find there, then return to me.",
[95776]="You have done well to slay the naga just off of our coast, but the fact that they are in our waters in such numbers means there is yet a larger threat.$B$BI have spoken to Kin'weelay, and he thinks these Brinescale naga are infiltrating the ruins of the Drowned City. If the naga are there, then they are up to no good and are likely searching for something.$B$BWe can't let them get their hands on anything that could compromise us here and it is time to put an end to this. Slay their leader and return to me.",
[95786]="$n, I have a friend in the Hillsbrad Foothills that is studying troll legends and evil magic. I think he may have insight about how this foul magic captured Colenel Kurzen's mind.$B$BI also have a scout's report that the local trolls seem to be agitated, mentioning the word...\"I'lalai\".$B$BI must know if this is related to Kurzen's corruption! Here, take the fetishes and legends along with this scouting report to Loremaster Dibbs. With any luck he will be able to unravel some of their secrets.",
[95787]="<Loremaster Dibbs' hands shake as he reads the scouting report and the troll legends.>$B$BCould it be? By this account it sounds like the lost troll city of I'lalai has risen just off the coast of Stranglethorn! We must investigate immediately. Why, if my research is correct this could be the archeological discovery of the century!$B$BPlease, I know it is a long trek back to Stranglethorn but if you find yourself in this Drowned City, collect any legends you find there and return them to me.",
[95788]="The Skullsplitter fetishes Brother Nimetz sent with you are indeed powerful, though I do not think they contributed to Kurzen's condition, or at least not directly.$B$BStill, if the rumors are true and the lost troll city of I'lalai has indeed risen from its watery grave, it is possible the dark magics used to raise the doomed city may be related.$B$BIf you dare to venture into the Drowned City of I'lalai, please gather any troll fetishes you find and bring them here to me for further study.",
[95789]="Hey pal, you look like you can handle yourself in a fight.$B$BBaron Revilgaz has me keep'n my ear to the ground for magical objects. Word on the street is that a sunken troll ruin has mysteriously become, eh, un-sunk, which means there are a lot of unclaimed goods, if you catch my meaning.$B$BProblem is, it's also caught the eye of pirates! Not just any pirates, the Saltseers specifically collect magical artifacts. I need you to go into the Drowned City, clear them out and take their stolen artifacts.",
[95790]="<This journal seems to have been torn to shreds. From what little you can make out, it looks as if this was a field journal of one of the unfortunate Explorers' League adventurers.$B$BChew marks on the outside of the journal suggest it was likely raptors.$B$BPerhaps its pages can be found and reassembled.>",
[95791]="The Saltseer pirates have been a thorn in my side recently and knowing they're in the Drowned City makes it worse! I mean they're always bad news, but there is one captain in particular I want outta the picture. That damned Captain Dreadrise!$B$BHe and his crew are very accomplished at gathering all the magical artifacts I've been after, and I'm tired of the competition.$B$BI want you to remove Captain Dreadrise and his Saltseer Coroners from the picture. Permanently.",
[95792]="If you wanna land a big score, you gotta go where others wouldn't dare! This cave behind me's rich with untapped mineral deposits. I'm talkin' BIG bucks if we can get a crew in there.$B$BThere's just this... teeny tiny... dragon problem. It's nothing, really.$B$BIf you're willing to go in there and save me the hassle of clearing the dragons out, there's a nice reward in it for you. Not to mention, you'll be in the good graces of a future mining tycoon!",
[95793]="Ah, a $c. I see great strength and determination in you--qualities necessary to rid these lands of evil.$B$BThe demons that walked these lands during the great battle were defeated, yet some still remain. It is important to prevent them from escaping.$B$BThe ruins to the east are dangerous. Carry your strength into their den. Destroy the unwelcome before our lands perish.",
[95795]="<You cover the dwarf's body with his cloak.>$B$BTravel to Lakeshire and personally inform Dorin Songblade what became of his brother within the Excavation Sites.",
[95798]="$n, I want you to take this I'lalai Fetish to my friend Abra in Dalaran. I would love to have her examine it if she has the time to do so.$B$BShe is also particularly interested in troll practices and magic, so I believe this discovery will be exciting for her to unravel.$B$BDo be careful, though. The Kirin Tor can be a bit particular about who they let into their grand city. If you haven't already become a noteworthy visitor, you may need to find a way into their good graces.",
[95799]="I must write my colleague in Ironforge at the Explorer's League immediately. This is a discovery of historical proportions.$B$BWould you mind delivering the letter to Ironforge for me? I will write a copy of my translations of the tablets for you.",
[95803]="Now that we've claimed the head of the tarnished commander, I need you to deliver it to the Undercity. Sylvanas Windrunner mistrusts us greatly, and all but openly disparages us.$B$BDeliver Rudolph Gelhardt's head to the Dark Lady. Show her that we tend to our own house and are devoted to the prosperity of the forsaken.",
[95805]="The sun and the moon, An'she and Mu'sha, are not part of our world like the elements, yet their light gives us life, guidance, and hope.$B$BWe pay respect to the spirits of the world, and so we pay respect to the twins as well.$B$BIf you would show your respect, take this smoldering incense and bring it to a shrine in the hills to the southeast, overlooking the mesa, south of the quilboar. Be quick, so that you can reach the shrine before the incense burns away.$B$BDon't get it wet!",
[95816]="Greetings, accomplished craftsperson!$B$BCompletion of this form will grant you non-exclusive, revocable, and legally limited permission to display advertisement signs for your tradeskill(s) all across Azeroth!$B$BOnce completed, please bring this to your local Azeroth Commerce Authority branch's Contract Coordinator to begin processing.$B$BHappy crafting!",
[95819]="Greetings, accomplished craftsperson!$B$BCompletion of this form will grant you non-exclusive, revocable, and legally limited permission to display advertisement signs for your tradeskill(s) all across Azeroth!$B$BOnce completed, please bring this to your local Durotar Supply & Logistics Contract Coordinator to begin processing.$B$BHappy crafting!",
[95820]="We have done well to create great relationships with the merchants and craftspeople of Orgrimmar. Among these excellent relationships is an orc named Karolek, a leatherworker who ensures a steady supply of hides and other useful equipment to us.$B$BHe also happens to be great at making signs!$B$BIf you'd like to get your sign made fast, I would recommend him over anyone else. Let him know I sent you.",
[95821]="The materials for the sign should be easy to come by as an accomplished crafter like yourself. All we will need is $1oa Heavy Leather and $2oa Mithril Bars.$B$BNormally for a rush order I would charge a few gold, but I have had a craving for homemade Goldthorn Tea lately. Don't worry, I enjoy making it myself, but I do need $3oa Goldthorn to make it happen.$B$BIf you bring me all of these, you'll have your first sign ready to go in no time!",
[95882]="An Alliance scouting party has been seen on a small island northeast of Rog'mar. They are led by a scoutmaster who has made tracking enemy movements increasingly difficult. The bastard even named his filthy pet after me as an open mockery. He knows I'm hunting him.$B$BThis human has eyes everywhere, and they need to be put out. I already claimed one before he managed to flee. Bring me his other as proof that the scoutmaster is no more. Show him he is not as untouchable as he thinks.$B$B-- Neza Bloodsnout",
[95883]="<The preparations for a hastily-assembled ritual are gathered unceremoniously on the altar. According to the scrap of note, everything has been gathered. All that's missing are the offering of blood and the Tortured Soul.$B$BThe undead around you look tortured enough. They may have what you seek.>",
[95884]="<The scrap of note is mostly illegible. What is still readable, however, are notes about preparations for an offering.$B$BAn offering stone is mentioned, as well as a ritual.$B$BPerhaps you can find this offering stone nearby.>",
[95885]="<All that's left now is the offering of blood.$B$BThe note scrap mentioned a 'willing sacrifice.'$B$BAn intense sense of dread washes over you.>",
[95912]="With each orc we cut down, another takes its place--somehow even more capable than the last. A skilled warrior must be training this new generation. If we are to make a dent in their numbers, we need to ensure they don't have a chance to recoup their losses.$B$BIf any soldier is brave enough, it's imperative we find this blademaster and put an end to him. He is likely at the trainee camp north of the Horde outpost even now. Kill him, take his banner, and destroy the orcs' morale.$B$B-- Ember Bladewhisper",
[95913]="<Tessa rocks her baby, trying to help her sleep.>$B$BIf she isn't hungry, maybe she's just tired. To be honest, Emma here was a delightful surprise, but that means we were a little unprepared. My husband built her this lovely bassinet, but I worry these blankets are too old. She deserves the best, after all.$B$BIf you're still willing to help, I would be forever grateful if you could find some pelts for me to line her bed with. If this stops her crying, I think everyone in Farholde would be grateful.",
[95924]="Ye there! Aye, I'm talkin' ta ye! We've made the discovery of a lifetime down in Un'Goro! Can ye believe it?$B$BThere's just one problem... our dig site's been overrun by voracious beasts of the killin' nature. Very unpleasant indeed.$B$BWith yer help, we can reclaim our camp and git back ta workin'. Now, what do ye say? I'll make it worth yer while.",
[95925]="$C, we've made the discovery of a lifetime! I can't believe it; the ruins in Un'Goro are open!$B$BWe've already sent a team but they have encountered... trouble. If you're headed in there anyway would ya be able to finish this map?$B$BIt sounds like there's an Achromatic Crystal in there and an unearthed watcher somewhere near a giant Western Gate that sounds interesting.$B$BThe other landmarks that would be helpful are the Pillar of Assimilation, the Western Gate and the Regrowth Vestibule.",
[95926]="You there! I have a job for someone of your... skills.$B$BI have gotten word from my sources of a crystal found in Shaper's Terrace that can seemingly drain the elements around it. Or perhaps it can drain life essence itself. It is unclear from this report.$B$BI must have a fragment of this crystal! Just think of the applications of such a powerful artifact.$B$BGo to Shaper's Terrace and bring me back a sample of this colorless Achromatic Crystal, and I will reward you for your efforts.",
[95928]="Ah, it is good you have come here, $c.$B$BI have been studying crystals of late and word has reached me about a peculiar set of crystals said to be from Un'Goro Crater. I have samples of the most basic ones, but I have heard tell of larger more potent crystals seen in a place called Shaper's Terrace.$B$BI do not know much of this place aside from it containing these crystals that supposedly have the very elements within them. If you find yourself there, please bring me a sample of each color.",
[95934]="My surveying tools show signs of a never-before-seen mineral in these caves. Cubic draconia, I call it. Probably worth a fortune.$B$BExciting as this is, no one's gonna come help me dig it up if I can't show 'em proof that it exists. Sure, I have the readings from my tools, but people like to hold a big shiny crystal, not look at charts.$B$BI'm sure there's a few crystals poking up from the dirt in there. If you're willing to dodge a few dragons and get one, you'd really be helpin' a gal out.",
[95935]="The dragon's head is all teeth, scale, and ash--a grisly prize taken from a grisly creature. Holding it, you feel the heat of its last fiery breath still radiating from its mouth.$B$BWhile the threat Scaldaron once posed is no more, the sentries at the Southern Watch ought to know about what happened here.",
[95936]="The dragon's head is all teeth, scale, and ash -- a grisly prize taken from a grisly creature. Holding it, you feel the heat of its last fiery breath still radiating from its mouth.$B$BWhile the threat Scaldaron once posed is no more, the warriors of Rog'mar ought to know about what happened here.",
[95943]="G'day, $Glad:lass;. Name's Bertrand, Bertrand Ironbrow! At yer service.$B$B<Bertrand extends a filthy hand.>$B$BThese fine folk contracted me tae oversee construction of this here keep. What they lack in experience they make up for in spirit! Problem is, I misplaced me tools.$B$BHad a bit of a run in with a few Twilight in a small grove northwest o' here. Had to choose between me life or me tools. On one hand, I'm alive. On the other... ye see where this is goin'.$B$BThink ye could help find me tools?",
[95951]="'Ey boss-$Gmon:lady;, ya need help from ol' Tan'jani? Don't worry about it, I fix you up good.$B$BOrcs be good at hittin' humans with axes, but when you wanna stick 'em before dey see ya comin', that's when you call on the headhunters. You wanna learn to stick 'em too? I see it in your eyes, heheh.$B$BFirst we get you your own spears. Dis one's mine. Go to the human camp to de west and take their wood. Take knife with ya. You can sharpen their lumber into good spears for stickin'. Den bring 'em back.",
[95955]="You got de spears, now ya gonna learn how to throw dem.$B$BDe Riverglades be full o' crocolisks. Nasty tings. Snap you up if ya ain't quick. Perfect for target practice, heheh.$B$BGo stick yourself a bunch of dem. Den you come back to ol' Tran'jani for ya prize. If ya can stick a crocolisk, ya can stick any'ting.",
[95957]="Here ya go, champ. One drink for ol' grumpy guts over there. If this doesn't sober him up, nothin' will.$B$BOh and uh... wash your hands after touchin' this. And don't get it in your eyes.",
[95961]="<Tessa's baby continues to wail loudly.>$B$BI guess she isn't tired. Oh... everyone makes it look so easy. Her father always knows how to cheer her up. If only he'd come home already.$B$B$n, I hate to ask this, but can you see what is taking him so long? He set out a while ago but he should have been back by now. Emma just lights up when she sees him.$B$BYou should find him at Powderfuse Port-- he seems to go there a lot lately. You'll know my Gray when you see him. He shines as brightly as the sun.",
[95975]="Tess says little Emm can't sleep without me? And you did all that for them? A total stranger? Damn it. What was I thinking...$B$BEven if I can't guarantee a perfect world for her, I still need to be a part of it. What am I even fighting for if I can't hope for a brighter future?$B$BThank you for helping my family in my absence, friend, but it's time for me to go home. If I could ask one more favor, can you pick some flowers and take them to Tess? Let her know I'll be home soon? I need to clean up first.",
[95981]="Taking away their pendants is just the first step. If the Kirin Tor really are shipping a steady supply of relics from Dalaran, we must stop them at the source.$B$BSearch the roads around Ambermill for Dalaran's wizards and watchers. Their presence has allowed free access across our borders for too long. If we can cull their numbers, that should put a stop to these pendants making it into Silverpine Forest in the first place.",
[95982]="Folks keep dumpin' their furry friends here like I know what I'm doin'. And then they blame me if they come back and their horse or wolf or... whatever they brought is dead or ran off. What do I look like, I'm runnin' a charity?$B$BYou look like you know your way around a trough. Mind whippin' me up some grub I can use to keep these beasties in check?$B$BIf you can't make it yourself, someone might be willin' to sell you some. And hurry! Last thing I need is a stampede of hungry animals.",
[95983]="The skeleton is badly mangled. Deep markings on its limbs vaguely match patterns of teeth and claws. Many days beneath the beating sun have made the bones pale and brittle as well. The brutality of both the attacker and the weather have rendered the victim's identity a mystery.$B$BYou can't take the whole skeleton with you, but you could bring its skull to the nearby watchman and see what he knows.",
[95984]="These markings are from a lion. By the look of them, this one's especially large. The leader of the nearby pride, most likely.$B$BIf rumor spreads about a man-eating lion prowling around on my watch, Demar will be furious. Fortunately, I have a plan.$B$BI can make a whistle that mimics the call of a wounded tallstrider. We can use that to lure the beast out. I'll just need one of their beaks to give it the right sound. There's tallstriders all over the plains. Get me a beak, and make it snappy!",
[95986]="The whistle's made, $n.$B$BTake it, and go to the top of the hill where the lions are. Should be just north of here.$B$BOnce you're there, blow the whistle, and our man-eater should appear. I'd tell you not to come back if you don't manage to kill him, but you'll probably be dead anyhow.$B$BNow then, off with you. Let's see if you fare better than our skeletal friend.",
[95988]="Talked to Gray, didja? Ball of laughs, that guy. Last thing he needs is you gettin' him another drink. This is an inn not a bar. He's lucky I haven't thrown him out.$B$BYou tryin' to take him with you, be my guest. Though I don't think he's in any condition to go anywhere like that. Not without a little goblin pick-me-up.$B$BWhy don't ya gather some ingredients for me from this list while I prepare your little friend his 'drink.' We'll see if he still wants booze after he's had my specialty cocktail.",
[95991]="It's dangerous enough transportin' horses 'round the glades without talk of some mysterious phantom crocolisk snappin' up my prized ponies! They say this one must be at least three times as big as a regular croc. And twice as mean!$B$BI ain't a gamblin' man. I ain't takin' no chances with my horses till someone puts this good-fer-nothin' monster down. If anyone finds this varmint along the rivers, bring me its tooth so's I know it's safe to travel again. Till then, I'm stayin' put!$B$B-- Wheatley",
[95992]="Dese waters be treacherous. My headhunters keep the paths clear as dey can, but there be a beasty stalkin' de rivers even we cannot catch. Excitin', eh?$B$BBoss say we gotta clear it out, so we got a little competition goin'. Find de white one patrollin' de rivers and bring me its fang. Whoever sticks this slippery crocolisk win de whole pot. Just don't get snapped yourself, heheh!$B$B-- Tan'jani",
[95998]="Well howdy there, $c. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. Good for you. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.$B$BIt's a big wide world out there and you'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful. Not sure how your outdoorsman skills are but I reckon I could teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.$B$BHave a seat near the fire, get comfy. I'll walk you through it.",
[96003]="As suspected, the vessels fused into something new--something powerful.$B$BI suppose if the vessels capture stored energy, there must be a way to use that power to our advantage. Fel artifacts are rarely safe or easy to come by, but we might as well do something with it, hmm?$B$BTime for a field test.$B$BTake the crystal and use it against Bethra'zel and Mazzogore--two of their most powerful demons. Their presence alone has ensured the camp is well protected. Let's see if we can change that.",
[96009]="One thing that never ceases to amaze me is the drive of humans. They see a desolate warzone teemin' with orcs and cultists and figure that's the perfect spot tae set up shop! Amazin'.$B$BBut, it's not me job tae tell 'em where to build. Just gotta show 'em how. And if we want this keep tae be as big as they say, we're gonna need lots o' wood.$B$BWith how dangerous the roads have become our lumber shipments from the mill tae the northwest are slowin' to a crawl. Think ye can fetch a few bundles for us?",
[96010]="Although I am sure we can attribute the damage to both pylons to the reckless centaur stomping about, I suspect the timing of their rampage resulted in the shards being separated. I know little about their quarrels, but I do know there are at least two main factions that have trespassed into Shen'dralas: the ferocious Magram and the cunning Gelkis.$B$BKeeping these treasures in the midst of a battlefield would be unwise. By now, I am assuming they have taken their trophies back to their own villages.",
[96015]="We should be thankful that our foe is stupid. An army of ogres at their disposal, and the Twilight's Hammer have them working in the mines nowhere near the fight. I don't know if I chalk it up to mismanagement or an internal struggle, but either way they're in no position to defend themselves.$B$BThat's where we come in. With the cult's focus divided, we have an opportunity to strike the enemy while they're vulnerable and split them further. Go to this mine and sow some chaos among their ranks.",
[96016]="Ye did good, and I can see yer itchin' fer yer reward. Sorry tae say, I'm not exactly a dwarf of many possessions.$B$B<Veyric gestures broadly at his remote location.>$B$BTell ye what, though. I hear a troll named the Windwatcher lives out in the Alterac Mountains. He's a powerful shaman himself, and an expert in storm elementals. If ye bring that there elemental core to him, I bet he can make ye a weapon worthy of yer victory.",
[96018]="You may have seen the floating sparks of mana scattered throughout Shen'dralas. This is a new phenomenon, likely the result of the damage the pylons have endured.$B$BWe need this mana back in a semicrystallized form. We can accomplish this by using the Mana Sieve found within the temple. Borrow the sieve and collect any floating mana orbs you find.$B$BThe temple's denizens will not appreciate their precious artifact being borrowed without their consent, but they will understand in time.",
[96025]="Thank you for your help, $n. A dear friend of mine awaits your arrival at the summit.$B$BYou can find her up the road to the east.",
[96026]="Dese good rock. Now need finishing touch. More rock.$B$BOnly rock can make rock stronger. Dat the way of rocks.$B$BMe see some tinies make extra heavy rock. Bring me heavy rocks and me make weapon.",
[96031]="You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, $c. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.$B$BWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels.",
[96044]="So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons.",
[96045]="Now that you've taken up Alchemy, I can also teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp once you've learned a bit. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste.",
[96046]="Mining isn't the most glamorous, but it's good honest work and a fine profession for you to explore.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Lodestone for your camp. Build one of these and everyone who wants to swing a sword will be eager to gather round your fire and soak up the extra \"oomph\" it can provide to increase their combat prowess.",
[96050]="You might not think so, but your skill as a fisherman can actually come in handy at camp.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Fish Bowl for your camp. You can use this fixture to help provide a bit of joy to yourself and your fellow adventurers. A happy adventurer is a strong adventurer and I'm sure your combat capabilities will reflect that.",
[96055]="Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate.",
[96056]="Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up.",
[96057]="Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.$B$BI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.",
[96058]="Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.",
[96059]="Now that you've begun your journey into being an enchanter, I reckon I can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp once you've learned the ropes.$B$BIt's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.",
[96060]="Let me be the first to share that I was a master swordsman in life. I forged weapons by day and wielded them by night.$B$BAs you are quite well aware, my relationship with this particular blade is now extraordinarily complicated. Though I think I could swing it around, I'm not convinced it would be of much use unless I was fighting other spirits. Is that really of any value to me in Shen'dralas?$B$BNonetheless, I would like its capabilities tested and I think our forests could use a gentle culling.",
[96063]="The fuel of the future's not coal, or oil, it's gas, baby! Those marshy ponds to the southwest spew it out by the ton, and I've got just the invention to put it to use--a new type of engine that runs on the stuff. The gas is a real pain to collect, though.$B$BIf you feel like making a humble contribution to the future of science and industry, why don't you help me get some of that gas? You can see it coming up from vents near the water.",
[96067]="You may have noticed my mechanical companion here, G45-B4G. Whirlin' around in that burlap chest of his is the one, and only, working prototype of my gas-powered engine.$B$BI figure it's in need of some stress testing. How'd you like to take him on in a fight? I can power him up with the gas you've collected.$B$BOh, and don't worry about hurting him. He can't feel a thing!",
[96077]="Yes, Thomas Belle.$B$B<Daythor's demeanor changes suddenly, appearing as though to recall a fond memory of this individual.>$B$BThomas was one of the first to fall as the scourge laid siege to our outpost. I hadn't heard of his passing until the battle was over. Tragic... He was such a promising young man.$B$BI suppose it would be right for us to deliver this to his beloved Michelle. If memory serves me right, he spoke often of Goldshire.",
[96081]="If there is one thing a fighting force always needs, it's bandages. Unfortunately, Farholde has no reliable way to manufacture cloth. Thus, we depend on imports from the goblins or, if we are lucky, what we can take back from the orcs.$B$BCurrently, our supply of quality cloth is running low. I will have to start making bandages of old shirts before long. If you have the means to aid us, you would be saving many lives.",
[96082]="I will fashion the cloth you've given me into bandages. In the meantime, please take these ones that I have already made, and dress the wounds of the soldiers who need it. It should be a matter of basic first aid.$B$BYour assistance here is both necessary, and highly appreciated. I simply cannot be everywhere at once.",
[96083]="You have done all you can here, for now.$B$BIf you wish to be of further aid, go up the hill to the chapel. It is the smaller building outside the main church.$B$BSister Rowland is looking after a few quarantined soldiers there who have contracted an unknown illness.",
[96084]="I will spare you the grisly details, but these soldiers are violently ill. The nature of their sickness leads me to believe there is an issue with either their food or their water.$B$BI've already checked the crops coming in from the nearby farms, so this only leaves the water, which comes from the local rivers. The best place to collect a sample is from the pools in the plains to the north. Nearly every river runs through the area, so it would be wise to check for contamination there.",
[96085]="The impurities in this sample look organic in nature. Not quite waste, but certainly something toxic.$B$BI am no expert on wildlife, but I would guess that there is something upstream causing the water contamination. Some kind of animal, or at least a creature.$B$BFollow the rivers as far north as you can, and see if you can find what is responsible for this. If it is an animal, it must be put down. It is for the safety of all here in Farholde.",
[96101]="Greetings, $c. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.$B$BYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.$B$BHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.",
[96102]="Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.$B$BI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.",
[96103]="The skeleton is badly mangled. Deep markings on its limbs vaguely match patterns of teeth and claws. Many days beneath the beating sun have made the bones pale and brittle as well. The brutality of both the attacker and the weather have rendered the victim's identity a mystery.$B$BYou can't take the whole skeleton with you, but you could bring its skull to a hunter at Rog'mar and see what they know.",
[96104]="These markings are from a lion. By the look of them, this one is especially large--the leader of the nearby pride.$B$BI would gladly hunt the beast myself, but you have first claim. Instead, I will aid you.$B$BI can make a whistle that mimics the call of a wounded tallstrider. You can use it to lure the lion out. I'll just need one of their beaks to give it the right sound.$B$BThere are tallstriders all over the plains. Find me a beak and the hunt can begin!",
[96105]="The whistle is made, $n.$B$BTake it and go to the top of the hill south where the lions dwell.$B$BOnce you are ready to face your quarry, blow the whistle and the beast should appear.$B$BI wish you luck in your hunt. May you return in glory.",
[96107]="A hunter goes through more arrows in her lifetime than there are stars in the sky.$B$BPersonally, I make mine by hand. I only trust my own work.$B$BThe coarse feathers of the nearby buzzards make for excellent fletching. Would you aid me by collecting a few?",
[96108]="Arrows are always essential, but sometimes you need something more potent to take down your prey.$B$BThis is where poison coatings come into play. They ruin the meat, but if you need something dead, they do the job.$B$BPoisons can either be brewed or, if you are brave, gathered. You strike me as the latter.$B$BThe vipers by the pools to the south produce a powerful venom. If I have estimated you correctly, I think you could collect some of it.",
[96109]="As important as a hunter's weapons is her quiver. A good quiver holds many arrows, while not being so large as to slow the wearer down. It must be durable, and fit snugly onto the body.$B$BAround here, there is no better material for a quiver than the pelts of lions. They are already well-suited for the life of a hunter on the plains.$B$BThe lions gather on a hill to the south. You can see it from here. Please, bring me their pelts.",
[96125]="Now that the lion hides have been collected, and the orcish poachers culled, I can finally get a break.$B$BAt least, that's what I would say, if the man who was supposed to relieve me of my watch wasn't missing.$B$BDunston Willis, explorer extraordinaire, went to investigate the ogre settlement to the north a few days ago. He said he'd take over my post upon his return.$B$BFind him. If he's alive, bring him back here. If he's hanging up on meat hooks, bring me proof so Demar can send me someone else.",
[96126]="I'm not sure how you got in here, but please, listen to me.$B$BAs you know, I serve as a watchman for Farholde Keep.$B$BWhile on patrol, I was ambushed by a band of these brutes and taken prisoner. Now, I am forced to fight in the ring for their amusement.$B$BI haven't much strength left. If I'm to escape, it's now or never.$B$BMy captor is an ogre they call \"Gronok the Butcher\". He has the key to my shackles. Will you bring me that key and help me out of here?",
[96130]="Among the prairie wolves that hunt the hills nearby is one that is especially aggressive. We have taken to calling her Chakuyak. She has become a threat to travelers coming from abroad.$B$BShe stalks the trees west of Stonebull Lake, moving from tree stand to tree stand.$B$BEnd this threat and bring me her pelt, and I will speak your praises to the chief. Beware, for she is dangerous! You might see other hunters seeking her out there, and perhaps you could work as a team.",
[96131]="I'm sure you've met that old stick-in-the-mud, that lives in the cave south of here?$B$BYou must take this staff to him along with my feather. He will know what it means. Or he won't! Either way it will get his attention.$B$BHe may be an oldstone, but he is reliable. He's one of the few mortals I would trust with a matter as grave as this.$B$BQuickly, Dirtwalker! I fear a shadow is falling over Hyjal we cannot see.",
[96135]="Euck, just bein' around these blasted totems is givin' me the willies--but that's good. This much twisted corruption will be exactly what we need tae summon the quilboar's elementals.$B$BGo to the Thousand Needles and find a suitable spot for your defenses. The steam pools should work. They're rich with fire, earth, water, and air alike. Place these totems and be ready for a fight. The Razormane won't take too kindly to yer interference.",
[96136]="As you have no doubt experienced yourself, the elements of Azeroth are unique to those in Zephras. It is one thing to channel the forces of nature within the elemental plains, and another thing entirely to do it down here in the muck.$B$BI could grant you your totem of air, but I think it would do you more good to meet with the one who trains the other earth-bound initiates. What say you, $n?",
[96145]="Traveler, be wary! Though the Shrine of Aviana lies ahead, the area is claimed now by the harpies of the Wormwing tribe.$B$BLike my family, the Highfeathers, I am a follower of Aviana, but the Wormwings are not so loyal. They are a danger to anyone who passes through their territory.$B$BIf you can make your way past them, my cousin Phoebe Highfeather helps to protect the shrine.",
[96204]="Now that I'm free I'm going to make these vile creatures regret ever laying eyes on a Windshaper.$B$BLet's get out of here, $c.",
[96209]="The ancient, Orokai, stands vigil just outside of town. Take this to him. The ancients are wondrous and wise. Provided this branch has not been separated from its parent tree for too long, he will be able to \"speak\" with it to learn what tales it has to tell.$B$BYou can find Orokai to the southwest of the town, not too far away.",
[96222]="While war rages throughout the region, the Maraudine centaur stand unchallenged in the Valley of Spears. I worry that they will grow callous in time and stir further unrest if the other clans continue to turn a blind eye to their presence.$B$BKhan Hratha possesses a Maraudine Key Fragment, and I wish to have it as a negotiation tactic. Find a war horn mouthpiece from the centaur there and use it to challenge him atop the highest peak.$B$BBring the key to me, and I will have a proposition for you.",
[96241]="Something funny be happenin' over there at Gloomrise. Ol' Mazu'kon be hearin all about these nasty new beasties skitterin' all around there.$B$BSome say those creepy crawlies got a venom that have some unique properties and this be gettin' me curious. Take my extractor. Use it on the dead bodies layin' around that place to harvest the venom. Do this and I be in ya debt, mon.",
[96243]="It's past time ye heeded the earth, brave Shaman. The elements already prickle in yer skin, but once ye speak with the stone, the ground itself'll set firm 'neath yer soles--and in yer soul.$B$BSeek out Teo Hammerstorm, in Coldridge Valley. Ye'll find him within Anvilmar, a holdfast forged by hammer, fire, and will.",
[96252]="$C, I would ask a favor of you. One that is deeply personal.$B$BWhen they ambushed and killed my sisters, the Wormwings took their jewelry claiming these treasures as trophies of battle. What's worse, they've stashed our treasures in their nests with their unborn young; further proof of their depravity.$B$BPlease collect my fallen sisters' treasures. Avoid harming the unhatched eggs if you can, but I'll lose no sleep over the broken eggs of our enemies.",
[96255]="<Something wriggles ominously within the bone pile as green ooze seeps out from under the freshly added bones.>",
[96259]="There is an ancient tauren burial ground at the place called Gloomrise, just northwest of this camp. Of late it has been infested with a particularly vicious brood of spiders. These spiders not only pose a threat to the people of Mulgore, they are also damaging a site that most tauren consider to be sacred.$B$BIt would be of great service if you could travel to Gloomrise and put an end to this infestation. The ancestors will surely smile upon you if you see this done.",
[96260]="Have you heard what befell the burial ground at Gloomrise? Giant spiders--rumored to have a venom so strong that it can wake the dead--have spread like wildfire. Nasty business, if you ask me.$B$BOne of the scouts dispatched to investigate returned half dead and covered in an incredibly resilient, crystalline spider silk. I harvested what I could, but I would highly value more samples of this silk for additional study.$B$BBring me more of this crystalline silk and I will reward you.",
[96261]="As is often the case with infestations such as the one we are facing at Gloomrise, a single powerful matriarch often leads to the rapid spread of a hostile spider population.$B$BIf we wish to drive these beasts off for good, we'll need to seek out the progenitor and end her. When you go to Gloomrise, seek out the broodmother there and destroy her. I'd advise you to bring allies, and be ready for anything. These seem to be no ordinary spiders.",
[96262]="I've known these hills since I was a hatchling. If there is one thing I know, it's that pinecones can solve a lot of problems.$B$BProbably not what you expected, eh?$B$B<The crow winks at you, conspiratorially.>$B$BGo fetch me some; it's part of a little scheme I'm hatching. I promise you it will be worth the effort.$B$BYou should be able to find them under any healthy or living tree nearby. Stay away from those corrupted ones though, those pinecones aren't any good!",
[96264]="So yer a big shot shaman now, eh? Ye've mastered the elements and want tae put 'em to good use? I think I got just the thing.$B$BIf ye want the elements' respect, ye gotta repay yer debts to 'em. They help you, you help them. And right now they need all the help they can get from those who would abuse their power.$B$BEarth's rumblin', $n. It speaks of the quilboar amassin' for some ritual of terrible power. We need tae go investigate their kraul and see what they're up to. Bring me back whatever ye find.",
[96294]="<The Broodmother you just killed is no spider at all, but rather a night elf druid who assumed a twisted animal form. A variety of questions flood your mind about the nature--and purpose--of the spiders at Gloomrise.$B$BYou notice a note peeking out of the folds of the dead elf's robe. Perhaps this document may answer some of the questions filling your head.>",
[96296]="<The second you near the pulsing nodule it falls from the tree, exposing a weeping green sap. It seems the tree has corruption within its bark that has spread deep, but the tree is not yet dead.$B$BLooking around it is clear it has spread to some of the surrounding trees, but not all suffer from the same level of corruption.$B$BPerhaps it is not too late to save the infected trees nearby.$B$BSurely the Highfeathers would be grateful if you remove as many corrupted knots as you can find.>",
[96301]="With the venomous, poisonous heart of the chimaera Ghansurok in hand, soak in the ancient waters of the Well of Eternity.$B$BWatch closely how the waters react to the corruption, how nature remembers what systemic corruption has tried to unmake.$B$BBring the organ back to me, and together we will read the signs it bears, and learn whether balance can yet be restored... or if the wound runs too deep.",
[96302]="I've compacted this potent, pungent resin. Take this prepared incense and stand before the fallen form of The Defiler's remains.$B$BSpeak the incantation as the smoke rises, not to banish what remains, but to steady the spirit. His visage still carries the memory of terror, and even now it stirs fear in those who linger too long.$B$BLet the smoke carry calm and resolve, warding the mind against dread, so that those who walk this place may remember the victory, not the horror.",
[96303]="$n, the ancestral spirits called to Hyjal during the great battle weren't all lost. Some linger still, drawn to Nordrassil after the great sacrifice. These wisps have stayed within the root canopy that hangs over the well, trapped in a state of purgatory between this world and the next.$B$BUse this enchanted branch to bring peace to these wisps, joining their memories with eternity.$B$BYou need not release them all yourself. Recover the will of five and return the branch to us.",
[96321]="I... don't have much time, mortal. You must take this staff, a branch of the world tree... corrupted... wrong. I carried it here...$B$BThe Wild Gods... they must know. Take it to her. The... crow...$B$B<The dying Wild God grows still and his eyes stare blankly ahead. What little is left of his corporeal form seems to break apart and drift away. There is a faintly glowing branch on the ground, with a sickly green crystal affixed to its head.>",
[96332]="A second wave of Naga was approaching the keep when we were falling back. I suspect that the battle is still raging inside.$B$BWe Kor'kron play blood for blood. If you are going in there anyway, I want you to kill any Naga you see. I saw a sorceress among them as well, and you can bet that was their leader. Bring me her head.$B$BWe lost a lot of good orcs today and I won't rest easy knowing that we didn't give as good as we got.",
[96334]="Most of the humans we fought wore blood red bandanas. I seem to recall hearing of a criminal organization operating in the Eastern Kingdoms known as 'The Defias Brotherhood' who are known for their red masks. Why they are active here in Kalimdor I don't know, but kill any that cross your path and bring their masks to Eitrigg in Orgrimmar.$B$BHe'll be able to determine if these are in fact Defias masks.",
[96335]="Wow! That was impressive. The way you took down that dragon was really something!$B$BWhile you are here... do you think you might be able to help me get out of this ball and chain?$B$BIf he hasn't fled or been killed already, the torturer they call 'The Questioner' should have the keys to these shackles. Get the key from that sadist and bring it to me.$B$BI promise that I'll make it well worth your while if you do.",
[96337]="I told you that I'd make it worth your while to free me. I don't have any gold for you, but I have something better.$B$BTake this. It will help you find a treasure more valuable than gold. Do what you want with it, but if anyone asks you where you got it, tell them that the person who gave it to you died.$B$BTell them he was vaporized by dragonfire... blown out to sea.",
[96369]="<The King is dead--killed in an escape attempt just before the Naga attacked. Many Kor'kron died to learn this news, but this knowledge could shake the Alliance to its core. You need to return to Commander Folkar and tell him what you've learned as quickly as possible.>",
[96381]="Was spyin' on the shore of Alcaz with my trusty lookin' glass whilst you were off eavesdroppin' on Lady Proudmoore. I think the island may be under attack. I saw naga--lots of them, chargin' onto shore.$B$BThe enemy of my enemy is certainly not my friend when it comes to naga, so let's do the world a favor and take some of them out. I also spied what looks to be the leader--a spellcaster type barkin' orders. Take her out as well, if you can.",
[96390]="Dark Iron spies have infiltrated Dun Morogh. To what end I canna' be sure, but this is a problem we need to nip in the bud before it is allowed to grow.$B$BHead eastward to Ironband's Compound and kill the Dark Iron spies that you find there.",
[96392]="Greetings to ye, friend. My name is Earthseer Farsen and I'm visiting Dun Morogh from Aerie Peak. As I was travelin', I couldn't help but notice that we have, well... a bit o' a Dark Iron Dwarf problem.$B$BIf ye have a moment, I can show ye what I mean. I've got a bit o' magic that should do the trick.",
[96435]="<Felflick cackles gleefully as he regards the bloody bones of the Ashen Reign leaders.>$B$BOh this is just perfect!$B$B<Felflick hops back and forth in his cage, snickering all the while.>$B$BNow it is time to give those warlocks the fate they deserve. There is a massive bone pile to the west of here if you follow the road. Trust me, it's impossible to miss. That's where all their 'failed' experiments go.$B$BThat is where I wish to dump these fools' remains. Let the whole world know what failures they are!",
[96438]="$n, I need your aid. One of our brothers passing through Nigel's Point in Desolace overheard details of a battle that took place at the Mannoroc Coven. It was reported that one side brought powerful holy magic to bear in the battle against the warlocks there. Wielders of the light were certainly involved.$B$BI'd like to learn more of who was involved in this skirmish. If one of our people was involved--or fell there... I want to know about it.",
[96449]="Come to think on it, I do know of a secluded spot far to the south of here. Someone once told me it was called Newman's Landing, though don't ask me who this \"Newman\" is. You should start looking for Ol' Aeonas there.$B$BYou are welcome to make use of my old dingy moored just over yonder just past the northernmost dock. She isn't much, but she'll get you there faster than swimming.$B$BI do hope nothin' happened to him. I'd rest easier if you went and checked on our friend.",
[96476]="Aeonas mentioned something about Felwood, so it's possible that's where he is. There's a small settlement in the southern portion of the woods there known as the Emerald Sanctuary. I'd suggest asking around there to see if anyone has seen him.",
[96494]="With the perimeter scouted, you've proven useful and trustworthy enough to bring into the fold.$B$BI'm here representing SI:7's efforts to gain crucial information important to the Alliance. Not just anyone is privy to this knowledge. Mind your discretion.$B$BA druidic cult known as the Blackthorne Pact has taken root nearby, operating in service to something they call the Wild King.$B$BFind the domain of this \"Wild King\" and mark it. Then we can report back to Stormwind with certainty.",
[96529]="Your help has been key to our scouting efforts. Take this information to Master Mathias Shaw in Stormwind.$B$BRemember, you're not to speak of our activities here, my presence, or SI:7 involvement to anyone else. I have a lot to continue setting up here, and plans to keep on track.$B$BWe'll be in touch.",
[96550]="The aged scabbard is embellished with carved designs and markings. This matches the description spoken by the war veteran. A dramatic view of the land below is a breathtaking sight.$B$BPerhaps simply holding the scabbard in your hand while remembering the veteran's words will beckon the spirit to this memory.",
[96558]="Beneath the shattered stones of that watchtower lies a cache we buried in haste, when the world was starting to burn. What little we carried from Hyjal rests there still. Take it--you have earned that much.$B$BThe pull is increasing... the mountain no longer holds me as it once did. I am unsure if we will ever speak again.$B$BBecause of you, I remember who I was, and who we were. Go with my thanks, and let this spirit finally be at peace.",
[96559]="Every Gnomish test pilot knows that one must be prepared for the worst-case scenario when taking to our great skies!$B$BThat's why we never leave the hangar without our pilot survival kits. They have a self-activating beacon attached that will radio our position home as soon as you open it. Not to mention being stuffed full of other useful supplies.$B$BIf you can find that pack wherever it fell, by all means open it immediately and help yourself to the contents. You'll still be doing me a favor!",
[96561]="<You unfold the simple parchment.>$B$BTo my Rowdy Redridge Rebels,$B$BThe lumberjacks here say the gulpers in that pond are biting like they're racing each other to the bait. Good fish, better eating. After this war is over, we're due an angling competition between friends.$B$BThe setting is simple: we stand on the center island and fish till the sun slips behind Hyjal's highest peak.$B$BWhoever catches the most, doesn't have to gut 'em for our dinner!$B$B-- Tobin --",
[96603]="Archmage Rhonin is presently abroad investigating a disturbance in the flow of magic across Azeroth. The Archmage has charged me with soliciting the aid of strong adventurers like yourself in gathering important field data to aid him.$B$BTake this Arcane Censer. While afflicted by its magic, you will be able to extract motes of unstable magic from the most skilled spell casters and other singularly powerful entities you may encounter. Bring me said motes and the Kirin Tor will be in your debt.",
[96604]="Lok-tar, $c. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.$B$BYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.$B$BHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.",
[96605]="Greetings, $c. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.$B$BYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.$B$BHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.",
[96606]="Greetings, $c. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.$B$BYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.$B$BHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.",
[96607]="Greetings, $c. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.$B$BYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.$B$BHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.",
[96608]="Greetings, $c. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.$B$BYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.$B$BHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.",
[96609]="Are you familiar with Silvermoon Shimmerwine? It has a delicate flavor that is entirely unique to the vineyards of Eversong and it is the one thing I truly miss from my homeland.$B$BUnfortunately, it is extremely hard to find on this side of the Thalassian Gate.$B$BI had a patron bring me a bottle that he claimed to have \"liberated\" from blood elves in northern Azshara. If your adventures take you to that region and you can recover more bottles for me, I would handsomely reward your efforts.",
[96616]="Could this be? Travelers have returned to Hyjal!$B$BI can hardly believe it! Perhaps with your aid we will finally be freed of this place. With the Scourge remnants to the east we have been subject to constant raids and many have fallen victim to their corruption.$B$BPlease, $c. I would ask a favor of you. In the valley north of here grows an herb with blue flowers that can alleviate the pains of the infection. Gather some and bring it to me so I may help the wounded.",
[96622]="I would ask one last favor while I have you here, friend. Could you deliver the poultice I have made to two of my companions here in camp?$B$BEnho is in our infirmary to the left. He is very weak but I yet hope he will be able to overcome the infection. I have been spoon-feeding him broth to try to help him regain his strength.$B$BThe other is Maruke.$B$B<Ortak hangs his head in silence for a moment.>$B$BYou will find her north of here, where we keep the few mounts we have left.",
[96626]="So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.$B$BCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.",
[96627]="$n, you have proven your competence as a protector thus far. That is why I am now entrusting you with an unusual task.$B$BI've heard of a new adventurer down the road by Goldshire. Go and see what he's doing.",
[96628]="Wait, $n. I have another ask of you, before you brave that tunnel.$B$BMy mountaineers have reported an adventurer that's shown up just outside of Kharanos. Could you deliver these supplies to him?",
[96629]="So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.$B$BCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.",
[96630]="<The journal appears to be quite plain, detailing the life and adventures of someone you've never heard of.$B$BThere are multiple entries mentioning camping. It seems to be quite... fun.>",
[96634]="So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.$B$BCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.",
[96638]="More and more adventurers like yourself have been seeking glory and fortune outside of the safety of Thendal Grove. There's one such adventurer who has made a camp outside of Shen'dar Village, along the road leading southwest out of Thendal Grove.$B$BSeek him out and see what you can learn from him that may help you in your own travels.",
[96646]="So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.$B$BCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.",
[96652]="<The journal appears to be quite plain, detailing the life and adventures of someone you've never heard of.$B$BThere are multiple entries mentioning camping. It seems to be quite... fun.>",
[96655]="So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.$B$BCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.",
[96656]="$n, you have proven yourself trustworthy in your endeavors against the Scarlet Crusade so far. That is why I am now entrusting you with an unusual task.$B$BI've heard of a new adventurer down the road by Brill. Go and see what she's doing.",
[96658]="So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.$B$BCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.",
[96659]="Wait, $n. I have another ask of you, before you leave us.$B$BThere is an adventurer by the name of Kaga Wildhoof who has made camp just outside of Bloodhoof Village. She has greatly helped me in the past, and now I see my chance to repay her. Could you deliver these supplies to her?",
[96661]="So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.$B$BCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.",
[96666]="Barkskin speak more good on you, friend, but there is yet more for you to do.$B$BRaise your hand to our foes. Honor our ways.$B$BWe watch close, and then we will have more to say to you.",
[96674]="<Mirt's eyes grow wide as you approach.>$B$BWhoa, who are you? My mom said there was a new person here. She said you killed a lot of Scourge and are super strong! Have you ever fought a bear? *gasp* A DRAGON!? I--$B$B<Mirt looks behind himself, then looks bashful.>$B$BMaybe... you could help me? I was supposed to be watching the sheep but they got out when I was making mud dragons. They are over on THAT side. I'm not allowed to go over there. Mom says they might hurt me. Could you go find the sheep?",
[96676]="Well, informant, you're being promoted.$B$BTake these updated orders to Johun at his base camp in Hyjal. There's some additional equipment in here that he'll be needing for our operations in the Summit.$B$BYour assistance in these matters is pivotal to our overall strategy in Kalimdor, $n. Tarry not.$B$BYou are dismissed.",
[96770]="There exists a troll witch doctor that goes by the name of Zum'rah. I have history with this particular troll, and I'd like you to kill him for me.$B$BGo to the Sandfury stronghold of Zul'Farrak, deep in the deserts of Tanaris. Find Zum'rah inside and destroy him. Bring his head to me--intact--and I'll see that you are fairly compensated.",
[96771]="In the region known as the Riverglades to the southeast, there is a place called the Krol'dok Stronghold. A highborne known as Zalfan Moonshadow has been seen there in the company of the Twilight's Hammer.$B$BI'd pay handsomely if you'd rid the world of this cretin for me. He brings shame to the proud lineage of the highborne by consorting with fanatics and using stolen arcane knowledge in their service. There are few enough of us left without worms like him sullying our good name.",
[96772]="Timear and I have been scrying the area on Kalimdor known as Alcaz Island and we've all but confirmed the presence of a powerful magic user there. The mage in question was able to dispel our probes, but before she did, I was able to glean an image of a tome of some sort. I believe it was a journal, written in ancient draconic script.$B$BI don't know what is in that book, but I'd like to study it. We want you to travel to the hidden prison beneath Alcaz Island and recover that book for us.",
[96773]="There is a servant of the Lich King that makes his home deep in the quilboar lair known as Razorfen Downs. It is known to us that he makes use of a scrying orb known as \"The Coldbringer's Eye\" to direct the movements of his lesser minions elsewhere.$B$BGo into Razorfen Downs and retrieve the Coldbringer's Eye on our behalf, $c. The Kirin Tor would pay handsomely to obtain this artifact so that we may study it and understand its inner workings.",
[96775]="Ol' Mazu'kon got a bone to pick with a Witch Doctor that go by the name of Zum'rah and I be thinkin' you can help me out with that.$B$BZum'rah practice all his bad voodoo in the Sandfury city of Zul'Farrak, far to the south in the deserts of Tanaris. Go there. Kill Zum'rah, and bring me his head.$B$BTrust me mon, the world be a better place with his head stuck on pike outside my hut than it be sittin' on his shoulders.",
[96776]="I have had a vision.$B$BDeep in the place known as Maraudon, past the earth song falls, there is a chamber filled with brilliant white crystals and guarded by mighty giants. At the highest part of this chamber is a crystal of exceptional brilliance. It is an aspect of the sun god, the right eye of the Earthmother herself--An'she.$B$BI've dreamed of its radiance and it calls to me. $c, remove An'she's Radiance from that place and bring it here where it belongs, under the open skies of Mulgore.",
[96779]="Sometimes, $r, a single cut in the right place will drop a foe dead. The same is often true of organizations.$B$BOur agents have identified a key target among the ranks of the Syndicate: a man by the name of Lord Tomas.$B$BHe plays an instrumental role in the functions of Durnholde Keep, in Hillsbrad Foothills. If you wish to be of service to Ravenholdt, go to Durnholde and eliminate him. The quicker, and quieter, the better.",
[96781]="We have noticed a Syndicate scouting party prowling around the ruins of Alterac, led by a man named Barton.$B$BThey're clearly searching for something, but I cannot know what without reading his scouting reports.$B$BI ask that you pickpocket the report from him, rather than killing him outright. Barton's death will tip off the Syndicate that we're on to them, and they will certainly take counter-measures to cover their tracks.$B$BIf you hope to find him, he is most likely among the Syndicate at Strahnbrad.",
[96782]="It seems our friend Barton here has made this very easy for us. He is after two heirlooms of the Perenolde family within the ruins of Alterac. The Blade of House Perenolde, a sword, and the Royal Aegis of Perenolde, a shield.$B$BFrom the report, it seems these armaments are within two towers among the ruins. Best we acquire them before the Syndicate does.$B$BThe ogres occupying the ruins are fierce, but I trust you should be able to sneak past them without needing to bloody your blade at all.",
[96783]="Stromgarde Keep is one of the Syndicate's largest strongholds. Many of the organization's most important dealings take place behind its walls.$B$BI have received word of a certain trade taking place between members of the Syndicate somewhere in Arathi Highlands, and I'm certain the details of this trade can be found somewhere in Stromgarde.$B$BTo infiltrate the keep without arousing suspicion, you'll need a disguise. See if you can find one among the Syndicate outside the keep, at Northfold Manor.",
[96784]="<You recall Myrokos' instructions to find out about an important deal going on with the Syndicate in Stromgarde Keep. With your disguise, you should be able to talk to members of the Syndicate somewhat freely. Surely, one of them knows something.>",
[96785]="Who do you think you are? Showing up and sticking your nose in official business.$B$BI'm not telling some rookie anything about the higher-up's dealings without good reason. Unless you've got something important, or valuable, for me, I've got nothing to say to you.",
[96786]="Falconcrest sent some guys to do a handoff at the southern part of Thoradin's wall. I don't know what they're picking up. Must be good, because everyone involved has kept it a total secret. I don't think the guys picking it up even know what it is.$B$BThat's all I've got. Don't make me regret telling you that.",
[96796]="This looks like something that the tinker in the hills, Kaylaena, could make use of. She barely visits ever since the loss of her mentor, Yaely.$B$BLook for her workshop in the hills to the north. After Archimonde's fall in the great battle, the two of them scavenged what they could easily bring back themselves, picking many of the machines on these foothills clean.$B$BPutting this debris to new use is better than allowing it to rust here. Your errand helps new life sprout where it was choked by metal.",
[96797]="We often try to find surviving family for many of our charges, and occasionally we find something hopeful. I've received word that Randal here may have a surviving family member. The man's name is Danneth, and he is a soldier stationed at Nethergarde Keep. I need someone to travel there and find the man.$B$BIf you can, please convince Danneth to come retrieve his nephew. I don't think the two have ever met, but they are family all the same and Randal belongs with him.",
[96798]="Sergeant Danneth was last seen on patrol with his squad near Serpent's Coil, just south of Nethergarde Keep. One of the members of his squad stumbled back into the keep, badly wounded and claiming that the entire squad was killed or captured. That soldier died a few hours later, unfortunately.$B$BWe don't have confirmation that Danneth is dead, but chances aren't good. I can't spare the men to push into the cult's lair, but if you wanted to go and look for the man, I'd not refuse the aid.",
[96799]="<Lieutenant Connar listens as you tell him the reason you are here.>$B$BSo, Danneth has an orphaned nephew in Dalaran? If you haven't spoken to him about this yet, I'd suggest you do so. He doesn't exactly seem like the parenting type, but he might surprise me.$B$BIf he does want to go and collect the boy once he's recovered, he has my blessing to take leave for that.",
[96811]="I think I'm ready now. Let's get going when you are ready.",
[96812]="Yes... yes, I will take the boy in. He is family and I'm all he has. I need to recover for a bit longer, but I'll be taking leave and heading to Dalaran as soon as I am able.$B$BPlease return to the Matron and let her know that I am on my way. I'll do my best to ensure that my brother's child is kept safe and grows up strong.$B$BI swear it.",
[96821]="We see fewer and fewer travelers from Razor Hill these days. The scorpids were never much fun, but now I hear there are spiders making their nest along the road.$B$BIf your travels take you up north, kill some of the spiders on your way. Then, let Razor Hill know the path's a bit safer for them.",
[96822]="We lost many brave warriors of the Horde when we sacked Tiragarde Keep. Now that the humans have reinforced the ruins, we cannot collect their remains to properly honor their deaths.$B$BGo to the ruins surrounding the keep, and search for the weapons left by our fallen kin. We will display them in a place of honor.",
[96825]="Our hunters and fishers bring back plenty of savory food for our troops - but it's rare that they get a sweet treat.$B$BI've seen a cactus that produces a prickly, tasty fruit. But it only grows in the hills to the west, where the wretched quilboars make their camps. Make your way past the quilboars and bring me some of those fruits. And be careful - the fruits are as spiny as the quilboars!",
[96830]="My axe still bled demon gore when I heard a human screaming high above.$B$BI looked up and saw this man dangling in the claws of a great chimaera. He fought back fiercly causing the beast to lose its grip and drop him.$B$BFrom that height, no warrior walks away. Even enemies deserve dignity, so I dragged him into the shade to pass in peace.$B$BFor my part, I track the farseers' visions--friends remain in Hyjal, far northwest.$B$BFind the remaining Horde in my stead. Honor requires me here.",
[96833]="Gh... Ghan. Sur... Okk... Ghansurok. That's the fel chimaera's name. I thought I could manage out here... ugh... alone. No chance. Picked me clean into the air.$B$BStuck my dagger through its closest eye I could find, and I fell farther than the tree tops.$B$BI wasn't the only one who bit off more than I could chew this time. Haha--agh... I shouldn't make myself laugh, this hurts bad enough.$B$BBroken bones we could mend, but... the venom... is too vile.$B$BPass on a warning. I beg you!",
[96873]="The trolls east of here have lost their will to the witchdoctor, Zalazane. He uses many cruel magics to keep hold of his prisoners' minds, but one of his favorite tricks is to make them wear pendants wrapped in evil binding spells.$B$BPractice your enchanting skills by stripping the magic from these pendants, and bring me the results. And don't accidentally put one around your neck, if you value your freedom!",
[96874]="Have you seen the huge beasts of Thunder Ridge? I keep thinking the spines on their backs would be perfect for crafting the head of a mighty axe. Saru laughed when I told him... but what does he know!?$B$BAs part of your smithing lessons, you can help me out! Bring me some of those spines, along with grinding stones to sharpen them.",
[96875]="Orgrimmar is always expanding, $c. And when the peons need hides to line the walls and roofs of our new buildings, they come to me!$B$BThe hides of the lizards in Thunder Ridge are typically too thick for armor, but they make excellent building material. Bring me some of their hides, along with a few lighter cured hides. Let's see your skill with leather!",
[96876]="The pack has the name \"Ukor\" crudely stitched along the flap.",
[96877]="The enormous hoof serves as proof of your victory over the mighty lizard.",
[96895]="Not sure if you heard, but two emissaries of the Argent Dawn just passed through here. I don't mind the Argent Dawn, but I don't like them poking around Tirisfal unsupervised either. They were both Forsaken... but that doesn't make me any less nervous.$B$BOne of them just passed by here, headed southeast. There's a group of scourge cultists snooping around the outskirts of the city in that direction. If those two heard about them, there's no doubt that would have caught their attention.",
[96896]="Danitha and I fought against the Scourge in the defense of the Undercity when Naxxramas attacked. We lost many good friends that day, including the hero after which this keep was named--Garek Bandarion.$B$BHe might just have been the first Forsaken to rediscover how to wield the Light as a paladin. I am encouraged to see his legacy and potential live on here with Danitha and her cohort.$B$BIf only the rest of the Forsaken felt the same way...",
[96897]="The Scourge are a blight on our lands, and their living servants are the worst of them. The people of Tirisfal have enough to deal with between the mindless dead and the Scarlet Crusade. If you wish to do some good, help me put an end to this scum.",
[96898]="It wasn't long ago that the citadel of Naxxramas bore down upon this city, intent on wiping the Forsaken off the map. Both the Forsaken and the Argent Dawn lost much that day to secure the future of the Forsaken.$B$BDuring the battle, the great necrotic focusing crystal mounted atop Naxxramas was shattered and its fragments were scattered all over this area. I suspect that is what the cultists are here for. Help me recover the fragments and deprive the Scourge of them.",
[96899]="You've done a great thing for the cause of the Argent Dawn here today, and I thank you. I don't know how familiar you are with the fortress of Bandarion Keep, but my commander and I were headed that way to meet with the paladins that reside there. That was before we learned of the presence of the Cult of the Damned.$B$BIf you'd like to learn more about the Argent Dawn and our mission, seek out my commander at Bandarion Keep, to the northwest of here. I'll remain here to mop up the rest of this mess.",
[96912]="Heya pal, step right up! You look like you know which end of the sword goes where!$B$BIt just so happens that I have a long list of challenges that only the most elite fighters will be able to accomplish. Wanna take a stab at it?",
[96913]="You again, eh? Ready for the next test? I hope you aren't squeamish. You might need to bleed for this one... or preferably make the other guys bleed first.",
[96930]="We need powerful magic indeed to counter the strength that Ve'han Talongrasp now commands. The staff Velician snatched might just be the key.$B$BMy powers as a druid are not what they once were. We will need aid from the divine denizens of the mountain in order to stop this evil.$B$BReturn to the crow you met up the mountain. She is wise but the spirits of the wilds are ever-capricious, even in the face of dire threats. She may be challenging, but we will need her help.",
[96931]="Listen, dirtwalker. I am, of course, known for my intellect and wit but there is one that is even more majestic and powerful than I.$B$BNaturally, I am speaking of cleverest, most cunning, and comely of the Wild Gods, Jereman! Every bird knows her name, and she is wise beyond her wingspan. She certainly will know what is needed for that oldstone's magic.$B$BShe nests up in what you dirtwalkers call the Cradle of Tranquility. Touch the crow effigy on the old bridge and she may appear!",
[96939]="I believe one of my good friends may have an idea for an additional source of power for Ketharas's gambit.$B$BHe is close friend, of course, and he will be thrilled to lend his aid to an agent of my will such as yourself!$B$BYou can find that old stinkfeather in the area south of here that is crawling with undead. Mourning's Rest I think you mortals call it?$B$BMake sure you mention that I sent you! He will LOVE that... most certainly!",
[96957]="Listen, mortal. Though it may not appear a glorious job, those that are under my wing help keep the natural balance. We return many essential nutrients to the soil, allowing for new life.$B$BThese undead have disrupted the cycle here and have driven off those that seek shelter under my wings. While you are out there being the little murderous creature you are, would you collect some bones for me?$B$BI would like to rebuild the nests of my children and followers so we may feast when this blight has ended.",
[96959]="War.$B$BBy the time I heeded the call of our clans, the battle had passed, and only ashes answered my blade.$B$BMy purpose is forged anew.$B$BThis mountain remembers strength--ancient power riding its winds and holding its water. I would earn the right to walk its spine, to reach the fallen stronghold that lies upon the road to the summit.$B$BDemons profane these graves. Before I fight at your side, I must know you stand capable. Light the two bonfires and return to me. Their flames draw our enemy out.",
[96964]="If the hermit truly wants his little gambit to leave the nest and fly, it will likely need a potent energy source. One that can sustain itself without collapse.$B$B<Jereman looks to the sky and clacks her beak together as she considers.>$B$BAh, yes. I know just the clever creature we can consult. Go north into the area you mortals refer to as Dae'gun, the one with the demons, and seek out the fox Wild God Renalard. I believe he will have a solution to our little puzzle.",
[96971]="Say, while you're out and about prancing in my lands, would you mind doing me a favor?$B$BOnce the war had been won, many of the various armies up and left. For whatever reason, they decided some of their supplies were not worth taking. That, or they all died. Who could say?$B$BRegardless, these supplies are of use to my kits and me. Unfortunately they also tend to be where the demons are. Take this tuft of fur with you and use it on the demons to distract them while you grab the tools.",
[96978]="Ever since those nasty Blackthorne druids came to power many of the less powerful gods here on Hyjal have... well to be blunt they've attempted to upend the natural order of things.$B$BThe very worst offender of this is Kala'th.$B$B<Jereman rolls her eyes.>$B$BThat silly deer seems to fashion herself and her herd as predators. Again.$B$BDon't get me wrong, it was quite amusing at first, but now it is time we get things back in wing.$B$BGo speak to her to see if you can bring her back to reason, please.",
[96979]="I am a druid of the Circle, walking the long path to honor the great world tree. I misjudged how much the climb would ask of me, and the winged hunters that haunt these slopes have made caution a necessity. These old ruins offered shelter, and I accepted it.$B$BThis place is suitable for a humble offering, yet no ritual should be given without living water. If you would, fill my gourd at the falls ahead.$B$BWhen you return, speak to me of the trail you walked, and of what stirs upon it.",
[96982]="Ah, I've been expecting you, $c. It would seem the winds have brought you to me this day. You have come seeking a kodo, correct?$B$BThe kodo is a noble beast that is slow to anger, and you would be hard pressed to find a more dependable companion.$B$BToday you have an important choice to make. You and your kodo will travel the world together, so find which one speaks to you. Fear not, whatever choice you make will be the right one.$B$BGo examine the kodos and return to me when you have made your choice.",
[96983]="You're capable, fast, fearless. Fire will draw the demons from their hiding places, and with them, their warlords. They will come seeking dominance. Instead, they will find vengeance waiting. This is the moment where the will of the mountain speaks through us.$B$BCome, let us carve a path through these hellspawn and end their reign. My blade yearns to cleave through their ranks.",
[96991]="The climb grows steeper from here, as you say. Even an empty pack weighs on tired legs. I would ask another kindness of you, traveler. Take my excess gear and carry it ahead to the Summit, where Marn Euhron aids in restoring a foothold near Nordrassil.$B$BI will follow at my own pace when my ceremonies here are complete. When I arrive, I will reclaim them from him and assist him in their work. This way, we both honor the journey and gifts of the mountain.",
[96992]="You know, they packed enough tools to get the essentials started, but there's never enough fastening material. Only so much cordage-winding my hands can take.$B$BResourcefulness is even better than being prepared.$B$BTake an empty bag to the burned-down remains of the alliance buildings around the Cradle of Tranquility southwest of here, and fill it with as many nails and brackets as you can find in the ashes.",
[96994]="Lok'tar, $c. Come to bond with your first wolf? Good.$B$BThere is no stronger bond than that of an orc and their wolf. They are no mere mount, but are a lifelong companion and friend.$B$BOurs is not a bond chosen by vanity. No, each orc and wolf forms a special bond that goes beyond a mere purchase.$B$BThey will choose you as much as you will choose them. You will understand when you meet them.$B$BGo and find which wolf speaks to you. Return to me when you have your answer.",
[96996]="Now that you have completed your training, it would seem the winds wish you to bond with your first strider.$B$BThese galestriders have been ridden by our ancestors for generations. Despite their wispy and slender appearance, they are steadfast and fierce mounts.$B$BYou and your strider will traverse the world together, so you have an important choice to make. Fear not, whatever choice you make will be the right one.$B$BGo examine the striders and return to me when you have made your choice.",
[96997]="Greetings, $c. I imagine I can guess what has brought you to my stables today.$B$BIf you are looking for a mount, you have come to the right place. Be warned though, riding an undead steed is not for the faint of heart.$B$BAs such, you have an important choice to make. You and your undead steed will travel the world together for good or ill. Fear not, whatever choice you make will be the correct one.$B$BGo examine the undead horses and return to me when you have made your choice.",
[96998]="The skeleton still clutching a throwing spear has the telltale signs of a troll headhunter.$B$BIn one of its bony clutches is a wrap of leather adorned with troll characters and smudges of face tints in Darkspear colors. This must have been a makeup pouch used to apply war paint.$B$BDarkspear tribe members may recognize the writing on the sacred skins.",
[96999]="Whoever wore dis fought wit' purpose. An' Sen'jin be a small village... blood an' kin run close dere.$B$BSomebody back home be missin' dis wrap--and da warrior who carried it.$B$BWhen ya trek to Echo Isles, take dis wrap wit' ya. Bring it home to Sen'jin. Dey'll know who it belong to--and dey'll honor ya for seein' it returned.",
[97000]="Before this... second life, I learned the grain of wood in my father's shop.$B$BWhen war reached Hyjal, he stayed behind, crafting arms for those bound to the summit. I fled to Lordaeron. His final letter came from that mountain camp, and no word followed.$B$BMy death was likely no gentler than his. When I rose in Undercity, it felt like years had passed--but barely two had.$B$BYou look capable of the climb. Any remnant you find of my father, Lawrence Sawyer, would bring me solace.",
[97001]="Inside the wardrobe, a ledger records trades of hay, lumber, draft animals, and land. Other notes--personal and unfinished--are tucked between its pages.$B$BThe figures tell their own story: the Sawyer family was skilled at turning timber into weapons, tools, furniture, and wagons alike.$B$BThumbing through the pages reveals other kin of the family. Abigail Sawyer is listed among the relatives.$B$BShe would be very interested in this.",
[97003]="You there, $c. I need your aid. There are rumors of a beast that makes its lair deep in a cave at Thorn Hill, northeast of here. The Razormane call it Chol'aruk or \"The Ravener\". It's supposedly five times the size of a normal quilboar with a thirst for blood that can never be sated.$B$BMost don't believe the tales. But I do--because I've fought its like before.$B$BSeek out its lair and slay Chol'aruk. Bring me its head. I warn you though--prepare well and do not go alone.$B$BBlood and thunder, $c.",
[97006]="I've added a note and my signature beside my name on the original page.$B$BTake it to Royal Overseer Bauhaus at the Undercity Census and explain where it was found. He must know how it came to me while I remained at my shop.$B$BYou can be honest and say to him that Abigail Sawyer told another stranger her sob story and you happened to actually have the means to follow up on it.$B$BAgain, thank you for doing this for my family.",
[97007]="I've stamped the pertinent pages for Abigail's records and updated our own documents.$B$BAbigail will have to send a follow-up to the Royal Census when she intends to transport any of the property into Forsaken territories.$B$BYou may return her ledger and bring with it a reminder: Her contractual obligations to the War Quarter's commissary are not yet fulfilled, so she would be prudent to wait before attempting to act on any of these pre-war ownership claims.",
[97009]="Left bleeding and abandoned--thrown aside so an army could flee. I was meant to die buying them moments.$B$BInstead, I was cursed to endure, forced to watch ever-burning demons finish what steel could not. This is my fate.$B$BBut something is changing. Horde and Alliance return to this desecrated mountain, and war stirs again.$B$BMy fury answers it.$B$BIf yours does as well, prove it. Bring me two handfuls of felhound spikes from these Defiling Hounds.$B$BThe pain will align our wills.",
[97010]="The rune-etched shards are prepared. Dropped from high enough, they'll shatter upon impact, ripping through armor and demon flesh.$B$BThere's a tower overlooking this wasteland. It will give us the height we need.$B$BWe climb. I'll keep to the shadows and guard your flank.$B$BWhen we reach the top, signal me by making the first throw. I'll bring ruin down on them.",
[97017]="Ah, it's a big day fer ya I see; here for yer first ram are ye?$B$BThese rams are the most steadfast and sturdy in all of Azeroth. They're fiercely protective of their rider. Aye, you'll have a hard time finding a more stalwart companion for yer journeys.$B$BSo, you have an important choice to make. You and yer ram will traverse the world together so choose wisely! Not to worry lad, whatever choice you make will be the right one.$B$BGo see the rams and return to me when you've made yer choice.",
[97018]="Hello, $c! It would seem yer now seasoned enough as an adventurer for me ta teach ye how to ride a ram, for a fee o'course.$B$BVeron will provide ye with a free mount once ye have trained with me, and after you'll be able to purchase any additional mounts ye would like. There are many creatures out in the world, and each requires their own riding skill, but ye will have to find trainers for each.$B$BSpeak ta me when you have enough coin, and I'll teach ye all I know about riding rams.",
[97022]="Danitha Morr has ordered you to report back to Bandarion Keep to receive additional training. Please make your way back to the keep as quickly as you are able.",
[97045]="Greetings! Are you here to examine our horses?$B$BThese steeds are descendants from both the historical Lordaeron stock and our own local horses. You won't find a more steadfast companion for your journeys.$B$BChoosing one may be difficult as they are all excellent and trained to be steady even when in danger. Don't forget, you and your horse will traverse the world together. I'm sure whatever choice you make will suit you best.$B$BGo examine the horses and return to me when you have made your choice.",
[97046]="Salutations! I see today is a big day indeed; today you will synchronize your biometrics to the rider detection protocol of your first mechanostrider! This protocol will help the strider distinguish you from other possible riders.$B$BAs such, you have an important choice to make. You and your strider will traverse the world together so choose wisely! Fear not, whatever choice you make will be the correct one.$B$BGo examine the mechanostriders and return to me when you have made your choice.",
[97047]="Hey! You! You have to help me! I was just out exploring the jungle when, all of a sudden, I was ambushed by these maniacs! I don't know what they plan to do with me, but I've heard talk of tigers and headshrinkers, and I don't want part in either!$B$BI don't know how, but you have to get me out of here! Please! A key to this cage, a disguise to sneak out, something! Anything!",
[97048]="Listen, I can't repay you right now, but I'm a cook on Captain Aransas' ship. I'll be sure to put in a good word for you when I get back to Booty Bay. You should speak to the captain when you get the chance. I'm sure she'll be grateful to have me back.",
[97049]="If you're headed into Shaper's Terrace, I would ask a favor of you.$B$BThere are reports of slimes that live in the pools by the colorless Achromatic Crystal. I believe their essence could be of use in my experiments, and would like you to bring me some samples for study.$B$BI will make it worth your while.",
[97074]="Hello, $c! It would seem you are now seasoned enough as an adventurer for me to teach you how to ride a saber, for a fee of course.$B$BLelanai will provide you with a free mount once ye have trained with me, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts ye would like. There are many creatures out in the world, and each requires their own riding skill, but you will have to find trainers for each.$B$BSpeak to me when you have enough coin, and I will teach you all I know about riding sabers.",
[97119]="In addition to seeing to the spiritual needs of the people here, I feed them as well. I'm not exactly a trained cook, but after five years, I've learned a thing or two about preparing food!$B$BI'm sure that folks here would love a taste of something different. I remember, before we assembled on the mountain, there was a goblin from Everlook who was serving platters of tiny, Savory Stag Sliders... I would love to taste one of those again. We have plenty of stags up here, too! Think you can cook some up?",
[97130]="Lan'dalock and I have been discussing a recent development in the south seas involving an ancient Gurubashi ruin that has suddenly appeared off the coast of Stranglethorn Vale.$B$BSuch a site has significant archeological value. We'd be highly interested in obtaining one of the idols that certain witch doctors amongst the ancient Gurubashi would use as a ritual focus for their blood magic.$B$BEnter this \"Drowned City\" and recover one of these idols for us.",
[97168]="$n, the spirits weigh heavy, both materially and spiritually. I'm in need o' yer help. Deep within the depths of the Scholomance in Lordaeron lies the Great Ossuary, thick with shadows. I'm craftin' a device to cut that dark, but I lack the means to finish.$B$BBring me two diamonds: one Azerothian, and one Pristine Black. These are not trivial items, aye -- I just don't have the resources myself. Could ye provide me with the two diamonds?",
[97169]="Death Knight Darkreaver lords over the Great Ossuary in the Scholomance. He threatens to twist the spirit realm to do his own bidding, and he must be stopped! This is where the scryer you helped make comes into play.$B$BUse the divination scryer in the heart of the Great Ossuary's basement to call forth Darkreaver's spirit minions. Defeat the spirits and the death knight himself will appear. $n, bring me his head! Only his demise will reverse the damage done to the spirit realm!",
[97170]="Hello, $c! It would seem you are now seasoned enough as an adventurer for me to teach you how to ride a horse, for a fee of course.$B$BKatie will provide you with a free mount once ye have trained with me, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts you would like. There are many creatures out in the world, and each requires their own riding skill, but you will have to find trainers for each.$B$BSpeak to me when you have enough coin, and I will teach you all I know about riding horses.",
[97171]="Greetings! Are you here to examine our horses?$B$BThese steeds are descendants from both the historical Lordaeron stock and our own local horses. You won't find a more steadfast companion for your journeys.$B$BChoosing one may be difficult as they are all excellent and trained to be steady even when in danger. Don't forget, you and your horse will traverse the world together. I'm sure whatever choice you make will suit you best.$B$BGo examine the horses and return to me when you have made your choice.",
[97173]="The Blackmaw furbolgs in the mountains overlooking Azshara have been dabbling in dark magic. While a primitive people being corrupted by demonic magic is nothing new for Azeroth, Lan'dalock and I would like to study their spell foci.$B$BTravel to the stronghold known as Blackmaw Hold and recover one of the Blackmaw Ritual Totems for us. Only the most powerful of the Blackmaw's shamans will be carrying one of these, so bring allies and take care.",
[97174]="The time has come, $n. As in life, paladins of the Forsaken are not complete until they are able to form a bond with a charger. This is no ordinary steed, this is a powerful spirit of retribution.$B$BSpeak with Danitha Morr at Bandarion Keep to learn more. She will guide you on what to do next. The road before you will be difficult, but as our orc allies like to say--blood and thunder $G brother : sister;!",
[97175]="No worthy endeavor is completed without some sacrifice, and this first task requires just that.$B$BYou must acquire High Priest Zayus's exorcism censer for your task. Even though its use will be for good reason, due compensation must be given for it.$B$BProceed to Orgrimmar and speak with the High Priest Zayus there. Zayus will seek a...\"donation\" for the loss of his censer. It will be a small price to pay when all is said and done.",
[97176]="I have added some dirt from the tainted ground of Terrordale in the Eastern Plaguelands to the censer. Go there and use this censer to find areas with the greatest signs of corruption. You'll know these areas by the green necrotic auras that rise up from the ground at the location where tormented souls congregate.$B$BUse the censer to reveal these spirits. Free them from their torment. When you have put these souls to rest, return and we will discuss the next steps.",
[97177]="With the blessings of the loa, take the censer. I be usin' it more than once to exorcise bad voodoo spirits, and it should serve ya well for the trials what be comin'.$B$BYou best be headin' back to Danitha now, $n. Ya quest continues with her.",
[97178]="A paladin's charger needs a proper barding or it is little more than a mindless beast. The barding used by your charger not only needs to be of the finest materials possible, but must also be suitable for attunement to the spirit realm.$B$BThere is a smith outside of Tarren Mill that has done great work for our paladins in the past. He is a modest and unassuming orc, but his work is superb and is well-suited to our needs. Seek him out and commission him for this task.",
[97179]="We require several things for the barding--runecloth for the lining, arcanite bars for the plating, Arthas' Tears for the spiritual attunement, and Stratholme holy water for the spiritual imbuement. Lastly, I'd charge a modest fee for the labor and for the saddle and stirrups to go with the barding.$B$BBring me these materials, and I will be able to complete your barding. I'll get to work on the saddle while you work on gathering these items.",
[97180]="<Ott wipes the sweat from his brow and grunts at his work approvingly.>$B$BThere you are. My trade is mostly in the creation of weapons, but I believe that this might be some of my finest work nonetheless. I thank you for the trust you and your fellow paladins have shown me.$B$BNo doubt Danitha Morr will want to see the work for herself as well. Take your barding to her, and give her my thanks for allowing me to complete this commission on your behalf.$B$BLok-tar, $c.",
[97182]="A paladin charger's barding requires the blessing of a powerful equine spirit. In the ruins of Dire Maul the corrupted treant known as Tendris Warpwood has such a spirit imprisoned. Seek retribution on behalf of this spirit, and free it from its bondage. With luck, it may be willing to provide its blessing.$B$BTo help ensure success, I'd also advise you to bring a special type of spiritually-attuned feed. Travel to Eastern Plaguelands and speak with the ranger known as Nathanos Blightcaller about this.",
[97183]="As the barding rests on the back of the Ancient Equine Spirit, it glows white hot. The air is thick with power for a brief moment, and then the barding disappears from the back of the horse and is now secure in your backpack.$B$BEven through the leather of your satchel, you feel the heat still coming off of the saddle. It would seem that your offering of vengeance has been accepted, and the barding has been blessed. It's time to return to Danitha Morr at Bandarion Keep.",
[97184]="We now must assemble a Divination Scryer that will be vital for your final trial. The exorcism censer you used in Terrordale is the catalyst for it, and I should be able to fashion a suitable housing for the scrying device.$B$BThe last components needed, though, are two diamonds--one white, one black. This represents the duality of our nature as paladins of The Forsaken. These two will be the beacon by which the scryer will pierce the veil between the living and the dead.",
[97185]="In this satchel you will find the items you will need for your trial. Use the divination scryer in the heart of the Great Ossuary's basement to bring forth accursed spirits to face justice. The power of your judgements will be extremely valuable in this battle, so use them wisely.$B$BOnce you have dispersed these spirits, Darkreaver will appear. Defeat him and claim the lost soul of the charger. Show it the path of justice and retribution that you walk and with luck, it will take its place at your side.",
[97186]="So you need feed to give to the incorporeal spirit of a horse? Interesting.$B$BYes, I suppose I can help you with what you need. I have spent a considerable amount of time rearing beasts that are... let's say--no longer entirely of this world, and I know a thing or two about how to sustain them.$B$BI simply need some of the spiritually-enriched biscuits that the Argent Dawn sells... and a small offering of gold. For my time, of course.",
[97188]="Greetings, $c! You are now seasoned enough as an adventurer for me to teach you how to pilot a mechanostrider, for a fee of course.$B$BMilli will provide you with a free mount once you have trained with me, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts you would like. There are many creatures out in the world, and each requires their own riding skill, but you will have to find trainers for each.$B$BSpeak to me when you have enough gold, and I will teach you about riding mechanostriders!",
[97194]="Mok'ra, $c. You are now seasoned enough as an adventurer for me to teach you how to ride one of our wolves, for a fee of course.$B$BOgunaro will provide you with a free mount once you have trained with me, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts you would like. There are many creatures out in the world, and each requires their own riding skill, but you will have to find trainers for each.$B$BSpeak to me when you have enough gold, and I will teach you about wolf riding.",
[97196]="There is a servant of the Lich King that makes his home deep in the Death's Head quilboar lair known as Razorfen Downs. It is known to us that he makes use of a scrying orb to observe and direct the movements of his minions elsewhere.$B$BWith this artifact, we'd be able to hunt down the covert agents of the Scourge and put an end to them and the threat they pose to Kalimdor forever.$B$BGo into Razorfen Downs to the lair of Amnennar the Coldbringer and retrieve the orb known as the Coldbringer's Eye for me.",
[97197]="Muln tells me that there is a location in the deepest depths of a place called Blackrock Mountain where the barrier between Azeroth and the elemental plane has been damaged, allowing a myriad of elemental creatures from the realm of the Firelands to escape into this reality, including giants as large as an Anchor Pylon!$B$BI'd very much like to study any fragments of material that could be gathered from one of these creatures. Would you brave the Blackrock Depths and recover a sample for me?",
[97198]="The Blackmaw furbolgs in the mountains overlooking Azshara have been corrupted by dark and sinister magic. We do not know the full extent of the corruption and what impact it may have upon the elements in the area, but we hope to understand it better.$B$BTravel to the stronghold known as Blackmaw Hold and recover one of the Blackmaw Ritual Totems for us. Only the most powerful of the Blackmaw's shamans will be carrying one of these, so bring allies and prepare for a difficult battle.",
[97200]="Ey, welcome $c! Ya now be seasoned enough as an adventurer for me to teach you how to ride one of our raptors, for a fee of course.$B$BZjolnir will provide ya with a free mount once you have trained with me, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts ya would like. There are many creatures out in the world, and each requires their own riding skill, but ya will have to find trainers for each.$B$BSpeak to me when ya have enough gold, and I will teach ya about raptor riding.",
[97203]="Greetings, $c. It would seem you are now seasoned enough as an adventurer for me to teach you how to ride a skeletal steed, for a fee.$B$BZachariah will provide you with a free mount once you have trained with me, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts you desire. There are many creatures out in the world, and each requires their own riding skill, but you will have to find trainers for each.$B$BSpeak to me when you have enough coin, and I will teach you about skeletal horses.",
[97204]="Greetings, $c. It would seem you are now seasoned enough as an adventurer for me to teach you how to ride a kodo, for a fee of course.$B$BHarb will provide you with a free mount once ye have trained with me, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts you would like. There are many creatures out in the world, and each requires their own riding skill, but you will have to find trainers for each.$B$BSpeak to me when you have enough coin, and I will teach you about riding the noble kodo.",
[97205]="Hello, $c! It would seem you are now seasoned enough as an adventurer for me to teach you how to ride a galestrider, for a fee of course.$B$BI will provide you with a free mount once ye have trained with me, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts you would like. There are many creatures out in the world, and each requires their own riding skill, but you will have to find trainers for each.$B$BSpeak to me when you have enough coin, and I will teach you about riding galestriders.",
[97223]="All of the raptors you see before you are ones I have trained myself. They come from all over Kalimdor, but some of the finest come from the Bloodtalon raptors on the isles off our coast.$B$BOne raptor amongst them, the Bloodtalon Matriarch, is particularly savage and has killed many from our village and has become too dangerous to leave at our borders. If you can strike her down, return with her eggs so that we can raise the hatchlings as allies instead of enemies.",
[97225]="When we fled the isles that Zalazane and his ilk now inhabit, we left behind many precious idols that help us commune with spirits we worship: our loa. They are of grave importance to our tribe.$B$BThe followers of Zalazane show no reverence for our loa and have scattered these idols across the largest of the isles.$B$BThis is an action that will not go unnoticed if we are not able to collect these idols, and offending a loa is a grave matter.$B$BGo, find as many loa idols as you can and return them to me.",
[97236]="A fresh specimen from a beast of this size is quite a find. Perhaps someone in Aldrassil familiar with the study of spiders would be interested in the fang.",
[97242]="Yelmak doesn't want his apprentice breaking anything. Well, anything more than he already has.$B$BHe told me the young mixer in training has too much pride to ask for help when he really needs it. Yelmak wants to give him a taste of a particular home-brewed recipe.$B$BGather a mix of cattail and speargrass cuttings taken from the plants growing around the water in the Valley of Honor. I'd get them myself, but if I left the shop, Whuut would surely know we're catering to his mood.",
[97243]="Even though we are in the realm of Skywall, this is still the elemental plane. The spirits of all four elements speak to us, if we deign to listen. One among us Windshapers is in particular attunement with the element of fire. A shen'dorei by the name of Olariaan Swiftburn.$B$BBring this to him at the Shrine of Flames in the Gustberry Lowlands. You'll find it tucked away along the edge of the island, west of Valanaar.",
[97244]="There is an Al'Aketh Skypriest called Faladiel. He was once a caller of the flame and a stalwart Windshaper. Like so many Al'Aketh, he mortgaged his loyalty for power and his hands are now stained with the blood of his former brothers and sisters.$B$BYou will find Skypriest Faladiel at the farm to the northeast past Valanaar, just to the south of the Shrine of Akir. Kill the betrayer. Bring me his heart. It is a gruesome task, but it is needed for the ritual we are to perform.",
[97245]="The residents of the Shen'dar Highlands speak of an ancient forest sprite called Kuramaa. They say it lives inside of a twisted stump at the summit of a hill near the highlands Anchor Pylon.$B$BGo to the highlands and find this stump. Rap your fist upon the bark and Kuramaa will appear. Best the spirit in combat, and bring me its wooden mask.$B$BBe warned however, this entity will be exceptionally resistant to much of your magic. Only the touch of flame will lay low the spirit.",
[97246]="My son, Migi, always takes off to play with his friends all day. I tell him to pick up a lunch at Borstan's, but I know he almost never does, because he comes home starving. These kids think their games are more important than their own bodies!$B$BPlease, stop at Borstan's Firepit and tell him you're there to deliver Migi's lunch. You can almost certainly find Migi behind Grommash Hold with the rest of his friends.$B$BDuties keep me here during the day and I can't watch over his every meal.",
[97249]="Now that I know his parents worry about how much he's actually filling that belly, I've got an idea.$B$BThey made me promise not to pack the same meal every day, so Migi grows a taste for more than one thing. Still, whenever the smoker's full and we're making sweetglazed hog belly sandwiches, he always shows up for lunch. We've started crumbling the leftover crispy glazed bits as a topping--something we can add daily.$B$BTake this to him. Maybe he'll start showing up early and bringing friends!",
[97253]="Hey, got a sec?$B$BSo, apparently, nobody I've sent to deal with the recent pirate problem has come back alive. After five or six attempts I thought, \"what if I sent a machine instead?\" Turns out, scimitars double as screwdrivers in a pinch, and before I could redirect it home, it was already in pieces and scattered across their camp!$B$BI need those parts back, and since this is a quick little retrieval mission, I'd wager your odds for survival are MUCH higher than the others. Whaddya say?",
[97257]="Now we will perform the ritual.$B$BI will place the materials onto the altar and call forth the spirits of flame. If the offering is accepted, they will appear and light the Eternal Flame. You will then hold your torch forth and capture the flame.$B$BCarry the lit torch to Valanaar and place it in the Brazier of Eternal Flames. You must do so quickly, for the flames of the Firelands are quick to dissipate here in Skywall.",
[97264]="The Shardtooth are becoming more rabid every season. They compete with each other and the predators of the wilds for what limited food sources they can reach.$B$BMore often, they attack us, hunger driving their aggression in the bitter cold.$B$BThe bears are numerous and strong-willed. With their numbers reduced, the families that remain will grow stronger than ever.$B$BHelp them on their way. Cull the eldest of them.",
[97265]="Ever strike a deal with a satyr, mon?$B$BI have. How could I resist? The promise of power, knowledge far exceeding what any ordinary tome could offer... all alongside an eager and charismatic minion. What more could I ask for?$B$BBah, of course they would never bend the knee to a mortal. I bargained when I had nothing, only to be cast aside with even less.$B$BNow, I want revenge. Revenge against the Hatefury. Raid their camp to the northeast! Stain the dirt with their foul blood.",
[97270]="There must be more to the Maul than this!$B$BPerhaps the loud Spectator who oversees the event at Dire Maul will know!",
[97275]="Whuut is a prodigy. That much is true. But he doesn't yet have the experience, wisdom, and time on the stirring rod to know how to respect alchemical processes.$B$BHe is exhausting all of the rarest and most exotic reagents we have available without pausing to practice and refine his basic skills.$B$BGive him this potion I've brewed with a quick tonic method. He'll reconsider everything he's doing when he learns how local remedies and careful touch are the first true mastery.",
[97279]="With an influx of new recruits like yourself, it's been hard to keep our weapons supplied. Our weaponsmith, Kzan, is running low on training weapons and I'd like to see what kinds of skills you possess to get an idea of what I have to work with. Luckily for you, I have a solution to both.$B$BWhile you're out there cutting your teeth on boars, salvage six abandoned training weapons. Our failed recruits left them laying on the ground. Once you do, return them to our weaponsmith Kzan behind me in the Den.",
[97281]="<Before you is a strange orb with a dull surface. When picked up a small electrical current seems to vibrate from within. Upon closer inspection, it looks as if a dark mist swirls within and every so often a small electrical spark can be seen.$B$BIt is clear the harpy was using it for some purpose. Perhaps Rezlak would be interested in this object?>",
[97282]="\"Rezlack, when an opportunity comes knocking make sure you're ready to seize it.\" That's another gem Gazlowe taught me and that's exactly what I intend to do.$B$BThis orb doesn't seem damaged, it just looks like it's out of juice, but I've the idea to supercharge it back to full strength!$B$BThere are a bunch of thunder lizards in a gorge west of here. They have organs that hold a strong electrical charge that would be perfect for this.$B$BGo harvest some and bring them back to me!",
[97284]="If Malem is still alive, then I suspect the Burning Blade orcs are expecting someone to come searching for her soon enough. They will certainly be ready for a fight.$B$BI would prefer if you kept a low profile and stayed out of their way, but the far more likely reality is that they will be looking to meet you, blade to Burning Blade, at every opportunity.$B$BSo how about we plan to keep score from the start. Kill as many as you can, and I'll make it worth your time.",
[97319]="A cousin of mine on Kalimdor has been cutting his way through the most dangerous sites there and, last I heard, is on his way to Mount Hyjal.$B$BThis seems like a ridiculous waste of time.$B$BIf you ever find yourself out in that part of the world, it would be good to know that he hasn't gotten himself killed. Yet.",
[97326]="Hey! You've got time to help us out! I know you do, I can tell by the way you smiled watching the game we're playing.$B$BThis spot behind Grommash Hold is nice because it's clear enough for us to set up our figures. But what stinks is we don't have enough rocks for chairs or tables.$B$BYou're big and strong... d'ya think you could carry back some medium-sized rocks, smooth enough to sit on if we need a rest?",
[97327]="It breaks my heart to admit, but my brothers and sisters inside Blackmaw Hold are irreparably corrupted.$B$BIf you bring me some of their personal belongings, I can at least give their families something to remember them by. Every bundle you recover will serve as a symbol of your service to my people.",
[97328]="<As you sift through the debris left behind by a horrible zeppelin crash directly above, you find evidence of a hefty shipment of supplies that has long since been plundered of all its value. Even the shipping labels have been torn and shredded, leaving only the words 'Booty Bay' barely legible on one.$B$BCountless two-toed footprints and several patches of divotted earth all lead toward ruins in the northwest.>",
[97329]="You! Yes, you! Come here, keep your voice down!$B$BI screwed up big time. I managed to secure a sweet deal for Booty Bay to use their zeppelin tower for expedited deliveries and on our very first route I saw a huge bird--err, got SHOT DOWN just to the east of here!$B$BI survived the crash, unfortunately, but before I woke up, I was already being dragged by my ears! Now I'm surrounded by bloodthirsty trolls and locked in a cage!$B$BLook, I just need the key, okay? I can escape on my own.",
[97331]="Wait, wait, don't go yet!$B$BI know I said I just needed the key but... well, they caught me once, they could do it again, right? I'm just one goblin, and there's hundreds of trolls around here!$B$BYou've already put enough of a dent in their numbers to get this key, so it should be easy enough to stand guard while we mosey on out of here, huh?",
[97332]="As much as I don't like the guy, I've heard what the Bloodscalp tribe do to their prisoners, and it ain't pretty. I'm glad Zimmix made it out alright.$B$BHowever, I have another urgent delivery and I do NOT trust him to take it on. The problem? Nobody else will be available to take this before he does. You, however, have rescued lost cargo and a captured goblin, so you're looking pretty trustworthy from down here.$B$BAny chance I can convince you to take this to Whizzbuzz at Powderfuse Port?",
[97378]="$n, you have proven you are a strong and dutiful hunter and I am impressed by your bravery. It is only because of this I offer you this hunt.$B$BA wind serpent hunts along a road off the coast of Feralas and has been ambushing travelers, and leaving their corpses strewn about the road. It is clear she does not hunt out of necessity. This is a creature that no longer shares the Earthmother's blessing.$B$BThe windserpent Mirrorscale makes her lair at the bottom of the waterfall along the coast of Feralas.",
[97386]="$n! Your arrival is timely, as always.$B$BYou have provided valuable assistance to the defense of Grom'gol, and we are grateful. After your recent push against the ogres nearby, we sent out a scout to see if there are more out there that may try to enact vengeance against us. As it turns out, there is a cave far to the east that they have claimed as their hovel.$B$BGather a friend or two and make it very clear that we will not tolerate another threat to our settlement, now or ever!",
[97403]="These chimaeras are a cruel joke. Two tongues, both foul, snarling frost and hunger. As if this wasteland needed more teeth.$B$BThis clearing is all we have, constantly overcome by storms before we can settle further. The two-headed Chillwind Ravagers circle us, testing our resolve, bleeding our time.$B$BWe spend more hours driving them back than building anything of worth.$B$BCull them. Break their presence here. With fewer prowling beasts, we may yet carve something lasting from this frozen waste.",
[97404]="There are two old matriarchs, long aged past their cub rearing cycles. Perhaps they are sisters. They could also be two kindred bears who've shared a similar passing of seasons.$B$BRegardless of what has brought them together, they still have a ferocity and will to live that demands respect. Attempting to set up a camp like this one has been difficult for us, with these two grizzled Shardtooths.$B$BBring back the heads of Kuroma and Kamuro, and try to end them swiftly, skillfully, and with mercy.",
[97405]="Gnaz over there has been building that death trap for the competition all the way over in Kalimdor. I have been warning him that his constant late-night tinkering is making a ton of noise, and last night I saw an ogre peeking his ugly head out from behind that tree!$B$BHe's obsessed with this ambitious dream to win the Mirage Raceway Championships, but I'm obsessed with not getting mauled to death! Please head over the hill to the north and make sure they stop snooping around the place.",
[97411]="Hail, $c! I can tell by your demeanor that you've seen and done much in this world. Yet I'm willing to wager you haven't seen a piece of armor like this.$B$BPerform a small favor for me and I'll be willing to trade it to you for an ordinary set of bracers.$B$BI'm in need of a sizeable sample of venom drawn from the spiders and scorpions that inhabit Silithus. Bring this to me along with a few gold coins and I'll perform the exchange.",
[97413]="Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet. In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.$B$BThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together. Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces. Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.$B$BI, for once, shall rest in peace. I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!",
[97446]="Ah, I've been expecting you $c. It would seem the winds have brought you to me this day. You have come seeking a kodo, correct?$B$BThe kodo is a noble beast that is slow to anger, and you would be hard pressed to find a more dependable companion.$B$BToday you have an important choice to make. You and your kodo will travel the world together, so find which one speaks to you. Fear not, whatever choice you make will be the right one.$B$BGo examine the kodos and return to me when you have made your choice.",
[97447]="Well met, $c. I've something that might interest you.$B$BI have in my possession a set of armor much like the one worn by those of your profession, but of much higher quality. I'd be willing to trade the bracers for ordinary ones in exchange for a small favor.$B$BThe blood of the frostsabers and bears that inhabit Winterspring has properties I'm in need of at the moment. Bring me a sizeable sample of it along with the bracers and a small amount of gold. You shall find the effort worth your while.",
[97453]="Hi, can you help me?$B$BMy parents finally let me come along with them to this big jungle and they even let me pick a few plants just outside the gates. I'm trying to study herbalism so I can be an alchemist one day!$B$BAnyway, I almost filled my backpack when a bunch of huge, angry weeds came out of nowhere and started spitting at me!$B$BI ran away, and I'm fine, but now they won't let me play outside of the camp anymore. Can you make it safe for me, and then tell my mum?",
[97485]="Blessings of An'she, friend.$B$BWe tauren have a tradition of scattering incense to the winds and I was hoping you'd be interested in honoring this tradition.$B$BYou will need to craft the incense by purchasing herbs from Nida, cedar from Nata, sinew thread from Mahu in the mid rise, and ceremonial flint and tinder from Naal on the upper rise. Once you have these items, combine them and spread them off the south facing cliff of Hunter's Rise.$B$BYou will find a mat and incense at the ceremonial site.",
[97490]="Hey bub, I'm trying to break down some junk to get parts for my machine, but things are gettin' too hot.$B$BI know what you're thinking, Winterspring? Getting hot? As you can see, my crusher and reployer are running, but sputtering hard! What they really need is something to cool 'em down that won't melt, slide, or burn off.$B$BIn the southern hills roams a nasty giant we call Hailspite. Put an end to Hailspite and bring me the frosty moss that grows on his crags.$B$BIt might work for me!",
[97530]="A merchant caravan took a wrong turn through the desert and got jumped by the Dunemaul ogres. Only reason they made it out alive is 'cause they tossed some cargo overboard to distract the brutes.$B$BMust be this merchant's got friends with the nobs runnin' ships and zeppelins, 'cause now they want ME pickin' up what got lost.$B$BI'm stuck here working. But if YOU see a nice shiny bangle while you're beatin' on ogres, I'll make it worth ya while.",
[97534]="Pssst, wanna know somethin'? It's easier to make profit in a place like this than you think... it's all about knowing how to market! I've seen what these tech-heads do when they get their hands on something they think they can turn into a fuel cell.$B$BEven better if it's still glowin' or sputtering steam.$B$BWhy don't we strike a deal? Bring back some of the parts that fall off their machines in the desert, and I'll kick you back a share of the coin I get from selling the salvage back to the junkers!",
[97536]="The Matter Transporter required experimentation to get right. Many tests were conducted on all sorts of materials... with various outcomes! Some of the results are no longer with us. Others have become dangerously charged!$B$BThese subjected objects emit an energy that burns if you stay near for too long. Almost like they've been charged with a year's worth of the desert sun's power.$B$BTake this Crate of Radioactive Refuse and empty the contents in the sand a safe distance from town and other trash.",
[97540]="Oh, this fresh water smells so good...$B$BI'm going to stop for a moment and have a quick swim and a drink.",
[97558]="One part of undeath no one mentions is what happens when we are injured. How does the skin of an undead heal itself?$B$BWell, it doesn't.$B$BOurs is a cursed life, $n. We must take from the living to further our own existence.$B$BWhen we sustain an injury, we must replace our skin which usually means animal hides. Since different hide thicknesses are better for different places on our bodies a variety is key!$B$BBring me wing membranes of a duskbat, hides from a darkhound and skin of a Vile Fin murloc.",
[97617]="Hullo there, you look like the helpful sort.$B$BThe name's Dorgaron, and I'm with the Explorers' League. We've not had the best of luck with diggin' in the Badlands, but I know darn well there's artifacts to find and collect!$B$BBefore I can convince the boss to let us send another crew out here, I need to prove that the dig sites are safe AND haven't been picked clean.$B$BIf you find yourself down south, gather a few reasonably intact artifacts and some leftover equipment that hasn't been smashed yet.",
[97663]="I noticed a few rocks that seemed unusual in the Dustbowl. Upon closer inspection, I saw that they had carvings! I could not resist making rubbings of them to study later.$B$BThe nearby ogres took notice of my presence and before I could even react, I woke up under the care of the innkeeper, and with a terrible headache.$B$BNow, I am down all of my supplies and without any study material while I heal. Can you venture to the east in search of my pack, and take rubbings of the etchings yourself?",
[97821]="<Upon the elemental's demise, a relic fell from its core that glimmered in the sand.$B$BAs it was tilted in your hands, the reflection of the surrounding environment obscured it from your own view. Only once you saw a cracked surface that warped the reflection was it clearly visible again.$B$BPerhaps someone would be interested in this discovery.>",
[97883]="Bring Blackhand's head to Major Mattingly at the city gates. He and his men will proclaim the great victory you have achieved this day, so that the rest of the Alliance may be inspired by it.$B$BYou've done a great justice this day, $n. One that all will remember--including our enemies.",
[97891]="You! Quickly, I need you to bring this potion across the slime canal to Doctor Martin Felben in the Apothecarium!$B$BIt has a very limited shelf life, and no I can't go myself, my knees rattle and pop out if I attempt to run.$B$BJust another lovely side effect of undeath, apparently.$B$BBut we're wasting time! Here, take this and go!$B$B<Alessandro makes a shooing motion.>",
[97899]="So, you chose to cook up brews and potions as an Alchemist. I'm sure that'll come in handy in your travels.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste.",
[97900]="So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons.",
[97901]="Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.",
[97902]="Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.",
[97903]="So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a $c.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives.",
[97904]="You might not think so, but your skill as a fisherman can actually come in handy at camp.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Fish Bowl for your camp. You can use this fixture to help provide a bit of joy to yourself and your fellow adventurers. A happy adventurer is a strong adventurer and I'm sure your combat capabilities will reflect that.",
[97905]="Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate.",
[97906]="You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, $c. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.$B$BWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels.",
[97907]="Mining isn't the most glamorous, but it's good honest work and a fine profession for you to explore.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Lodestone for your camp. Build one of these and everyone who wants to swing a sword will be eager to gather round your fire and soak up the extra \"oomph\" it can provide to increase their combat prowess.",
[97908]="Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up.",
[97914]="Auberdine is a humble place, $c. You won't hear its name spoken in the boughs of Darnassus. Most reference only what the Sundering took from us--the thriving cities of Ameth'Aran, Bashal'Aran, and... Lathar'Lazal.$B$BYet Auberdine remains in their shadow.$B$BI would see our work here recognized. A new vessel connects us to the kingdom of Stormwind, bringing life and supplies to our shores. I beseech you to join its next voyage, and bring this letter to a human called Baros Alexston.$B$BMake our home known.",
[97915]="So, you chose to cook up brews and potions as an Alchemist. I'm sure that'll come in handy in your travels.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste.",
[97916]="So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons.",
