[97960]="Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up.",
[97961]="Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.$B$BI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.",
[97963]="So, you chose to cook up brews and potions as an Alchemist. I'm sure that'll come in handy in your travels.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste.",
[97964]="So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons.",
[97965]="So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a $c.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives.",
[97967]="You might not think so, but your skill as a fisherman can actually come in handy at camp.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Fish Bowl for your camp. You can use this fixture to help provide a bit of joy to yourself and your fellow adventurers. A happy adventurer is a strong adventurer and I'm sure your combat capabilities will reflect that.",
[97968]="Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate.",
[97969]="You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, $c. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.$B$BWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels.",
[97971]="Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up.",
[97972]="Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.$B$BI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.",
[97973]="Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.$B$BI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.",
[97977]="The Gnarlpine furbolg would not turn on their ancient allies so readily. We must learn more of their plight.$B$BSearch their abandoned homes for totems. If any survived the chaos of their departure, their engravings may tell us more of what happened here.$B$BYou'll find their camps along the western edge of the glen, though the grell and grellkin may have scattered them beyond.",
[97979]="You are born kaldorei--the children of the stars--and have inherited a birthright unlike any other in this world. Elune's grace may illuminate our strengths, helping our strikes hit true, or it may help conceal us just as the moon may eclipse the sun.$B$BOur Long Vigil after the defense of Mount Hyjal has ended, and we have joined an Alliance of others--which you will meet in due time. For now, you are nestled in the boughs of Teldrassil.$B$BDemonstrate Mother Moon's gifts, and bask in her blessings.",
[97987]="Around the time these cliffs collapsed, I heard elvish ballistae firing. Bolts struck dangerously close to my home along the road to Quel'Thalas.$B$BI fled, leaving the avalanche of trees and rubble behind. I heard shouts in what could only have been shen'dorei! It was harsh even to my ear. I caught only a few words: \"traitor,\" \"blood,\" \"enemy.\"$B$BMy suggestion: take this knowledge to Saera Wirraway, a high order skyborne in Stormwind's Park. Though not of one line, we once shared a heart for answers.",
[97988]="Around the time these cliffs collapsed, I heard elvish ballistae firing. Bolts struck dangerously close to my home along the road to Quel'Thalas.$B$BI fled, leaving the avalanche of trees and rubble behind. I heard shouts in what could only have been shen'dorei! It was harsh even to my ear. I caught only a few words: \"traitor,\" \"blood,\" \"enemy.\"$B$BTake this knowledge to Corswyn Aseril, a windshaper skyborne in Orgrimmar's Valley of Wisdom. Though not of one line, our hearts once sought the same truth.",
[98013]="Steel yourself for your time in the ruins, young one... you will not be granted free passage there.$B$BScores of cursed Highborne, now known as naga, roam the once great city. Travel northeast and dispatch them from this land.$B$BWhat they once were... is no more. If they aid the Twilight's Hammer, they can bring only further pain to the forests that once gave them shelter.$B$BWar is what they seek, $c. War... is what we will bring.",
[98021]="If you'd like to get started doing some good in our world, I'd recommend reporting to a man named Gryan Stoutmantle in Westfall to the south, at the settlement known as Sentinel Hill. His people are in need of aid.$B$BAfter journeying here from another plane of existence, the problems our lands face may seem small. I assure you, the aid you provide to those impacted by such problems means everything to them, and you will grow stronger for your labors.$B$BGood luck out there, adventurer!",
[98024]="After journeying here from the elemental plane, the problems our lands face may seem small. Rest assured, the dangers the horde faces are very real, and you will grow formidable should you survive your service.$B$BIf you'd like to get started doing some good in our world, travel southwest to the vast lands known as the Barrens. There is a settlement there known as the Crossroads. The proud citizens there are ever in need of aid.$B$BGo with honor, adventurer!",
[98025]="Attention!$B$BA reward is being offered for the death of the owl \"Jai'vhanel\" also known as \"Swordfeather\".$B$BUnfortunately this owl has gone mad and has begun to attack travelers as they journey along the road near Auberdine.$B$BJai'vhanel was last seen north of the Ameth'Aran ruins near the mountain base. Bring back one of her jet black feathers as proof of her death.$B$BReward claims for this bounty should be claimed with Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine.$B$BThe Auberdine Village Council",
[98027]="<The silver necklace in your hands gleams gently as you examine it. The small crescent moon shape seems similar to other night elf symbols you've seen before.$B$BUpon flipping the necklace over there is a small inscription: \"Alor'lormah, Maliynn\". Perhaps it belongs to Maliynn in Astranaar?>",
[98028]="All that remains of the powerful elemental is a globe of what seems to be pure water, clouded by some unknown substance. The edges of the sphere seem to be clear until you turn it--as if the cloud actively prevents you from peering within.$B$BWhatever happened to it--and to the ruins it was guarding--is still active in some way.$B$BOnly Onu, the Ancient of Lore at the Grove of the Ancients to the far south, would have a chance at knowing more.",
[98042]="<As you tear away the single page from the Twilight Tome, a foreboding voice floods your mind, uninvited.>$B$BThey have failed.$B$BYou will be forgotten.$B$BThey will lose the eye they gained.",
[98046]="<Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm's gaze narrows.>$B$BYou're still here?$B$BTake the phial and get out of my sight, $c. It is clear my answers do not lie in the waters, just as they did not before.$B$BPerhaps one of the priestesses in the Temple of the Moon to the south will dispose of it.$B$B<Fandral looks away, no longer speaking to you.>$B$BI must look elsewhere if this is to work...",
[98059]="Hillsbrad's council hasn't answered our new magistrate's letters. The last word I pried out of a passing merchant from the town did little to justify their silence.$B$BWe're only asking for a small platoon--yet I'm told multiple siege ballista rest in pristine condition within a walled-off compound.$B$BWalk into their town hall like a citizen returning a census request, and place this neatly upon the bookkeeping table.$B$BReturn to me when the deed is done.",
[98065]="You must bring this to Tyrande at once! I will transfer it to a more ceremonial container for you.$B$BDo not be afraid. The High Priestess of Elune is firm, but kind. She protects all who enter Darnassus, and carries our goddess' light to all.$B$BShe will be glad to receive this sacred water. You will find her directly above us.",
[98071]="Worked a bit o' a trade with the Dun Garok brew-kin. We're not the only ones missin' the vineyards of the Fallrook family, it seems! Most o' the best bottled years are long since drank, but we do have cases of the wine still in the cellars.$B$BBring this case of Fallrook Varietal to Dun Garok in the southeast and leave it with 'em by their gatherin' fireplace at the bottom of their fort.$B$BIn return, carry a sack o' the Homebrew Hops back with ye.$B$BThat keep is the closest thing to home around here!",
[98072]="You're quite the go-getter! I have just one more favor to ask, if you're up for something a bit more dangerous.$B$BThe crocolisk trade is steady money, but they're small fish compared to what whelp scales will bring. Folks will pay top dollar for a sack of those.$B$BCrocs of the sky, I call 'em! There's no way my apprentice could get them--but it seems right up your alley!$B$BYou'll find whelps far to the east, along the Green Belt. But be careful, there's nasty orcs in those hills!",
[98093]="I'm so glad you saw me!$B$BThe weather was lovely this morning, so I walked from Camp Taurajo down the golden road. When it came time to head back, I couldn't--a pack of hyenas started circling, and Stormhide lizards blocked my only escape.$B$BScrambling up this tree I went, and now there are too many foes about at this hour for me to make the run home through the fields.$B$BWould you mind clearing out these Stormhide and Hecklefang Stalkers for me?",
[98094]="Now that we can trust you to deliver critical information to our forward spies, there's an extra task for you.$B$BBring this to Deathstalker Masoj almost directly south of us. He'll have more for you to do once you get there and hand this to him. He is posted on elevated terrain north of the rotten vineyard they call Nethander Stead.$B$BOur plan to take control of these lands continues steadily.",
[98095]="Our high command inserts strategic troops using bat riders. Key points around the foothills have lost their signaling beacons.$B$BTake these vials. Uncork them in three locations: the hills bordering Dun Garok, the plateau overlooking Dunholde Keep, and the last on the ridge of the Headland above the town of Hillsbrad. The vapors that emanate will be like a potent tuning rod to the senses of the bat, drawing them to the desired drop-off points once more.$B$BLook for crushed empty vials and renew our marks.",
[98096]="I joined the Sentinels following my elder sister, Keldara. She's stationed out at Talrendis Point in Azshara. I sadly have not seen her for some time.$B$BIf you are able, would you be willing to make sure she's okay? She hasn't responded to my last letter... I fear the worst.$B$BShe reports to Commander Truesong. I would start there and follow the chain of command--I wouldn't want you to get into trouble on my behalf!",
[98109]="Hailen last said she was only going to survey the north reaches, so if it was her you found, there must be more to the story. Her last report contained useful intelligence regarding the stalwart ranger redoubt of Quel'Lithien Lodge.$B$BThere is a high elf, Adon, that resides northwest of the ruins of Northdale, near the road to Quel'Thalas. He might have a better understanding of the elven movements through these territories.$B$BI'll ensure we have a burial for this soul, whomever it may be.",
[98155]="The Pesterhide hyenas of Thousand Needles have the most gorgeous coats. I haven't seen such a brilliant hue of fur like that in all of my travels!$B$BI would like to send back some pelts to my sisters back in Stormwind, as I know they could make something incredible out of them.$B$BI don't have any fighting experience, so I would be very grateful if you could gather some of the Pesterhide pelts in my stead.",
[98156]="$n, you have been so helpful to me I hate to ask for yet another favor. It will be some time until I am able to return home to Stormwind. I was wondering if you would mind delivering these pelts to my sisters in my stead?$B$BI am sure you are more likely to return there before I am able to. Please deliver these pelts to my sisters Kelly and Kimberly in Stormwind. They can usually be found in the Park.",
[98166]="Greetings! Are you here to examine our horses?$B$BThese steeds are descendants from both the historical Lordaeron stock and our own local horses. You won't find a more steadfast companion for your journeys.$B$BChoosing one may be difficult as they are all excellent and trained to be steady even when in danger. Don't forget, you and your horse will traverse the world together. I'm sure whatever choice you make will suit you best.$B$BGo examine the horses and return to me when you have made your choice.",
[98189]="My goodness, it's--it's beautiful!$B$BThe Blind Princess was to deliver this to Menethil Harbor before tragedy struck. We were so close!$B$BI believe it was to be signed for by Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Keep just behind us. Why don't you do the honors of finishing the job?",
[98190]="You'll want to take this to Stormwind right away. Proud as I am that this keep and harbor bears King Terenas Menethil II's name, we are a calm harbor in a very nasty storm of enemies. It's just not safe here.$B$BThe Dragonmaw in particular would sacrifice much to loot something like this... and I shudder to think of what they'd do with it.$B$BDon't bother going up the chain of command on this one, $Glad:lass;. Go straight to Highlord Fordragon with this. He'll know where it will be best kept.",
[98192]="You little! You help Krak smash the red bities and get scale hide!$B$BKrak smash red bities to take scale hide, but Krak hands too big. Krak keep cutting hides, make them full of holes.$B$BBut you little! You go get hides from red bities in Dragonmurk in south. They mean and fast. You little, could get eaten.",
[98197]="This harbor was first built by the Old Horde as a staging ground for their naval invasion of Hillsbrad. Completely circumvented Lordaeron's defenses!$B$BSo many lives lost...$B$BWhat's worse is that fleet was built with the very resources they stole from Khaz Modan!$B$BPlenty of it remains in the harbor after Admiral Proudmoore routed the brutes and built this place for the Alliance. We'll need it to bolster the town's defenses with the Dragonmaw on the move.",
[98203]="The Witherbark know we be huntin' them like the traitors they are. Makin' plans and hideouts to keep their tribe in the shadows even after we burn 'em for their deceit.$B$BOur scouts be findin' a cave west of Hiri'watha. One witch doctor, Ti'ik, he bring his voodoo inside--rot, decay, an' wrigglin' larvae for some foul magic.$B$BWe not lettin' that filth crawl through our homes while we sleep. Go, take his head, and crush whatever they be growin'.$B$BHe be tough, so don't go underestimatin' him, ya?",
[98205]="My associate Gizzix and I are looking to set up an outpost, and I can smell an opportunity here!$B$BOr maybe that's just the swamp gas. Either way, I could use some help.$B$BThe little black dragons flyin' around here haven't exactly been \"friendly\". They even singed poor Miss Melly!$B$BLook, I have some good coin for you if you're willing to get rid of some of these horrible dragon whelps.$B$BSo, you in or not?",
[98208]="I came to Menethil Harbor from Auberdine, from the great tree Teldrassil, to recover a bloom of great import to my people.$B$BMy people's ship the Flying Osprey crashed here many moons ago, joined with the Kul Tiran Third Fleet. Among its cargo was the flower known as Nord'el--Bloom of the Heavens in your tongue--bloomed under a full moon at the peak of Mount Hyjal, our former home.$B$BPlease help me retrieve it! The wreckage is just south of the city, but it is inhabited by fierce murloc raiders!",
[98209]="Would you please deliver Nord'el to elder Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine?$B$BThe boat from here should be able to get you there swiftly.$B$BI apologize for the request, I truly do. I remain fatigued from my journey here--and from fleeing those murloc devils when I first attempted to retrieve the sacred bloom!",
[98215]="After going through a gauntlet of very cranky whelps, I think it's time we fix this little reoccurring problem we keep running into.$B$BBeing flammable.$B$BI've been watching these dragons for awhile and it seems like they are immune to their own fire! Well, at least their scales are.$B$BIf you're willing to do some extra work, I'd be happy to compensate you for any shed scales you come across out there. With any luck we'll have enough to make us some gear to cover ourselves. Oh, and Melly too of course.",
[98216]="Old Gods?! This cannot be good news at all!$B$BI've made out a new bit on the stone that speaks of a guardian of some kind. Whatever it is, it must be linked to the stone!$B$BTake it with you and see if you can find a big Titan construct of some sort in the excavation. Read this here final passage on the stone and see what happens!$B$BIf I'm right, you'll activate the thing. Take it out if so, but try to preserve anything interesting! We simply must know more!",
[98221]="In the Second War the Dragonmaw built a fleet where we now stand, intending to take Hillsbrad. They nearly succeeded!$B$BThey were routed by the red dragons, left to mere stragglers deep in the mountains. However, there has been a surge in activity in their encampment northeast of Menethil.$B$BDun Algaz is proof that they intend to march to war once again and retake this land. Find their attack plans, take note of any critical information, and destroy them. We need to know where they will strike next!",
[98223]="This book has been badly burned--perhaps by the dragonfire that destroyed much of the Dragonmaw clan.$B$BOf what little is legible, it seems to describe rituals relating to the use of the Demon Soul that the clan had used to control the dragons.$B$BIt is far too incomplete to be of real use, but based on roughly inserted pages on animal hide it seems Nek'rosh had attempted to salvage it. Freshly dried ink mentions a \"Shadow Council.\"$B$BCaptain Stoutfist in Menethil Harbor would want to know about this.",
[98230]="After the War of the Three Hammers that tore dwarven life as we knew it apart, the Wildhammers settled here, founding the mountain fortress of Grim Batol.$B$BIt was a wondrous place. Gryphons soared everywhere you looked, diving down through the wetlands to grab a fish.$B$BIt didn't last long, sadly.$B$BHowin Kindfeather is one of the first Wildhammers to return in ages. Keeps to himself, far outside of town. Follow the road east--you'll find him eventually. He could surely use a hand.",
[98231]="Miss Melly got burned pretty bad by those whelps. I think they scared her. I haven't been able to convince her to move!$B$BListen, I have an idea.$B$BI once bought this snake oil potion that obviously didn't work as intended but it DID heal a cut I had. One of the active ingredients was supposedly an herb called Wyrmtail that's found around these parts.$B$BIf my hunch is correct that might help Miss Melly's burns. Go see if you can find some and bring it back! Anything is worth a try.",
[98233]="I was having a drink with my buddies over at the tavern a few nights back and they dared me to try and take on one of those nasty oozes alone.$B$BSeeing as I don't have a sword, you can probably guess how well that went.$B$BWhen I went to attack it my sword got stuck and things didn't go as planned.$B$BI need to get it back before my sergeant realizes I lost it! It should be stuck in an ooze out there somewhere, west of here across the bay.$B$BPlease, if you're headed out that way, can you look for it?",
[98240]="Word is officially out on those whelps, $n. We already have an order in!$B$BI'll package 'em up all nice for you, then you take it out to the customer. I know, I know; it's just one last favor, I promise!$B$BThese will be for one \"Howin Kindfeather\". Sent his gryphon into town of all things with a letter for the order! Says he's just off the road to the east, a bit past Whelgar's Excavation Site, if you're familiar.",
[98245]="I don't know who I hate more: the bloody Dark Irons, the Dragonmaw, or the drakes they rode.$B$B<Howin spits.>$B$BI aim tae make things right. But we're gonna need some supplies.$B$BThese whelp scales will protect against dragonfire a good bit, but they're a pain in the arse tae weave together.$B$BThe Razormaw raptors up in Raptor Ridge to the northeast and Saltspray Glen to the northwest are so named for their pointy chompers--they oughta break through the scales.$B$BBring me a handful of the incisors.",
[98246]="I'll need some eggs if my plan is going tae work. Bassbeak needs a nice an' full belly--I ain't in the business of hoppin' on the back of a surly gryphon.$B$BThey need to be perfect--no cracks or anything.$B$BTake some from the Razormaw raptors--they're known for having yolks the size of a gnome's noggin. You can find 'em in Raptor Ridge to the northeast and Saltspray Glen to the northwest.$B$BLet's make it a nice even dozen, just to be safe.",
[98247]="<A torn shipping label can be found on the side of the now fully stocked crate. Though the intended recipient is torn off, details of its origin still remain.$B$B\"Property of the Azeroth Commerce Authority. Please return empty crates or unfulfilled shipments to our local trade hub at the Three Corners crossroads in Redridge Mountains. Couriers will be compensated for their time and travel.\"$B$BBeside the text is a crudely drawn map of the area near the aforementioned destination.>",
[98248]="<A torn shipping label can be found on the side of the now fully stocked crate. Though the intended recipient is torn off, details of its origin still remain.$B$B\"Return damaged shipments or empty crates to the Durotar Supply and Logistics trade outpost, now conveniently located due west of the Crossroads in the Barrens. Your time is valuable and we will compensate you for your efforts!\"$B$BBeside the text is a crudely drawn map of the area near the aforementioned destination.>",
[98251]="Gaaah!$B$BI'm so angry. They said Ashenvale was easy to follow. Easy for who? The beasts? The birds?$B$BOne moment I was gathering an herb, the next I'm trapped in this ravine. Do I truly have to circle half the forest to reach where I stood just moments ago?$B$BWhen I'm like this, my spells grow volatile and behave... differently.$B$BCould you thin the wildlife nearby? Even their stupid hooves grate on me. I despise this cursed forest.",
[98252]="Show my Eye of Kilrogg the way out of this ravine and back to the Ashenvale road. Keep it moving and I'll follow once I see a clear path.$B$BI'll stay here--one of us should keep our bearings. If you lose the way, I can guide you back through the eye. I will not have us both wandering blind in this malicious forest.$B$BI can hold the channel for four minutes. No longer. Reach the road before the vision breaks, or return to me and we try again.",
[98282]="Certain alchemical recipes require ingredients sourced from, well, very dangerous places. And those are often just the base herbs! The other ingredients are even worse!$B$BI need to make more antivenom before I can leave again. I swear everything in this marsh is venomous. It's like it runs through the land itself!$B$BCan you help me? I'll need a venom gland from the spiders in Thelgen Rock to the far southeast. But it has to be unruptured, or too much venom will spill out before you can get here. Sorry!",
[98283]="The natural order of this land is breaking. Once it was that the Razormaw raptors kept the land from overgrowth. They now live in fear of their alpha, named only for the carnage it leaves behind.$B$BI fear the beast has been driven mad by the sickness that we have yet to fully excise.$B$BIt will respond to the malignant flesh of the diseased bears below Raptor Ridge, to the northeast. Leave their entrails in its cave lair.$B$BCarnage will come. Bring me its head.",
[98284]="Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.",
[98285]="An engineer is ever-resourceful, and if you are in the wilds alone, it's always good to be able to put your trade to use. No good camp is complete without a few helpful constructs!$B$BYes, come back and see me when you've gained a little bit of experience as an engineer and I can show you how to make something special!",
[98286]="Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.",
[98287]="Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.$B$BI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.",
[98291]="I plan tae get back into Grim Batol and reclaim it for the Wildhammers, $n. Or at least learn a thing or two.$B$BDon't look at me like that, now. I know the risks. I don't intend tae go in hammer swingin', ye know.$B$BRegardless, I'll need your help first. The Dragonmaw orcs march as we speak. They're all up an' down the Dragonmaw Retreat, where the red dragons routed them before.$B$BI need you tae thin their numbers before I have any chance of gettin' close. Ye can't miss 'em if you follow the road east.",
[98293]="The Dragonmaw are stockpiling all manner of weaponry. It would be wise to relieve them of these before more soldiers can be armed.$B$BCaptain Stoutfist in Menethil Keep would surely be interested in these.",
[98297]="I did a quick test flight while ye were out. The good news is the armor ye helped me craft for Bassbeak works like a charm!$B$BThe very bad news is I saw a group o' them Dragonmaw in the process of enslavin' a red dragonspawn.$B$BAbsolutely not. Not again.$B$BYou have tae take it out. You'll certainly need friends tae do so. Kill the warlocks holding it down first--that ought tae free it. Then put it out of its misery.$B$BNone of them will stand in the way of the Wildhammer.",
[98298]="Ah, it's all become so embarrassingly clear! Arugal hardly had any magic at all, let alone enough to create the worgen. 'Arugal's Curse.' Pah! Barely potent enough to last a few seconds.$B$BThese shackles prove he can bind the beasts, not create them. The worgen clearly spread their curse a different way. I would know how.$B$BGo to the Greymane Wall to the south. The worgen seem to be spreading to the humans nearby. Tear the beasts apart and bring me whatever you find. This requires a more direct approach.",
[98299]="If there is one thing we do know, it is that Arugal is responsible for worgen within Silverpine--be it his own machinations or otherwise. What we don't know is how it spreads.$B$BWhile I research a way to stop the curse, our first priority is to contain it. It appears this affliction cannot infect forsaken, but a large group of humans have gathered by the Greymane Wall.$B$BGo to the wall and put down these refugees before they have a chance to become servants for Arugal. And try not to get bit, $r.",
[98300]="My work here is far from over, $n. And I need tae send word to me wife Claira in Aerie Peak--and get Falstad an update as well.$B$BBut that's my business. Wildhammer business.$B$BThat said, you ought tae let King Magni Bronzebeard in Ironforge know about all this as well. Wetlands is but a stone's throw from his lands, and none of what's happenin' here is good news on one's doorstep. This letter oughta do the trick.$B$BYe can travel back through Dun Algaz or fly from Menethil Harbor to get to Ironforge.",
[98310]="There are other, larger golems all around the Wetlands. They each bear inscriptions marking them as Ados, Modr, Golm, and Neru--matching the missing pieces of the Goaz Stone you found!$B$BI'd be willing to bet if we can bring pieces of them as well, we'll reveal more of the Goaz Stone!$B$BYou'll find Ados at the Dragonmaw Gates to the east, near Grim Batol. Modr is right outside Dun Modr to the north. Golm lies beneath Grim Batol, east of Dun Algaz. Neru's behind Direforge Hill, to the northeast.",
[98313]="Whatever this is all about, $n, it's epic stuff alright.$B$BI'll bundle everything up nice for you. Take it to Historian Karnik in the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge. You'll usually find him in the back, nose-deep in some tome or another in the library.$B$BIt'll take a downright army to crack the case on this one, but if what we've seen so far is any indication it will well be worth it!",
[98319]="It's bad enough havin' a troll problem, but the mountains are filled tae the brim with wendigos! They normally keep to their own caves, but they seem tae be spreadin' like bunnies. Now they've filled the Grizzled Den north of here.$B$BIf we want Whitebeard's report, we're gonna need to find my partner Cornelius. The blockhead got a little too excited and charged in head first. Brave, but stupid.$B$BHead into the cave and see where he is. And feel free to take out some of the beasts while yer at it.",
[98321]="Hoha! Good to see a $r who's not afraid to get their hands dirty.$B$BIf yer lookin' fer work, I'm afraid I'm a little short on supplies at the moment. Our most reliable source of ore has been overrun by wendigo and now the cave has been abandoned. The miners had to drop everything when they fled!$B$BSay, why don't ye poke yer head around the Grizzled Den to the west and see if you can find some of our missing shipments. It would save us a great deal o' trouble.",
[98322]="Spelunking dark caves is adventurer business. My job's just to make reports and send them over to Ironforge.$B$BTrouble is, one of my reports hasn't... well, reported back. I asked a few mountaineers to learn more about the wendigo problem we have out here, but I haven't heard from them.$B$BIf you're already going to be out and about, what say you check in with Mountaineer Gretchen just west of town. I'm late enough as it is!",
[98323]="Hopefully ye put down a fair number of the mongrels while you were in there. Shame about Cornelius, though.$B$BFrom what you described, there's not much to report other than the cave is a lost cause. Whitebeard's not gonna like that answer, but I'm not darin' sendin' anybody else into that death trap.$B$BFeel free tae pass along the message, $n. I'm not leavin' this spot till the mountain's secure.",
[98325]="I seek the best the Horde has to offer, $c. And ONLY the best.$B$BThere are certain tasks that require a degree of valor that few possess. And fewer still are willing to lay it on the line when it really counts.$B$BAre you $r enough to do what must be done? Let us speak if so.$B$BIf not, begone. I have no time to waste on cowardice.",
[98340]="It would seem that you are ready for the next step in your journey, young druid. Dendrite Starblaze has sent for you, and wishes for you to seek him out in Moonglade once again.$B$BYou have already learned to call upon the magic to take you to Moonglade, so you should be able to embark immediately if you choose. I would suggest you leave soon, if you wish to continue your druidic training.",
[98341]="A spirit of your homeland has recently appeared here and has asked me to guide you to it. This windborne cat spirit has come to tutor and mentor you so that you may take the feline shape of the spirit on Zephras.$B$BAll druids eventually seek this wisdom, though it seems your homeland has a slightly different shape than our traditional one. If you desire to take this spirit's feline form, you will need to undergo our trial.$B$BIt can be found in the southern part of Moonglade, south of the twin bridges.",
[98342]="To draw upon my spirit, you will need more than a few words. To understand and respect my form you must prove that you can embody cunning, stealth, and if you should be cornered, ferocity.$B$BIn the Barrow Dens just east of here, are three relics of my favor you must acquire. They are guarded by powerful enraged spirits that will attack you on sight. A statue at the entrance will bless you with temporary stealth to get past them.$B$BReturn these relics to me. We will see if you are ready to take my shape.",
[98362]="The time has come for us to part ways once again, young one, as the application of your lessons takes you back to the one who sent you to me. It would seem your instructor, Turak Runetotem, has found a worthy pupil in you. I believe I see one as well. Heed his lessons and you shall soon be able to draw upon the Great Cat Spirit to take its shape.$B$BGo back to whence you came. When the time is right, we will meet again.",
[98386]="Orcs, gnolls, murlocs. Everything seems to be out to stop me from getting this bridge done on time. Now we have word there's an infestation of tarantulas at our lumber mill!$B$BIf you're up to earn a bit more coin, would you head over to Alther's Mill to the east and clear out their spider problem? Place is as good as useless to me if I can't safely send workers to collect shipments.$B$BOh, and if you see ol' Alther, tell him he owes me for cleaning up his mess.",
[98389]="Greetings, $c. Yes, I am a paladin. Not even death can stop the Light.$B$BThis is something my kind have in common with all Forsaken--we have overcome what the living view as their end. However, some even among our own fear us; they suspect we will smite them as some monstrosity.$B$BIn truth, our relationship with undeath is complex, but I am not here to hurt our own. Help me show the others this. Venture to Night's Web Hollow to the northwest and free the freshly raised fools trapped by the spiders there.",
[98392]="These belts... look closely at the leather, $n. Do you see the taint running through the fibers?$B$BI have a suspicion as to its origin, but we will need further proof to be sure.$B$BVenture back out into the harpies' nests to the west and take out their leaders. If their necklaces carry the same darkness as these belts, we'll have our answer.",
[98393]="It would seem that you are ready for the next step in your journey, young druid. Dendrite Starblaze has sent for you, and wishes for you to seek him out in Moonglade once again.$B$BYou have already learned to call upon the magic to take you to Moonglade, so you should be able to embark immediately if you choose. I would suggest you leave soon, if you wish to continue your druidic training.",
[98394]="In the southern part of Moonglade, on a hill overlooking the bridge, resides a wise and cunning being we call the Great Cat Spirit.$B$BMuch like the Great Bear Spirit, this spirit has served as a tutor and mentor to druids that desire to take the feline shape. All druids eventually seek its wisdom, and if you desire to take the form of a cat, you will as well.$B$BGo meet with the Great Cat Spirit and learn what it will teach you.",
[98396]="To draw upon my spirit, you will need more than a few words. To understand and respect my form you must prove that you can embody cunning, stealth, and if you should be cornered, ferocity.$B$BIn the Barrow Dens just east of here, are three relics of my favor you must acquire. They are guarded by powerful enraged spirits that will attack you on sight. A statue at the entrance will bless you with temporary stealth to get past them.$B$BReturn these relics to me. We will see if you are ready to take my shape.",
[98397]="The time has come for us to part ways once again, young one, as the application of your lessons takes you back to the one who sent you to me. It would seem your instructor, Mathrengyl Bearwalker, has found a worthy pupil in you. I believe I see one as well. Heed his lessons and you shall soon be able to draw upon the Great Cat Spirit to take its shape.$B$BGo back to whence you came. When the time is right, we will meet again.",
[98398]="I am impressed by what you have accomplished here in so short a time, $n. Would that I could ask you to remain here to assist me with my duties... but I know in my heart that greater tasks lie ahead for you.$B$BI have noticed the Oracle Tree has just shed a piece of its bark. No doubt it has a task that it wishes completed. You should speak with it.",
[98404]="In order to draw upon my spirit, you will need to undergo a trial. To understand and respect my form you must prove that you can embody cunning, stealth, and if you should be cornered, ferocity.$B$BIn the Barrow Dens just east of here, are three relics you must acquire. They are guarded by powerful enraged spirits that will attack you on sight. A statue at the entrance will bless you with temporary stealth to get past them.$B$BReturn these relics to me to pass the druidic trial of these lands.",
[98405]="In the southern part of Moonglade, on a hill overlooking the bridge, resides a wise and cunning being we call the Great Cat Spirit.$B$BMuch like the Great Bear Spirit, this spirit has served as a tutor and mentor to druids that desire to take the feline shape. All druids eventually seek its wisdom, and if you desire to take the form of a cat, you will as well.$B$BGo meet with the Great Cat Spirit and learn what it will teach you.",
[98417]="At the moment our fates bound us most vulnerable, tragedy fell upon our villages. Satyrs defiled our temples, their profane touch staining sacred boughs, and they slaughtered the innocent without mercy.$B$BKurothel was consumed by wrath. The druids are taking the fight to the satyr, and he has followed.$B$BOur bond endures. I feel my husband, west, within these woods. Please, return to me with news of his fate.",
[98418]="Kurothel mentioned sightings of what they say are wolf-men. Those of the pack now lurking in greater numbers in our forest. Last we had spoken, druids were pursuing communication with those of the beast heart who displayed measured control of their animal instincts.$B$BHis written words show a darker struggle. If there is anything we can do to help see HIM again, surely quelling the demon threat that is driving him to this burning transformation will be of aid to his anguished soul.$B$BSlay the Xavian, $n.",
[98424]="Some particularly worn papers are held separately, folded in Fizsprocket's inside breast pocket.$B$BThey seem to detail important information that could be used against the Venture Co. and its operations in the region. It would be prudent to look for more before returning to Morin Cloudstalker.",
[98427]="The shredder one of the pages speaks of--I have seen them before in my travels. They can decimate a forest in a fraction of the time that hand and axe can.$B$BEntire glades--homes to the Earth Mother's children for millennia--erased in days.$B$BWe will not allow this to happen in our home, a stone's throw from where our young ones take their first steps.$B$B$n, I must ask you to gather others, go back into the mine to the northeast, and ensure it fells not a single tree more.",
[98430]="Hail, $c. What brings you deep into such a dark and violent place?$B$BI was sent here by High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof as a part of our efforts to communicate with the gnolls that have taken residence. The rest of my mission must remain a secret, as do all things with the Longwalkers, the trusted scouts of our chieftain.$B$BAll you must know is our diplomacy was met with violence, and I fear I may be tonight's feast for the gnolls if you do not help me escape.$B$BAre you up to the task?",
[98435]="Our elders in Thunder Bluff must know of the progress we have made here, thanks to your aid.$B$BPlease, take this to Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem in Thunder Bluff. You will find him in the Elder Rise, on the east side of the city. You must take the lifts up to the center of the city, then cross the bridges to reach it.",
[98447]="Despite you putting down the Valor family ghosts, the reports of attacks have not ceased. It was a good gamble, but perhaps we did not settle their unfinished business after all.$B$BFrom my research, it sounds like this family all went missing at the same time. Whatever trauma caused their spirits to be chained to this realm must have happened all at once.$B$BOur only clue is where you found the book. Return to Raven Hill and see what you can find. Maybe bringing their weapons will spark something.",
[98459]="Bart Tidewater's a no-good cheapskate, I tell ya!$B$B\"Captain of the Maiden's Virtue\" he calls himself. That ship's sailed as far as a rock in Tanaris! He's no captain, he's an actor who won enough hands of poker to buy the Virtue in the first place!$B$BIf you ever find yourself in Menethil Harbor over in the Wetlands, give this to him and let him know it's from ol' Half-fish.$B$BThere's a boat from here that can take you right to the harbor, by the way. It'll be the second stop!$B$BAnd he cheats at poker!",
[98461]="If you're heading out of Auberdine, I could use your help!$B$BMy dear friend Tarrel and I were classmates in school. Oh, he was such a quickfire on all things excavation! We got split up after graduation--him to Wetlands, and me to here in Darkshore.$B$B<Hollee sighs, then her brow furrows slightly.>$B$BSorry, and his wife... Merrin.$B$BIt doesn't matter. If you go to the Wetlands, could you make sure he's alright? And maybe give him this? He's probably near Menethil Harbor. There's a boat straight there.",
[98463]="Look, I'm glad to have you at my bar, and that's exactly why I'm telling you this.$B$BThe real party? That's over at the Salty Sailor Tavern in Booty Bay. Yes, in Stranglethorn Vale--that Booty Bay.$B$BDon't give me that look. I know it's run by goblins. Bartenders talk, and bar patrons talk a LOT. All I'm saying is that if you want to see things get real wild, head over there.$B$BNixxrax Fillamug will keep you topped up, don't even worry.",
[98477]="Any experienced shaman who attempts to scry the elemental plane can tell you that there is a blip of sorts, a distortion that you feel as you cross over to the other realms of existence.$B$BWe have need of adventurers like yourself to help us better understand this disturbance. Take this Elemental Attractor. You will be able to extract motes of unstable magic with it from the most skilled spellcasters and other powerful entities you may encounter. Bring me these motes so that we may study them.",
[98512]="You there, stranger. Get low and keep quiet. We are not alone here.$B$BI was on patrol near the border and noticed that there are a number of Al'Aketh skulking around the house just up the hill there to the north. I don't know what they are doing here, but it can't be good.$B$BIf you want to make yourself useful, get in there and take them out. I'll wait here and watch your back.",
[98517]="Greetings, young Skyborne. The spirits have spoken of you, and tell me that you are ready to heed the call of fire. However, I shall not be the one to start you on that Path. Return to your home in the elemental plane, seek your mentors there. They will tell you what must be done.",
[98545]="Since you are here, I'd like you to deliver this letter to an old friend of mine in the Undercity. I'd deliver myself but I have a somewhat colorful history with the Dark Lady, and it would be better if a neutral third party made the delivery.$B$BYou are looking for a goblin named Glix Xizzix in the Trade Quarter area of the Undercity. I'm sure he'd be happy to compensate you for your time.$B$B<Leonid lets out a low chuckle as he hands you the letter.>",
[98574]="While you were helping me out, this memorandum was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. I'm thinkin' it came from the priest trainer Branstock. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance.",
[98575]="Ah, while you were gone a tablet came for you, $n.$B$BI usually avoid dealing with warlocks if I can help it, but I think you should read it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from your newly-appointed trainer, Nartok. He would have words with you when you're ready.",
[98576]="Ah, while you were gone a parchment came for you, $n.$B$BRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the mage trainer Mai'ah. She would have words with you when you're ready.",
[98581]="While you were helping me out, this rune was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. Based on the Wildhammer style to these inscriptions, I'm guessin' this came from the shaman trainer Teo Hammerstorm. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance.",
[98601]="While you were off dealing with the mindless Scourge, this scroll arrived for you. It reeks of the light, so I imagine it's of some importance to a paladin like yourself.$B$BRead it before heading out again. Just please--step away when you do. Paladins make me quite uneasy.",
[98731]="Now that you have received my blessing, return to Dendrite. He will instruct you further. I do hope we meet again someday.$B$BMay the shadows forever hide you and your foes easily fall prey to your claws, young one.",
[98738]="Now that you have received my blessing, return to Dendrite. He will instruct you further.$B$BUnfortunately I have little left to teach you for the moment. I do hope you come and visit me in Zephras again someday. I sense promise in you, young shen'dorei.$B$BMay the shadows forever hide you, your foes easily fall prey to your claws, and the winds guide your steps.",
[98739]="Now that you have received my blessing, return to Dendrite. He will instruct you further. I do hope we meet again someday.$B$BMay the shadows forever hide you and your foes easily fall prey to your claws, young one.",
[98830]="The air smells sharp and metallic as you reach down to inspect the corpse of Prince Tortheldrin. Extremely powerful magic was just dispelled here.$B$BYou notice that the corpse before you looks old and weathered, lacking the vitality that the prince exuded before he fell. There are other physical differences as well.$B$BOne of Tortheldrin's glaives lies near his body, broken in two. The Shen'dralar Ancients will want to know of what you observed here.",
[98887]="The Theramore Expeditionary Force are tenacious and continue to send reinforcements to bolster their position on the Darkspear Islands.$B$BGo, show them the might of the Horde! Bring me the evidence of your victory in this key battleground and you will be well rewarded.",
[98889]="The Theramore Expeditionary Force are tenacious and continue to send reinforcements to bolster their position on the Darkspear Islands.$B$BGo, show them the might of the Horde! Bring me the evidence of your victory in this key battleground and you will be well rewarded.",
[98891]="The Theramore Expeditionary Force are tenacious and continue to send reinforcements to bolster their position on the Darkspear Islands.$B$BGo, show them the might of the horde! Bring me the evidence of your victory in this key battleground and you will be well rewarded.",
[98893]="The Theramore Expeditionary Force are tenacious and continue to send reinforcements to bolster their position on the Darkspear Islands.$B$BGo, show them the might of the horde! Bring me the evidence of your victory in this key battleground and you will be well rewarded.",
[98895]="The battle against the Darkspear Raiders is heating up. Without urgent aid, the Darkspear Islands will be lost to us.$B$BIt is your duty as a proud member of the Alliance to ensure this does not happen. Bring me proof of your contributions on the front lines and you will be revered as a hero of the Alliance!",
[98897]="The battle against the Darkspear Raiders is heating up. Without urgent aid, the Darkspear Islands will be lost to us.$B$BIt is your duty as a proud member of the Alliance to ensure this does not happen. Bring me proof of your contributions on the front lines and you will be revered as a hero of the Alliance!",
[98899]="The battle against the Darkspear Raiders is heating up. Without urgent aid, the Darkspear Islands will be lost to us.$B$BIt is your duty as a proud member of the Alliance to ensure this does not happen. Bring me proof of your contributions on the front lines and you will be revered as a hero of the Alliance!",
[98901]="The battle against the Darkspear Raiders is heating up. Without urgent aid, the Darkspear Islands will be lost to us.$B$BIt is your duty as a proud member of the Alliance to ensure this does not happen. Bring me proof of your contributions on the front lines and you will be revered as a hero of the Alliance!",
[98903]="Go forth and represent the Theramore Expeditionary Force in battle at Darkspear Islands, $n! Achieve victory and show these Horde dogs the might of the Alliance!",
[98904]="Go forth and represent the Theramore Expeditionary Force in battle at Darkspear Islands, $n! Achieve victory and show these Horde dogs the might of the Alliance!",
[98905]="Go forth and represent the Theramore Expeditionary Force in battle at Darkspear Islands, $n! Achieve victory and show these Horde dogs the might of the Alliance!",
[98906]="The battle at the Darkspear Islands be locked in a stalemate, $c. Show those Alliance fools who the superior force is.$B$BCarry your head high in service of the Darkspear and claim victory in battle. The Loa will surely be givin' you their blessing, $c!",
[98907]="The battle at the Darkspear Islands be locked in a stalemate, $c. Show those Alliance fools who the superior force is. Carry your head high in service of the Darkspear and claim victory in battle. The Loa will surely be givin' you their blessing, $c!",
[98908]="The battle at the Darkspear Islands be locked in a stalemate, $c. Show those Alliance fools who the superior force is.$B$BCarry your head high in service of the Darkspear and claim victory in battle. The Loa will surely be givin' you their blessing, $c!",
[99047]="My sisters and I... were dispatched... Oracle Tree...$B$BTree... message. I... harpies... everywhere...$B$B<Eralya coughs up blood, grimacing through the pain.>$B$BI may not have long... no one coming. Please... Byancie... in Dolanaar...",
[99048]="A member of the Shattered Hand, a group of more... subtle fighters, was watching Tiragarde Keep from a distance. Her reports suddenly stopped coming in.$B$BI doubt the humans would have caught her, so I'm concerned something more dangerous is at play. See if you can find her. Hopefully the messages are just delayed.",
[99049]="The nearby area is destroyed with obvious signs of a skirmish. Whatever ambushed Heglan didn't make it out unscathed. There's probably signs nearby of what happened.$B$BOrgnil will probably want to see any evidence left by the attackers.",
[99050]="I will need your help acquiring the ingredients I need to stop the affliction long enough for Eralya to make it back here for further treatment.$B$BThankfully, our living home is still bountiful and will provide in our time of need.$B$BThe core ingredient is dewy lasher fronds. You'll find them around Lake Al'Ameth directly south of here, or Wellspring Lake and its river to the northwest.$B$BIn addition, I'll need an empty vial and some spring water. Both can be bought here in town, or traded for.",
[99051]="It wouldn't be the first time those snakes bothered us. They need to be taught that their presence is not tolerated here.$B$BFind where their scouts are setting up camp and slaughter them. Bring me back their fins as proof. We need to act fast to make sure they understand.",
[99052]="One of my scouts has reported a sea giant followed those naga down here. Not sure if they brought him intentionally or what, but he's dangerous in any case.$B$BIt's a young one, but it could still rip an orc in half in a heartbeat if they were caught off guard. I need him gone. But I'd suggest you find some help to deal with it.",
[99073]="The salve is ready. Take it to Eralya swiftly.$B$BI do not know if it will truly cure her. The rot festers quickly, and grows in strength as it spreads.$B$BIt will, if nothing else, ease her suffering. And that is still worth your haste.",
[99079]="The Longwalkers are our people's most trusted scouts. Though their loyalty lies with the High Chieftain alone, young Baine at times seeks their aid.$B$BThis is one such time. Longwalker Malah was dispatched near our borders to the east and did not return last night after three days. When this occurs, it is our duty to confirm their safety.$B$BI must ensure the village remains safe. Prove yourself, and seek Malah out. You will know her by her headband and feathered staff, emblematic of the Longwalkers.",
[99080]="Hear my words well: we will not yield a single blade of grass to the centaur.$B$BGo to their camp now, before they have rested and have a chance to ride to our village. Slaughter them all. Ensure none escape to the Barrens to rally others to their aid.$B$BIf you find the leader of this would-be raiding party, bring me his head so that it may serve as a warning to others who dare tread on our ancestral homeland.",
[99081]="You can see what appears to be a new centaur camp in the direction the arrows in Malah's back would have come from. There is a stir of activity, suggesting a small raiding party has made its way into Mulgore.$B$BThe Longwalker has a report in her still-clenched hand. Brave Wildrunner will want to know of Malah's fate--and her killers.",
[99082]="Your bravery defending your people demands recognition. Journey to Thunder Bluff to the northwest, our mighty city whose shadow grants us shade in the warmer months, and seek audience with my father.$B$BIt was he who led the charge with the young Warchief Thrall to reclaim these plains and drive the centaur away for good. As High Chieftain, he will reward you generously for your part in ensuring his own bravery is honored.$B$BYou must take a lift to reach the High Chieftain, who sits on the central rise.",
[99101]="Baine Bloodhoof leads our village. He must know of this incursion at once.$B$BBring him Longwalker Malah's report. You will find him at the center of town.$B$BQuickly, now. There is no time to waste!",
[99108]="Hail, young $c. Though you are not a warrior and I cannot teach you that path, that does not mean you would not benefit from my tutelage.$B$BBefore you lies the arena. In it, it matters not who you call mother or whether you wield sword or bow. All are equal, and all learn to sharpen their horns in direct combat.$B$BWill you enter our space, and learn our ways for yourself? You may face any of these novices, or any other willing adversary. I care not which.",
[99123]="I decided to do a bit of scouting in the crag on my own. Unfortunately my magic ran out at the wrong time and I've been stuck hiding here since.$B$BIf you could help me escape, I would appreciate it.",
[99127]="The fish just ain't biting today, and there's something wrong going on with them. It's not just empty hooks. I haven't seen a single minnow up in the water at all.$B$BLee here set up some traps overnight. Go check to see if we've at least got some stock there. If you find anything weird, make sure to show me.",
[99128]="This can only be the work of those murlocs on the other side of the lake. They're disgusting little things, with a vicious temper and teeth to match.$B$BIf we let this continue, there won't be any fish to speak of anywhere in this lake. If you could clear them out a bit, it would help me a ton.",
[99129]="Remy mentioned murlocs the other day... I'm pretty sure he hates the little buggers as much as I do.$B$BHe might have some ideas on how to keep them away from my fish in the future. I'd like to ask you to go chat with him and see if there's anything he can think of.",
[99130]="I've got a few ideas on how to deal with murlocs. And one of those also helps some others in the process.$B$BThere's a weed often found on farms in the area called duskweed, and in large quantities the petals are toxic to most animals. If we make some murloc bait with the plant, hopefully that can train those creatures to stay away.$B$BAnd some farmers get their fields cleared in the process. Truly a win-win... truly a win-win.",
[99131]="Tell Mathers he can come pick up the bait later today. I'll give him the rundown on the proper usage.$B$BHopefully he'll be able to sell his fish again soon. And we'll have less murlocs in this world.",
[99134]="You are not a member of the Deathguard, and therefore have yet to disappoint me.$B$BAs a reward for your relative lack of incompetence, you shall punish those that have demonstrated such talents in excess.$B$BSwiftly now--$n, is it?--or I shall add your name to my ledger for someone else's reward.",
[99141]="Make no mistake, $c--the Dark Lady demands the perfect execution of her will. As an Executor, it is my duty to see that this happens.$B$BReports from several of my Deathguards are overdue. Needless to say, my patience has run out. Obtain their reports and bring them to me in the Dark Lady's name.$B$BYou will find Deathguard Dillinger just west of here, by the graveyard. Deathguard Kristof is stationed at the waystation to the east. And check on the abomination Gordo; he wanders west near Stillwater Pond.",
[99142]="If you're heading east, towards the Balnir Farmstead, I have more you might do for me. Good help is ever so hard to find these days, as your run-in with Gordo illuminates ever so clearly.$B$BAs I acquire doom weed I perform some minor alchemical alterations and replant them on that farmstead to cultivate my ultimate creation. I call it tomb weed, and it shall be the herald of my glorious destiny.$B$BDo keep an eye on the Scourge in the area while you're there. They seem... drawn... to the weed. Curious.",
[99143]="Those fish men must think like actual fish, right? Which means anything they like, fish will like!$B$BIf you rummage through some of their junk and return to me with anything that seems like it would make good bait, I'll reward you.",
[99144]="Light bless you for finding me. I was on my way from Bandarion Keep to deliver a message to Shari Stilwell in Brill when these monsters captured me. They wield the Light with a hatred in their hearts that makes what's left of my blood seethe. It goes against all I meditate for... all I strive to protect!$B$B<Bareth Dawnstone steadies himself.>$B$BI know some still take issue with my kind, but I assure you our intentions are pure. If you would aid me in escaping this place, I would be forever grateful.",
[99152]="While the Tarnished in Shadowvale to the southwest are definitely a problem, we cannot allow the cellars below the town to fester into a full-blown Scourge uprising on Bandarion Keep.$B$BI need to get these trainees up to snuff in case that happens. You, however, are going to receive what I like to call a crash course.$B$BTravel beneath Shadowvale and retrieve some of their wretched bones so we can study them further. I need ones that still retain some of the initial reanimation magic--that's glowing ones.",
[99153]="Oi, you! Word travels quickly among our ranks. I heard about the work you did with the cultists around the remnants of the battle with Naxxramas.$B$BProblem is, one of them cultists got away with a piece of the focusing crystal. Seems to still have some juice in it. Best guess we have is it's somewhere beneath Shadowvale. It's either raising 'em or making 'em stronger, and you don't want either one.$B$BFind that crystal before this gets out of hand.",
[99156]="Damn it all! A new report came in while you were on patrol. There has been a sighting of a rogue abomination wandering Eastern Tirisfal Glades, near Venomweb Vale.$B$BSomething is wrong. Abominations don't just slip through the Bulwark unnoticed.$B$BKeep this matter on a strictly need-to-know basis. That said, such a creature will not fall easily; you will need allies if you wish to be more than its next meal.$B$BSee this through, and you will be duly rewarded. Bring me its heart as proof of the deed.",
[99159]="My hearth is open to warm any soul, but I'd like to ask you to help me if you could.$B$BI simply need more firewood. It is something I would normally do myself, but I have been preoccupied by other tasks.",
[99160]="You may have noticed the elementals nearby. A shelf of rock and ice fell from the mountain peaks a few days ago and riled them up.$B$BThese frozen mountains are already treacherous for the average dwarf or human without the elements taking form. I am not one for fighting anymore--so any of the spirits you can kill would help make the road safer.",
[99161]="I noticed that the first elemental that appeared after the rockslide was larger than its peers. And from what I can tell, it has been the source of occasional weather changes and other minor slides.$B$BI've been calling it 'Avala', if you could kill it and retrieve the core as proof, I will reward you.",
[99162]="Even mountaineers from Ironforge have to keep their wits about them when traversing through the peaks of Dun Morogh. Falling snow and ice often spells the end of some more novice members' lives.$B$BAfter a slide, I usually try to find any sign of survivors or victims--while praying to the Light that there's nothing to be found. But with the elements acting up, I've held off wandering too far. If you could look for some lost mountaineers and bring me their rifles, I will return them to Ironforge.",
[99187]="You may not be a Knight of Lordaeron--though perhaps you are, in a way. However, a Paladin you remain... and you know the power of an oath.$B$BThe Blackmaw are powerful totemics, and they would recognize the power of such an artifact as the Reliquary. Undoubtedly, they still possess it.$B$BThusly I'd ask this of you now--finish the quest I started. Return the Reliquary of Tyr here to Tirisfal Glades where it belongs. Only then will my oath be discharged, and my spirit may move on from this world.",
[99201]="Ey, welcome back $c!$B$BZjolnir will provide ya with a free armored mount once you have trained journeyman riding with me, and after that ya be able to purchase any additional armored mounts.$B$BSpeak to me when ya have enough gold, and I will teach ya to master raptor riding.",
[99202]="Greeting once more, $c. The time has come for you learn to ride one of our grandest mounts--the armored kodo.$B$BHarb will provide you with a free mount once ye have completed your training with me, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts you would like, just as before.$B$BThis will be expensive, but speak to me when you have enough coin. I will finish your training.",
[99203]="Ah, you've returned. Very good. Are you ready to learn to ride an armored galestrider?$B$BAs before, if you take the next step in your training with me, I will provide you with a free mount, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts you would like.$B$BIt won't be cheap, but speak to me when you have enough coin. I will teach you about riding armored galestriders.",
[99204]="You have returned. Good. It's time to take your next steps.$B$BOgunaro will provide you with a free mount once you have completed your final leg of training with me, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts you would like, as before.$B$BSpeak to me when you have enough gold, and I will finish your training.",
[99205]="You've returned, $n. Very good. It's time to learn to ride a proper mount, your armored sabercat.$B$BLelanai will provide you with a free mount once ye have trained with me, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts ye would like. There are many creatures out in the world, and each requires their own riding skill, but you will have to find trainers for each.$B$BSpeak to me when you have enough coin, and I will teach you all I know about riding sabers.",
[99206]="I'm glad you made your way back to me. I can tell by the scratches on your skin and the dirt on your armor that you've seen much of the world. It's time we got you a proper steed.$B$BKatie will provide you with a free mount once ye have completed the final leg of your training with me, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts you would like just as before.$B$BSpeak to me when you have enough coin, and I will teach you all I know about riding armored horses.",
[99207]="I can tell that you've come far enough to handle one of our top of the line, most powerful swift mechanostriders.$B$BMilli will provide you with a free mount once you have completed your final round of training with me, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts you would like just as before.$B$BThis won't be cheap, but speak to me when you have enough gold. I will teach you about riding our supercharged mechanostriders!",
[99208]="You are back. Good. It's time for you to learn to master the steed of a true Forsaken--the skeletal warhorse.$B$BZachariah will provide you with a free mount once you have completed the final round of your training with me, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts you desire.$B$BSpeak to me when you have enough coin, and I will teach you about skeletal warhorses.",
[99209]="Yer back! Good, good.$B$BAre ye ready for a proper mountaineer's mount, $n?$B$BVeron will set ye up with a free armored ram once ye have finished the final leg of yer training with me, and afterwards you'll be able to purchase any additional mounts ye would like.$B$BSpeak ta me when you have enough coin, and I'll teach ye all I know about riding armored rams.",
[99210]="If you're looking for a mount, you have come to the right place, though they may pale in comparison to the chargers you are accustomed to.$B$BRegardless, I encourage you to peruse our fine rams, should you want one. These",
[99211]="Greetings, $n. I didn't expect to see you back to my humble stables again so soon.$B$BYou certainly have had quite a journey. I think I can guess what has brought you here today.$B$BYou now have enough power, experience and skill to ride our deftest and most fearsome warhorses. These armored fiends will bear you through any trial, even past the gates of death itself.$B$BGo examine the armored undead warhorses and return to me when you have made your choice.",
[99212]="Salutations! I see today is a big day indeed; today you will synchronize your biometrics to the rider detection protocol of our fastest and fiercest mechanostriders! This protocol will help the strider distinguish you from other possible riders.$B$BIt clearly seems like you have enough strider experience to handle one of our very best.$B$BGo examine the upgraded mechanostriders and return to me when you have made your choice.",
[99213]="Greetings, $n! I am so glad to see you've returned to us.$B$BIt would seem you have enough experience to ride our fastest and fiercest steeds. You won't find a more steadfast companion for your journeys.$B$BChoosing one may be difficult as they are all excellent and trained to be steady even when in danger. Some may even recognize you from the last time you were here.$B$BGo and examine the armored horses and return to me when you have made your choice.",
[99214]="Greetings, friend! I am pleased to see you again. Today you have enough experience and aptitude to bond with our fastest and fiercest sabers.$B$BThese sabers are, of course, extremely intelligent and fiercely loyal to their bonded rider. You won't find a more noble and steadfast companion.$B$BAs such, you have an important choice to make. You and your saber will traverse the world together, so choose wisely!$B$BGo, examine the armored sabers and return to me when you have made your choice.",
[99215]="Lok-tar, $n. It is good to see you again.$B$BAs you know, there is no stronger bond than that of an orc and their wolf, and now you have enough experience to handle and ride our fiercest and fastest wolves.$B$BMany of these fine wolves remember you from the last time you were here and have grown since you first met. They are stronger, faster and braver than before, much like yourself.$B$BGo and find which armored wolf speaks to you. Return to me when you have your answer.",
[99216]="Gales greetings, $n! I can't believe this day has come so soon. Today I am proud to say you have mastered galestrider riding, so I may now offer you our finest, fastest and boldest striders.$B$BLike before, you and your strider will traverse the world together, so you have an important choice to make. Many of these striders have grown in your time apart, but I would be willing to bet they still recognize you.$B$BGo examine the armored striders and return to me when you have made your choice.",
[99217]="Ah, I've been expecting you $n. It would seem the winds have brought you to me once again, so you may ride our fastest and strongest kodos.$B$BToday, I am proud to present to you your next kodo. Much like yourself, each has grown stronger and faster since you last met.$B$BYou and your kodo will travel the world together just like before, so find which one speaks to you.$B$BGo examine the armored kodos and return to me when you have made your choice.",
[99233]="There must be more to the Maul than this!$B$BPerhaps the loud Spectator who oversees the event at Dire Maul will know!",
[99257]="While I watched in horror as you frolicked through the haunted woods with my precious relic, your meddling did inspire an idea.$B$BThe unstable rifts you encountered are the precursors to our pylon guards. We have been unable to conjure more for centuries, and I worry what might happen when those that remain inevitably flicker out.$B$BI know it seems counterintuitive, but see if you can find another pylon protector nearly on the verge of collapse and recover their Crystal Heart. I'll explain more after.",
[99258]="While sourcing the gems necessary to conjure the elementals is a challenge itself, the bigger concern is whether there is still enough loose mana in Shen'dralas to create them. With this heart, we can confirm once and for all whether we need to begin researching other means of defense.$B$BFor you, the task is simple. Simply toss this gem into one of those unstable rifts. If we're lucky, you'll have a fight on your hands. Don't feel compelled to hold back, if it works once, it will work again.",
[99260]="I was tasked to retrieve important data on the flow of elemental energy from the Overlook Standing Stones. That data is vital to our plans to safely travel between Skywall and Azeroth. Without that data to aid in our calculations, our attempts to steer our skycutter ships through the elemental plane will fail.$B$BThe data is likely lost at this point, and I'm in no state to attempt to gather it again. I told the Supreme Magister of your role in saving me, and he wishes to speak with you again.",
[99326]="Greetings! Are you here to examine our horses?$B$BThese steeds are descendants from both the historical Lordaeron stock and our own local horses. You won't find a more steadfast companion for your journeys.$B$BChoosing one may be difficult as they are all excellent and trained to be steady even when in danger. Don't forget, you and your horse will traverse the world together. I'm sure whatever choice you make will suit you best.$B$BGo examine the horses and return to me when you have made your choice.",
[99411]="Help, $n! My prized puppy, Kyle, has run away! I just know he's running around Bloodhoof Village, lost and hungry.$B$BWill you find him and feed him? Once he eats he will settle down and come home.$B$BTo feed him you will need to find food. His favorite meal is tender strider meat. Just venture east and you should find plenty of striders. Hunt one down and take its succulent meat to Kyle. When you see Kyle in town, put the meat down and he is sure to come to you.",
[99435]="Windsor has already set off to confront Lady Prestor in Stormwind Keep, $c. He spoke highly of your bravery. I suggest you hurry to his aid!$B$BHe is now certain that Prestor is Onyxia: Brood of Deathwing, twin to the tyrant of the Spire, Nefarian.$B$BAccording to him, even the Highlord is controlled by her trickery! The Marshal intends to break the spell and free all of Stormwind from the dark shadow of these fiends.$B$BFind him and ensure the deed is done!",
[99670]="Jereman is fortunate to be alive. It sounds like she fled from the lodge in quite the hurry, no doubt thrilled to be freed from her predicament.$B$BShe will wish to speak with you. Go, find her.",
}
